le=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><b>Corrosive Touch [Namatru]</b></span></span><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Normal:</b> Your body is that of a great toxic menace secreting horrible chemicals<br /> that eat away at what ever they touch like hungry insects leaving chemical burns<br /> though is the least of what you can do though. When active any brawl based<br /> melee attack, or an attack generated by another atavism leaves behind a viscus<br /> corrosive agent that eats into flesh, bone, and steel with equal ease. The corrosive<br /> compound is treated as a poison with a toxicity of Stamina that deals damage every<br /> turn until it has been fully resisted once with two successes. Objects are not so lucky<br /> Every turn they take 1 structure damage that bypasses durability.<br /> <b>Low Satiety</b>: Your deadly toxic touch damages armor, warping even the finest ceramic<br /> plates, and fine steel. Every turn until It expires the armor value of the target's ballistic<br /> armor decreases by 1, until it reaches 0. On the following turn, and every 2 turns after<br /> reduce general armor by one. Against objects it reduces Durability by 1 on the beasts<br /> next turn and every 2 turns after that.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> With the power of the beast behind it no force can stop this toxic<br /> \u200b touch. Increase toxicity by lair, damage becomes aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like Corrosive Touch, but Salamander Claws seems a little superfluous, what with Dragonfire and all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:45:58-08:00","id":817123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=816983#post816983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like Corrosive Touch, but Salamander Claws seems a little superfluous, what with Dragonfire and all</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are damage over time effects, meant to enhance other attacks. Originally I wrote Salamander claw as a Merit that required dragon fire, and gave the dot fire to other atavisms, and it didn't have satiety effects. When I realized it looked a bit awakward, I converted it to one of it's own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:51:27-08:00","id":817126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817123#post817123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Both are damage over time effects, meant to enhance other attacks. Originally I wrote Salamander claw as a Merit that required dragon fire, and gave the dot fire to other atavisms, and it didn't have satiety effects. When I realized it looked a bit awakward, I converted it to one of it's own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that. It's a good Atavism, I'll add it to the Homebrew folder so it's there if people want it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:52:04-08:00","id":817132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MatthiasThalmann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=815573#post815573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sons of Wayland</b><br /> <br /> While many beasts are creatures of destruction some are just as skilled at creating things: An Ugallu may forge deadly weapons cutting down enemies who thought to be protected by an armour, while an Anakim build mighty castles - or in the modern age skyscrapers - to show his power and leave onlooker in awe. Many of these beasts think that Wayland was one of them who became an apex after taking revenge on Nidung.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended<br /> <br /> <b>Normal effect</b>: Relying on the supernatural skills of its horror the beast becomes an excellent craftsman and has maximum (5) dots in the crafts skill. However, the items are not supernatural just extraordinary well crafted. The beast is also capable to recognise forgeries or inferior items at first glance. Once per chapter the beast may create an item that is enhanced with supernatural strength: A knife might impossibly sharp or a pillar might bear load that should according to the laws of physics crush it. Items created this way have their natural proprieties enhanced but do not gain new capabilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Low satiety</b>: The horror lurks just below the surface and all the beast works are imbued with its power. All items the beasts create are better than the law of physics allow them to be. However, strength is not the only thing leaking into the beasts products: the hunger the beast feels infects its creations as well. Jewels created by a collector try to get lost to make their owners feel the loss, weapons created by a hunter thirst for blood and cut and injure everyone careless enough, chandeliers made by a ravager fall onto the table destroying the cutlery and meal... To the beast those side effects are not necessarily bad: If it can witness the effects of his creations it can regain 1 dot of satiety.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: Weaving part of the primordial dream into its creations the beast is capable to create outright supernatural items mimicking the effects of other atavisms (e.g. the coat Wayland used to escape would be equivalent to Wings of the Raptor). If the beast has Family ties with another monster who can create magical items the beast may create counterfeits of those. However, such creations do not last for long in the real world and the supernatural effects evaporate after a number of hours equal to the beast lair.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's see:<br /> <br /> Normal Satiety: Rather than setting a flat bonus, how about Beasts find it easier to make exceptional items? Like, Exceptional Success at Build Equipment actions with three successes instead of five, but only for actual, physical items? Plans, organizations, and repositories are to ephemeral and/or decentralized to be covered by this. Vehicles, however, would be a special case; fitting with the new rules for vehicle modification, this Atavism would increase the number of mods a vehicle can support from (the Beast's Craft x 2) to (Craft x 3), or (Craft x 4) if they have the Automotive Genius Merit.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: I like the idea of items with desires (dare I say, Hungers) of their own. Rather than motion, though, it might be a better fit at this level if the item were to inflict a Condition or Tilt on a target, like in the stories where people become obsessed with enchanted rings, or become berserkers due to magic swords, or magic hammers that can send even the strongest warrior tumbling to the ground. I think this might be best represented by having the Condition/Tilt capable of being applied automatically against a target once per scene, giving player characters a Beat in exchange for the auto-application.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: This is the realm of magic carpets and helms of invisibility. The imbuing of the effect is permanent, and the Beast must either know the effect herself (5 Satiety), share a Lair with a Beast who does (6 Satiety), or have Kinship Ties with a creature with the ability in question (7 Satiety).<br /> <br /> That about does it. Any thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T13:59:41-08:00","id":817141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817132#post817132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, let's see:<br /> <br /> Normal Satiety: Rather than setting a flat bonus, how about Beasts find it easier to make exceptional items? Like, Exceptional Success at Build Equipment actions with three successes instead of five, but only for actual, physical items? Plans, organizations, and repositories are to ephemeral and/or decentralized to be covered by this. Vehicles, however, would be a special case; fitting with the new rules for vehicle modification, this Atavism would increase the number of mods a vehicle can support from (the Beast's Craft x 2) to (Craft x 3), or (Craft x 4) if they have the Automotive Genius Merit.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: I like the idea of items with desires (dare I say, Hungers) of their own. Rather than motion, though, it might be a better fit at this level if the item were to inflict a Condition or Tilt on a target, like in the stories where people become obsessed with enchanted rings, or become berserkers due to magic swords, or magic hammers that can send even the strongest warrior tumbling to the ground. I think this might be best represented by having the Condition/Tilt capable of being applied automatically against a target once per scene, giving player characters a Beat in exchange for the auto-application.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: This is the realm of magic carpets and helms of invisibility. The imbuing of the effect is permanent, and the Beast must either know the effect herself (5 Satiety), share a Lair with a Beast who does (6 Satiety), or have Kinship Ties with a creature with the ability in question (7 Satiety).<br /> <br /> That about does it. Any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, save on the satiety costs and the ability to copy non-Atavism supernatural abilities. While I agree that it should cost more that 1 satiety, I think that the costs you suggested were too high. Perhaps 3 for an Atavism you know and 4 for one from a Lair-sharing Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T14:05:04-08:00","id":817151,"title":"","content":"I think that for the 'applying conditions' thing for Low Satiety it could be quite interesting to come up with Conditions which fit individual items, as opposed to just having one Condition per Hunger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:26:22-08:00","id":817684,"title":"","content":"Does anyone have any ideas for a plant-based Atavism?<br /> I was thinking that perhaps the Normal effect could be the ability to 'root' oneself and, while doing so, the ability to photosynthesise and maybe communicate with other plants (not on the level of actual speech, but the Beast would be able to pick up impression like 'day', 'night', 'there's someone leaning against my roots', 'there was something powerful in the park last night' etc). <br /> I thought that maybe the Satiety Expenditure would allow the Beast to merge into plant life, existing as a kind of spirit inhabiting it, and able to travel through connected plant life.<br /> I've no ideas about Low Satiety though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T09:56:53-08:00","id":817716,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=589702#post589702\">This Atavism</a> I wrote a while back could work for certain species of arboreal Horror.<br /> <br /> As for your Atavism idea, I think it might look something like this:<br /> <br /> Normal Effect: The Beast can ask questions of plant life, receiving simple answers about recent/nearby phenomena.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: The Beast can root himself in place, gaining the Immobilized Tilt but adding his Lair to rolls to resist being moved or knocked over. While rooted, he can use the normal effect of this Atavism on all plant life within 10 x Lair yards, and heals all bashing damage every 15 minutes.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The Beast can command plant life to act on his orders, ensnaring victims, lashing out with thorns, force-feeding poisonous berries, etc. Roll Wits + Science to attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:40:10-08:00","id":817752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817716#post817716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=589702#post589702\">This Atavism</a> I wrote a while back could work for certain species of arboreal Horror.<br /> <br /> As for your Atavism idea, I think it might look something like this:<br /> <br /> Normal Effect: The Beast can ask questions of plant life, receiving simple answers about recent/nearby phenomena.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: The Beast can root himself in place, gaining the Immobilized Tilt but adding his Lair to rolls to resist being moved or knocked over. While rooted, he can use the normal effect of this Atavism on all plant life within 10 x Lair yards, and heals all bashing damage every 15 minutes.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The Beast can command plant life to act on his orders, ensnaring victims, lashing out with thorns, force-feeding poisonous berries, etc. Roll Wits + Science to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that something like that would work. I'll edit it a bit, add some fluff and put it up here so you can have a look. Any ideas for names?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:46:20-08:00","id":817759,"title":"","content":"Green Thumb? Malevolent Forest? Witchwood? Nature's Treachery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T10:48:49-08:00","id":817761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817759#post817759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Green Thumb? Malevolent Forest? Witchwood? Nature's Treachery?</div> </div> </div> </div> I like Witchwood. Which Family do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:17:22-08:00","id":817781,"title":"","content":"My first guess is Eshmaki.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T11:22:14-08:00","id":817785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817781#post817781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first guess is Eshmaki.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking maybe Ugallu, because the trees know. They know your past, they know your parent's pasts, they know <i>their</i> parent's pasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:19:46-08:00","id":817823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817761#post817761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like Witchwood. Which Family do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds very Eshmaki to me, but Ugallu works too.<br /> <br /> By the way, here's my attempt at an identity thief Atavism. Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Masked Fiend [Eshmaki]</b></u><br /> <br /> Be they prowling succubi, skin-walkers wearing human pelts or body-snatching parasites from outer space, humanity has always feared the monsters that could be hiding behind anyone's face. This Atavism allows Beasts to shape-shift in a way that facilitates infiltration and deceit.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> No roll is needed. The Beast takes on the appearance of someone they have seen in person within the last [Lair x 2] days as an instant action. The Beast can change ethnicity and gender, but their general age, body type and birthmarks remain. Clothes can also change, but they assume generic appearances. Scientific analysis will correctly identify genetic residue as belonging to the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast may imitate anyone they have seen personally at any point in the past, right down to birthmarks, missing or deformed body parts and radically different age and build. Clothes and accessories will become nearly identical to specific types, and documentation may be produced. The Beast gains 2 dots in the Alternate Identity Merit. Social rolls to impersonate gain [Lair/2 round up] as bonus dice, but Physical and Mental traits are unaffected. Scientific analysis will not identify genetic residue as belonging to the Beast, but it will not show up as belonging to any specific person.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> As an instant action, the Beast can split herself into a small group of individuals, with different appearances each if needed. The maximum amount of illusory people is equal to Lair x 2. They may move objects and use Social Maneuvering with the Beast\u2019s stats, but cannot break, repair or otherwise change objects. Should an illusion attack, the target feels pain and appears to be wounded, but suffers no damage and the apparent wounds disappear at the end of the scene. The same happens to the illusions, and any \u201ccorpses\u201d disappear if left unobserved for more than a moment. They can go any distance from each other, but fade away at the end of the scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 01-27-2016, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T12:23:15-08:00","id":817829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817823#post817823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sounds very Eshmaki to me, but Ugallu works too.<br /> <br /> By the way, here's my attempt at an identity thief Atavism. Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Masked Fiend [Eshmaki]</b></u><br /> <br /> Be they prowling succubi, skin-walkers wearing human pelts or body-snatching parasites from outer space, humanity has always feared the threats could be hiding behind anyone's face. This Atavism allows Beasts to shape-shift in a way that facilitates infiltration and deceit.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> No roll is needed. The Beast takes on the appearance of someone they have seen in person within the last [Lair x 2] days as an instant action. The Beast can change ethnicity and gender, but their general age, body type and birthmarks remain. Clothes can also change, but they assume generic appearances. Scientific analysis will correctly identify genetic residue as belonging to the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast may imitate anyone they have seen personally at any point in the past, right down to birthmarks, missing or deformed body parts and radically different age and build. Clothes and accessories will become nearly identical to specific types, and documentation may be produced. The Beast gains 2 dots in the Alternate Identity Merit. Social rolls to impersonate gain [Lair/2 round up] as bonus dice, but Physical and Mental traits are unaffected. Scientific analysis will not identify genetic residue as belonging to the Beast, but it will not show up as belonging to any specific person.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> As an instant action, the Beast can split herself into a small group of individuals, with different appearances each if needed. The maximum amount of illusory people is equal to Lair x 2. They may move objects and use Social Maneuvering with the Beast\u2019s stats, but cannot break, repair or otherwise change objects. Should an illusion attack, the target feels pain and appears to be wounded, but suffers no damage and the apparent wounds disappear at the end of the scene. The same happens to the illusions, and any \u201ccorpses\u201d disappear if left unobserved for more than a moment. They can go any distance from each other, but fade away at the end of the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I like this, especially the Satiety Expenditure bit. very original.<br /> <br /> I finished the plant Atavism. Here it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Witchwood</b><br /> <br /> When one thinks of monsters, plants do not immediately come to mind. Plants are sedentary, slow things. They cannot chase you, nor can they tear your flesh with claws and teeth, nor can they set your city aflame. All that plants can do is wait and watch and grow, ever so slowly. But that is enough. It is enough for roots to pull down your houses, brick by brick, inch by painful inch. It is enough to <i>know, </i>to know things about the world that humans cannot even dream of. It is enough to outlive generation upon generation of humankind.<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Stamina + Medicine + Lair (purging poisons)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast is a creature of infinite patience and his heart beats in sync with the pulse of the earth itself. He can hear the secret whispers of the trees and ask them to divulge the secrets of the past.<br /> <br /> The Beast can communicate with any plant life he can touch and can ask it questions about the past. How much a plant remembers will depend on its age and size (an ancient oak will remember further back than a patch of algae), but the older and larger it is, the less likely it will remember small events. Also, plants do not communicate with words so much as impressions and feelings and do not possess many of the senses that humans do. As a rough rule of thumb, plants will probably remember light and dark, rainfall or watering, drought and things touching them but not much else.<br /> <br /> The Beast may also root himself with an Instant action so long as he is standing, lying or sitting on bare earth. This applies the Immobilised Tilt to him but as long as he remains rooted he need not eat or drink (so long as the soil he is rooted on has water and nutrients (e.g. not desert sand)), adds his Lair to dice pools to avoid being moved or knocked over and may roll Stamina + Medicine + Lair to attempt to purge any poisons he is afflicted with and adds Lair to any dice pools to resist the effects of such venoms. De-rooting himself is another Instant action.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As the Beast\u2019s hunger grows, so too does his awareness of and connection with the natural world around him. So long as the Beast can bask in natural sunlight, he heals <u>all</u> Bashing damage every 15 minutes. Additionally, while rooted, the Beast can instinctively sense the position of any kind of plant life in an area equal to (Lair*5 yards) and heals Lethal damage at the rate of 1 point every 6 hours so long as he is constantly exposed to natural sunlight.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With the expenditure of a dot of Satiety, the Beast can channel power into nearby plant life, vastly accelerating its growth. In exchange, the Beast becomes able to shape the growth of any plant that he is bolstering. For each dot of Satiety thus spent, the beast can increase the Size of a plant by his (Lair*5). If the Beast directs the plants to grow into a structure, they deal damage to Structure equal to the Size increased and ignore Durability equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair. The growth takes 30 seconds per point of Size gained.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:25:15-08:00","id":817900,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on Witchwood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:37:58-08:00","id":817906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817900#post817900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any thoughts on Witchwood?</div> </div> </div> </div> I like it. I'd increase the radius of the Low Satiety effect to Lair x 10 yards, but that's not very important. I assume the Durability of the plants that are affected with Satiety Expenditure remains the same. I like how the Satiety Expenditure doesn't really need to be lightning fast. It's scarier like that.<br /> <br /> Now here's an interesting question: what would be a good Beastly twist to an Atavism that heals others? I think it should let you re-open the healed wounds if the target disobeys a command. It could be tied to the Anakim, as it could be very useful for extortion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:47:43-08:00","id":817917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817906#post817906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like it. I'd increase the radius of the Low Satiety effect to Lair x 10 yards, but that's not very important. I assume the Durability of the plants that are affected with Satiety Expenditure remains the same. I like how the Satiety Expenditure doesn't really need to be lightning fast. It's scarier like that.<br /> <br /> Now here's an interesting question: what would be a good Beastly twist to an Atavism that heals others? I think it should let you re-open the healed wounds if the target disobeys a command. It could be tied to the Anakim, as it could be very useful for extortion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice! <br /> <br /> I'm not sure about beastly healing, but one thing I can definitely see is some kind of connection to blood and blood-oaths. Perhaps it allows the Beast to bind another to an oath or service in return for healing or augmentation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:50:17-08:00","id":817922,"title":"","content":"Also, I was just thinking about how big a tree a Lair 10 Beast could create. If you were to start with a moderately large tree, perhaps an oak, you could end up with a Size 70 or 80 monstrosity. That's bigger than the biggest skyscrapers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:51:26-08:00","id":817923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817917#post817917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the advice!<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about beastly healing, but one thing I can definitely see is some kind of connection to blood and blood-oaths. Perhaps it allows the Beast to bind another to an oath or service in return for healing or augmentation?</div> </div> </div> </div> Atavisms can't do straight up mind control, but Nightmares can. As for augmentation, there's already Mother's Kiss, so I'd focus on boosting mundane stats. Besides, the threat of the Beast making your intestines spill on the ground by just looking at you if you don't obey is scary enough.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:53:42-08:00","id":817928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817922#post817922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I was just thinking about how big a tree a Lair 10 Beast could create. If you were to start with a moderately large tree, perhaps an oak, you could end up with a Size 70 or 80 monstrosity. That's bigger than the biggest skyscrapers.</div> </div> </div> </div> CoD Size is a wonderful stat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:57:18-08:00","id":817933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817923#post817923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Atavisms can't do straight up mind control, but Nightmares can. As for augmentation, there's already Mother's Kiss, so I'd focus on boosting mundane stats. Besides, the threat of the Beast making your intestines spill on the ground by just looking at you if you don't obey is scary enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mean mind control, I meant consequences (namely the wounds opening again) if the recipient breaks the deal. Sorry, I should have made that clear. My bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:58:47-08:00","id":817936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817928#post817928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> CoD Size is a wonderful stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed it is. It's always funny when you say that something's Size 10 and all the D&amp;D players say &quot;phew&quot;. Then you tell them how big that is in real terms. &quot;gulp&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:21:12-08:00","id":817997,"title":"","content":"Maybe a healing Atavism could have a Innsmouth sort of twist to it where it works by infusing people with some of your Horror's life force, replacing wounds with strange mutations? Like, at the normal level they'd be purely cosmetic, but at Low levels they'd serve as +0L weapons or provide a basic equipment bonus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:36:15-08:00","id":818005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817997#post817997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a healing Atavism could have a Innsmouth sort of twist to it where it works by infusing people with some of your Horror's life force, replacing wounds with strange mutations? Like, at the normal level they'd be purely cosmetic, but at Low levels they'd serve as +0L weapons or provide a basic equipment bonus?</div> </div> </div> </div> I like that, but I'd make the mutations last a week at most. If you wanna disfigure someone, there's Limb From Limb, Dragonfire and many others. I'd be leery of making this hypothetical Atavism addictive, as well. Your suggestion would probably make it a Namtaru Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T15:42:13-08:00","id":818009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818005#post818005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like that, but I'd make the mutations last a week at most. If you wanna disfigure someone, there's Limb From Limb, Dragonfire and many others. I'd be leery of making this hypothetical Atavism addictive, as well. Your suggestion would probably make it a Namtaru Atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want inspiration for this, look up Leviathan the Tempest, especially the Channel 'Everflowing Fetid Growth'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T16:11:47-08:00","id":818029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=817141#post817141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with this, save on the satiety costs and the ability to copy non-Atavism supernatural abilities. While I agree that it should cost more that 1 satiety, I think that the costs you suggested were too high. Perhaps 3 for an Atavism you know and 4 for one from a Lair-sharing Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aiming for copying other splats' powers, just for creating thematically appropriate ones; a wizard's crystal ball, a veil of a faerie maid, a shroud of an unquiet dead, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> As for the cost, I don't think price is a real issue, since Satiety is such an easily replenished resource. That being the said, the price for a permanently imbued effect should still be fairly costly, to represent the invested effort, if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:46:26-08:00","id":818241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=814199#post814199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea was that the Beast could literally take over another's life, a bit like Fetches from Changeling. Nights might be a bit short. What about months, with an Exceptional Success lasting a year?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it can be [Lair] months for a success, and then <i>[Lair]</i> years on an Exceptional Success. I'd also present an ability to end the effect early via touching the target and spending a Willpower point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:54:14-08:00","id":818244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818241#post818241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps it can be [Lair] months for a success, and then <i>[Lair]</i> years on an Exceptional Success. I'd also present an ability to end the effect early via touching the target and spending a Willpower point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see that working. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:06:02-08:00","id":818247,"title":"","content":"You're welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, trying to work out another Atavism based on what was said in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=816519#post816519\">this post</a>. Expect it soon.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding my Web-Spinner Atavism, does it make sense for it to be Ugallu affinity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:08:40-08:00","id":818248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818247#post818247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, trying to work out another Atavism based on what was said in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=816519#post816519&amp;quot;]this</a> post[/URL]. Expect it soon.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding my Web-Spinner Atavism, does it make sense for it to be Ugallu affinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure. It could be Ugallu, but it could just as easily be Namtaru or Eshmaki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:10:20-08:00","id":818249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818247#post818247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, trying to work out another Atavism based on what was said in <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=816519#post816519&amp;quot;]this</a> post[/URL]. Expect it soon.<br /> <br /> Also, regarding my Web-Spinner Atavism, does it make sense for it to be Ugallu affinity?</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to the new Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T00:26:36-08:00","id":818259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=816519#post816519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to request an Atavism for my horror based on the Ravagore from Hordes. The ability is called Eyeless sight.<br /> What it does in its home setting is remove the benefits of stealth, concielment, hiding in a forrest, or hiding with the aid of a smoke or dust cloud. Let's call that the guide for Low satiaty<br /> <br /> What it represents is being able to perceive the world through other, and sometimes unusual senses. Examples being echo location, heat sense, being able to feel the slight tremors in the ground as a person walks, or sense the supernatural energy inherent in many beings, and likely some mix of these.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy to see what experienced person can come up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this to your satisfaction? I used the Blind Sense Modification for the Unchained, the Shatter the Shroud Devotion from Vampire, and the Impossible Spoor Facet of the Wolf Gift of Hunting for ideas.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Eyeless Sight [Ugallu]</b></u><br /> You can run, but you cannot hide. For Ugallu with this Atavism, this saying is all too true for those they prey upon. It doesn't matter how thick the wall is,how dark the shadow they flee under, or even how much distance they can cover. One way or another, sooner or later, they are always found.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast can sense anything moving within 10 feet of his location per dot of Lair he has. He can feel these vibrations despite any physical barrier between him and the thing that is moving. He can see anyone who is invisible to the eye, but otherwise not hidden or obscured.<br /> <br /> This Atavism also allows him to sense people who are making an effort to hide, even with supernatural means. The player rolls Wits + Investigation vs. Dexterity + Stealth to discover the exact location of someone deliberately trying to hide. If the hidden person is using a supernatural power, he triggers a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> While assailed by the pangs of their Hunger, the Beast's vision becomes increasingly sensitive to the faintest of echoes made by the slightest of movements. He gains the 8-again quality to both the Atavism's detection roll, and the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a dot of Satiety, the Beast's Eyeless Sight is heightened to such a degree that he can detect all but the most elusive of hidden prey. He gains automatic successes equal to half his Lair dots (rounded up) on the detection roll and the Clash of Wills. Furthermore, if he succeeds in the Clash of Wills, he also dispels any supernatural powers used by his prey to stay hidden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:01:29-08:00","id":818340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818259#post818259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is this to your satisfaction? I used the Blind Sense Modification for the Unchained, the Shatter the Shroud Devotion from Vampire, and the Impossible Spoor Facet of the Wolf Gift of Hunting for ideas.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Eyeless Sight [Ugallu]</b></u><br /> You can run, but you cannot hide. For Ugallu with this Atavism, this saying is all too true for those they prey upon. It doesn't matter how thick the wall is,how dark the shadow they flee under, or even how much distance they can cover. One way or another, sooner or later, they are always found.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast can sense anything moving within 10 feet of his location per dot of Lair he has. He can feel these vibrations despite any physical barrier between him and the thing that is moving. He can see anyone who is invisible to the eye, but otherwise not hidden or obscured.<br /> <br /> This Atavism also allows him to sense people who are making an effort to hide, even with supernatural means. The player rolls Wits + Investigation vs. Dexterity + Stealth to discover the exact location of someone deliberately trying to hide. If the hidden person is using a supernatural power, he triggers a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> While assailed by the pangs of their Hunger, the Beast's vision becomes increasingly sensitive to the faintest of echoes made by the slightest of movements. He gains the 8-again quality to both the Atavism's detection roll, and the Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a dot of Satiety, the Beast's Eyeless Sight is heightened to such a degree that he can detect all but the most elusive of hidden prey. He gains automatic successes equal to half his Lair dots (rounded up) on the detection roll and the Clash of Wills. Furthermore, if he succeeds in the Clash of Wills, he also dispels any supernatural powers used by his prey to stay hidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it a lot, but I do have a question about the phrasing of one line.<br /> &quot;He can see anyone who is invisible to the eye but otherwise not hidden or obscured.&quot; does that mean if they are standing still they can not be detected under the normal effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:09:06-08:00","id":818343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818340#post818340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it a lot, but I do have a question about the phrasing of one line.<br /> &quot;He can see anyone who is invisible to the eye but otherwise not hidden or obscured.&quot; does that mean if they are standing still they can not be detected under the normal effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of removing it altogether, seeing as I'm having a bit of a hard time interpreting it, too. Admittedly, I copy-pasted a good portion of the text for the Normal Effect from the Blind Sense Form Ability.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose when you say &quot;invisible to the eye but otherwise not hidden or obscured&quot;, it could probably mean those who aren't making any effort of hiding their presence (muffling their footsteps, moving slowly, etc.) even if they aren't seen. Optical invisibility isn't everything to stealth, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-28-2016, 08:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:42:48-08:00","id":818358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818343#post818343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking of removing it altogether, seeing as I'm having a bit of a hard time interpreting it, too. Admittedly, I copy-pasted a good portion of the text for the Normal Effect from the Blind Sense Form Ability.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose when you say &quot;invisible to the eye but otherwise not hidden or obscured&quot;, it could probably mean those who aren't making any effort of hiding their presence (muffling their footsteps, moving slowly, etc.) even if they aren't seen. Optical invisibility isn't everything to stealth, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly when you mention it can &quot;see&quot; though barriers wouldn't that rather invalidate concealment and obscuring (though maybe not totally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T05:46:23-08:00","id":818359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818358#post818358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Particularly when you mention it can &quot;see&quot; though barriers wouldn't that rather invalidate concealment and obscuring (though maybe not totally).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. So, a person walking in a room that's walled off from the hallway the Beast could be in should be readily detected. Now, imagine another person hiding in that room, consciously trying to keep quiet and avoid being seen by anyone. <i>That</i> would require a roll. Plus a Clash of Wills if said person is a supernatural using his abilities to better conceal himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T06:47:26-08:00","id":818390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818359#post818359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. So, a person walking in a room that's walled off from the hallway the Beast could be in should be readily detected. Now, imagine another person hiding in that room, consciously trying to keep quiet and avoid being seen by anyone. <i>That</i> would require a roll. Plus a Clash of Wills if said person is a supernatural using his abilities to better conceal himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T12:04:09-08:00","id":818619,"title":"","content":"Anyone have an idea for a name for an earth/tunnelling-based Atavism?<br /> <br /> The beast I've got so far is The Maggot God, but I'm not sure if that works with the way that Atavisms are usually named.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-28-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:31:36-08:00","id":818688,"title":"","content":"OK, here's the Atavism. Tell me what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>The Maggot God (Makara)</b><br /> <br /> Despite the shelter and nourishment it provides, humanity has always feared the earth. We range upon its surface and delve into the upper reaches of its crust, but in truth we know less about the interior of our own planet than about the far reaches of space. Humankind seeks refuge in the caves and holes closest to the surface, but even a few metres down you begin to feel the weight of the earth pressing down upon you. Even there, the cold and darkness of places that have never seen sunlight begin to play tricks upon the mind.<br /> <br /> Little wonder then that the things that dwell down there in the lightless reaches, conqueror worm and blind insect alike, hold a special place in the fears of humanity.<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast is a creature of the earth. Not of the surface, but of the lower reaches, the earth below even the deepest mineshafts.<br /> The Beast gains the ability to move at half his Speed through the earth and at a quarter of it through stone (round both up). He cannot move thus through concrete or other artificial materials, although cut stone is fair game. The Beast moves as though swimming, with the earth opening up, flowing around him and sealing up the passage after him. This does not destroy the things he passes through nor does it leave a hole but it does weaken them, subtracting 1 Durability for every time the Beast passes through the same spot. While underground, the Beast can sense the topography of the earth within (Lair*100) metres of his location. This sense is not subject to the same restrictions as the burrowing ability, but can only act upon earth or derivatives thereof (concrete, metal and tarmac yes, plastic and wood no).<br /> In addition, the Beast is immune to suffocation, cold, heat and pressure as a result of being underground (he can breathe fine if he is trapped in a cave-in, but not underwater. Likewise, he can travel into the upper reaches of the mantle without being crushed or melted but cannot survive the pressure at the bottom of the sea, being burned in a house fire or the Arctic wastes.)<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Beast\u2019s Hunger spurs him to greater speeds in pursuit of his prey. The Beast now moves at his full Speed through earth and half that through stone.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With the expenditure of a point of Satiety, the Beast can bring others with him into the earth. The Beast can take a number of people with him equal to his Lair. So long as the Beast is holding onto the passengers, they will not suffer from pressure, heat or suffocation. Nothing is preventing the Beast letting go however and for every 5 points of Size that the passengers comprise, the Beast\u2019s Speed is reduced by 1.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T15:53:57-08:00","id":818802,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiosity, does anyone have any ideas about space- or vacuum-themed Atavisms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T18:15:16-08:00","id":818898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818802#post818802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, does anyone have any ideas about space- or vacuum-themed Atavisms?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/521440-spaaaace-tiiilts#post521440\">amechra's Space Tilts</a> might offer some ideas for effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T05:16:23-08:00","id":819133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818898#post818898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/521440-spaaaace-tiiilts#post521440\">amechra's Space Tilts</a> might offer some ideas for effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I've got a name, 'From the Outer Darkness', and I'm pretty sure it's a Makara thing.<br /> <br /> I'm still not sure what to put as the actual effects. I'm beginning to think that the fear of space is more suited to Nightmares, as it is very thought-based. Creating a vacuum or microgravity seems to work better with Lair Traits. If anyone has any ideas for this Atavism, please help me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:04:01-08:00","id":819155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819133#post819133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. I've got a name, 'From the Outer Darkness', and I'm pretty sure it's a Makara thing.<br /> <br /> I'm still not sure what to put as the actual effects. I'm beginning to think that the fear of space is more suited to Nightmares, as it is very thought-based. Creating a vacuum or microgravity seems to work better with Lair Traits. If anyone has any ideas for this Atavism, please help me.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>From the Outer Darkness [Makara]</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Strength + Intimidation vs. Stamina + Supernatural Advantage (Normal Effect)<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> Many Leviathans favor Lairs that either crush trespassers under extreme pressure, or cause them to suffocate from a sudden lack of air to breathe. Such Lairs evoke landscapes ranging from the lightless depths of the ocean floor to even the cold, unforgiving void that is Space. However it manifests, Makara who possess such realms often develop this Atavism as a means to further capitalize on their inhospitable nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> Anyone within a radius of [Lair x5] feet from the Beast are sent crashing to the ground by a wave of intense pressure. They suffer the Knocked Down Tilt, and take lethal damage equal to half the Beast's Lair dots (rounded up).<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The pressure inflicted by the Atavism becomes so powerful that those laid low by it can barely move an inch. They suffer the Immobilized Tilt, and suffer a penalty equal to the Beast's Lair dots to all Strength + Athletic rolls made to break free.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The influence of the Beast's Lair seeps out of the Primordial Dream in a more concentrated manifestation. Unless they somehow escape, anyone trapped within the area will rapidly die from either the heightened pressure or asphyxiation. Spending a point of Satiety inflicts the grave version of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=223525#post223525\">Suffocate Tilt</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T08:46:36-08:00","id":819285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819155#post819155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about this?<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>From the Outer Darkness [Makara]</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Strength + Intimidation vs. Stamina + Supernatural Advantage (Normal Effect)<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> Many Leviathans favor Lairs that either crush trespassers under extreme pressure, or cause them to suffocate from a sudden lack of air to breathe. Such Lairs evoke landscapes ranging from the lightless depths of the ocean floor to even the cold, unforgiving void that is Space. However it manifests, Makara who possess such realms often develop this Atavism as a means to further capitalize on their inhospitable nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> Anyone within a radius of [Lair x5] feet from the Beast are sent crashing to the ground by a wave of intense pressure. They suffer the Knocked Down Tilt, and take lethal damage equal to half the Beast's Lair dots (rounded up).<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The pressure inflicted by the Atavism becomes so powerful that those laid low by it can barely move an inch. They suffer the Immobilized Tilt, and suffer a penalty equal to the Beast's Lair dots to all Strength + Athletic rolls made to break free.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The influence of the Beast's Lair seeps out of the Primordial Dream in a more concentrated manifestation. Unless they somehow escape, anyone trapped within the area will rapidly die from either the heightened pressure or asphyxiation. Spending a point of Satiety inflicts the grave version of the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/144034-fan-made-conditions?p=223525#post223525&amp;quot;]Suffocate</a> Tilt[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, but I don't think it quite works with the name. I'd call that one Crushing Will or something. <br /> <br /> I did consider something to do with gravity though. I had an idea that the atavism might include some kind of 'pull you to me' thing, based on the way that, if you break a hole in the side of a spaceship, the air rushes out and pulls you towards it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:20:03-08:00","id":819352,"title":"","content":"Here's one I've been tossing around:<br /> <br /> <b>Long of Limb (Eshmaki)</b><br /> <br /> The crushing tentacles of the kraken. The skeleton lord who builds upon himself with the remains of his fallen troops. The demon-clown with the impossibly-long, razor-sharp tongue. Horrors from every nightmare are maestros of grabbing things (or people) that should be out of their grasp. You can never escape the monster's hideous touch.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast's reach is increased by ten yards. He can pick up and manipulate nearby objects, as well as make Brawl rolls against foes who think themselves out of harm's way.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast's limbs grow even longer when he is hungry, and deadlier too. In addition to the Normal Effect, the Beast's reach increases by an extra (2 x Lair) yards. Furthermore, when the Beast makes a Brawl roll against someone from across some kind of threshold (such as if the Beast is underwater and grabs someone on land, or lunges out of the shadows into the light), he may immediately perform a grapple move against his victim as if he had already established a grapple. The aboleth drags its prey into the deeps, while the demon-clown just wants to latch on from afar.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes the true horror (and Horror) of the inescapable truth of his hunger. Increase his reach by another ten yards. When he makes Brawl rolls at a distance, those who cannot see the Horror can only use Wits or Dexterity for Defense. Finally, add the Beast's Lair to all grapple rolls, which are considered an Exceptional Success on three successes instead of five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:23:26-08:00","id":819356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819352#post819352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I've been tossing around:<br /> <br /> <b>Long of Limb (Eshmaki)</b><br /> <br /> The crushing tentacles of the kraken. The skeleton lord who builds upon himself with the remains of his fallen troops. The demon-clown with the impossibly-long, razor-sharp tongue. Horrors from every nightmare are maestros of grabbing things (or people) that should be out of their grasp. You can never escape the monster's hideous touch.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast's reach is increased by ten yards. He can pick up and manipulate nearby objects, as well as make Brawl rolls against foes who think themselves out of harm's way.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast's limbs grow even longer when he is hungry, and deadlier too. In addition to the Normal Effect, the Beast's reach increases by an extra (2 x Lair) yards. Furthermore, when the Beast makes a Brawl roll against someone from across some kind of threshold (such as if the Beast is underwater and grabs someone on land, or lunges out of the shadows into the light), he may immediately perform a grapple move against his victim as if he had already established a grapple. The aboleth drags its prey into the deeps, while the demon-clown just wants to latch on from afar.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes the true horror (and Horror) of the inescapable truth of his hunger. Increase his reach by another ten yards. When he makes Brawl rolls at a distance, those who cannot see the Horror can only use Wits or Dexterity for Defense. Finally, add the Beast's Lair to all grapple rolls, which are considered an Exceptional Success on three successes instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, does this manifest as telekinesis in the physical world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:42:49-08:00","id":819365,"title":"","content":"To the un-supernatural, I would believe so, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T10:56:02-08:00","id":819372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819365#post819365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To the un-supernatural, I would believe so, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, just wanted some clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:28:04-08:00","id":819462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819285#post819285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like it, but I don't think it quite works with the name. I'd call that one Crushing Will or something.<br /> <br /> I did consider something to do with gravity though. I had an idea that the atavism might include some kind of 'pull you to me' thing, based on the way that, if you break a hole in the side of a spaceship, the air rushes out and pulls you towards it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see.<br /> And yeah, Crushing Will works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:26:53-08:00","id":819807,"title":"","content":"OK, I've had a go at writing From the Outer Darkness and I think it works, but the Satiety Expenditure might be too strong. If I could bet some feedback that would be great.<br /> <br /> <b>From the Outer Darkness (Makara)</b><br /> <br /> People don\u2019t like to think about space, not really. Oh, they talk about the planets and the stars and how they all orbit each other and how pretty they look, but they never dwell too long on what lies in between. The cold void that is as close to empty as really exists. The human mind cannot comprehend that place. It was not made to handle the sizes involved. Not meant to process the concept of so vast an emptiness.<br /> Except what if it\u2019s not empty? What if something <i>is </i>there, lairing in the voids between stars? What kind of creature could exist there, writhing in the un-light of dead stars?<br /> You know.<br /> You are that creature.<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive, Instant (Satiety Expenditure and slowing breathing or heartbeat.)<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>the Beast is a creature of the places between worlds, of the dark void where noting moves but it and the solar winds, feeble as they are. The need for air is a foreign to him and the time between meals or beats of his heart is measured in millennia. The Beast may go without food, water or air for a number of years equal to his Stamina before he begins to feel the effects of starvation, thirst or suffocation. The Beast is also immune to the effects of a vacuum beyond suffocation, such as boiling blood.<br /> In addition the Beast may, with an Instant action, slow down his heartbeat enormously, effectively placing venoms and poisons into stasis and allowing them to degrade into their component chemicals. This could also be used to fake death, as the Beast can also stop breathing without any ill effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As the Beast\u2019s hunger grows and the desires of his Horror begin to bleed through into his consciousness, he begins to see the warp and weft of reality and the flaws therein. As the alien mathematics that the Horror performs on instinct filter into his mind, he becomes aware of the places in reality that don\u2019t quite <i>fit </i>and learns how to take advantage of the little gaps and flaws in the world that go unnoticed by almost all.<br /> The Beast is aware of all distortions in space within an area equal to (Lair*10) yards including God-Machine Infrastructure, Avernian Gates, active spells of the Space Arcana, Trods and a Demon\u2019s Bolthole, although he only knows of its existence and location, not its nature.<br /> In addition, the Beast\u2019s Lair is added to his Speed and he may ignore any barrier which is less than the Beast\u2019s Lair feet thick as he steps through the cracks in reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With an exertion of effort the Beast pulls a hypergeometrical equation from the mind of his Horror, one that allows him to not only take advantage of a flaw in space-time, but to alter it to lead where he wants.<br /> The Beast can effectively \u2018teleport\u2019 to any location that he has been before or knows the precise coordinates of. These coordinates must be accurate to within at least a metre (so looking up the latitude and longitude of Fort Knox won\u2019t do you any good). This ability cannot transport a Beast to another realm such as the Hedge or the Shadow. It can operate within those realms though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-31-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T23:35:28-08:00","id":820192,"title":"","content":"So, any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T04:47:40-08:00","id":820261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=820192#post820192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, any thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Satiety Expenditure seems a bit too overpowered for me. It essentially renders the need for the Primordial Pathways moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T04:58:51-08:00","id":820269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=820261#post820261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. Satiety Expenditure seems a bit too overpowered for me. It essentially renders the need for the Primordial Pathways moot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I could easily make it so that it can only travel within the world you currently occupy and possibly limit the range. How does (Lair*100) kilometres sound to you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T05:06:38-08:00","id":820273,"title":"","content":"Yeah. That seems more plausible.<br /> If other people might still have reservations, perhaps spending Satiety to exponentially increase the Beast's speed (aka <i>hyperspeed</i>) could be a nice alternative to fall back to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T05:18:49-08:00","id":820279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=820273#post820273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. That seems more plausible.<br /> If other people might still have reservations, perhaps spending Satiety to exponentially increase the Beast's speed (aka <i>hyperspeed</i>) could be a nice alternative to fall back to.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea was that the Horror would use the teleportation to cross vast distances in space, hence the long (read: Unlimited) range. I was trying to get a sense of 'doesn't fit in our physics/cthulhu-ishness'. It was partially inspired by the Hounds of Tindalos from the Cthulhu Mythos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T05:37:34-08:00","id":820283,"title":"","content":"Ahh. Noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T03:00:14-08:00","id":822231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819352#post819352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I've been tossing around:<br /> <br /> <b>Long of Limb (Eshmaki)</b><br /> <br /> The crushing tentacles of the kraken. The skeleton lord who builds upon himself with the remains of his fallen troops. The demon-clown with the impossibly-long, razor-sharp tongue. Horrors from every nightmare are maestros of grabbing things (or people) that should be out of their grasp. You can never escape the monster's hideous touch.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast's reach is increased by ten yards. He can pick up and manipulate nearby objects, as well as make Brawl rolls against foes who think themselves out of harm's way.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast's limbs grow even longer when he is hungry, and deadlier too. In addition to the Normal Effect, the Beast's reach increases by an extra (2 x Lair) yards. Furthermore, when the Beast makes a Brawl roll against someone from across some kind of threshold (such as if the Beast is underwater and grabs someone on land, or lunges out of the shadows into the light), he may immediately perform a grapple move against his victim as if he had already established a grapple. The aboleth drags its prey into the deeps, while the demon-clown just wants to latch on from afar.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes the true horror (and Horror) of the inescapable truth of his hunger. Increase his reach by another ten yards. When he makes Brawl rolls at a distance, those who cannot see the Horror can only use Wits or Dexterity for Defense. Finally, add the Beast's Lair to all grapple rolls, which are considered an Exceptional Success on three successes instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can the Beast use Atavisms that rely on touch (like Limb From Limb) on someone they touch with this Atavism? Could a Beast with Fist of Nightmares use this to deliver it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T07:34:53-08:00","id":822367,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. I think I would say yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:01:13-08:00","id":822392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819352#post819352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I've been tossing around:<br /> <br /> <b>Long of Limb (Eshmaki)</b><br /> <br /> The crushing tentacles of the kraken. The skeleton lord who builds upon himself with the remains of his fallen troops. The demon-clown with the impossibly-long, razor-sharp tongue. Horrors from every nightmare are maestros of grabbing things (or people) that should be out of their grasp. You can never escape the monster's hideous touch.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast's reach is increased by ten yards. He can pick up and manipulate nearby objects, as well as make Brawl rolls against foes who think themselves out of harm's way.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast's limbs grow even longer when he is hungry, and deadlier too. In addition to the Normal Effect, the Beast's reach increases by an extra (2 x Lair) yards. Furthermore, when the Beast makes a Brawl roll against someone from across some kind of threshold (such as if the Beast is underwater and grabs someone on land, or lunges out of the shadows into the light), he may immediately perform a grapple move against his victim as if he had already established a grapple. The aboleth drags its prey into the deeps, while the demon-clown just wants to latch on from afar.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes the true horror (and Horror) of the inescapable truth of his hunger. Increase his reach by another ten yards. When he makes Brawl rolls at a distance, those who cannot see the Horror can only use Wits or Dexterity for Defense. Finally, add the Beast's Lair to all grapple rolls, which are considered an Exceptional Success on three successes instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, does the Beast have to move his arms in human form in order to use this? It's just because I had an idea for a Beast that uses this Atavism, along with Limb From Limb, like the vectors from Elfen Lied","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:14:41-08:00","id":822403,"title":"","content":"I'm unfamiliar with whatever that is. Is it an anime?<br /> <br /> Anyway, to answer your question, maybe? I was going to say yes, but then I began thinking about situations where the Beast is restrained in some way, and I think how one's extended limbs move is going to depend on the form the Horror takes. A rope golem is going to have an easier time of it than a skeleton lord. That's a bit of a soft interpretation though. Maybe the Atavism should give the Beast the Double Jointed merit for free?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:28:20-08:00","id":822417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=822403#post822403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm unfamiliar with whatever that is. Is it an anime?<br /> <br /> Anyway, to answer your question, maybe? I was going to say yes, but then I began thinking about situations where the Beast is restrained in some way, and I think how one's extended limbs move is going to depend on the form the Horror takes. A rope golem is going to have an easier time of it than a skeleton lord. That's a bit of a soft interpretation though. Maybe the Atavism should give the Beast the Double Jointed merit for free?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is an anime yes. If you're not comfortable with blood, don't watch it. Basically, I was envisioning a character who used this Atavism to fake hauntings (or perhaps used Kinship with Sin-Eaters to make real ones?), acting as an exorcist. He fed off of the fear that the people in the 'haunted' house felt, as he would wait before getting rid of the 'ghost', saying that the exorcism needs to happen on a particular day or whatever, letting them stew in their own fear for a while.<br /> <br /> About the Double Jointed Merit, I would give the Merit, but rather than actually saying that it gives them the merit, give them the effects of the thing in the Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:46:18-08:00","id":822429,"title":"","content":"That's a good point re: DJ.<br /> <br /> And that sounds like a pretty legit use of the Atavism around normies. Even if the Beast does have to move their arms, you can always brush it off as ritual mudras or such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:03:33-08:00","id":822443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=822429#post822429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point re: DJ.<br /> <br /> And that sounds like a pretty legit use of the Atavism around normies. Even if the Beast does have to move their arms, you can always brush it off as ritual mudras or such.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or I guess you could have two Beasts working together, one who creates 'haunting' effects and one who exorcises. The exorcist could easily be some other kind of supernatural, especially a mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T09:47:50-08:00","id":822468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=819352#post819352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's one I've been tossing around:<br /> <br /> <b>Long of Limb (Eshmaki)</b><br /> <br /> The crushing tentacles of the kraken. The skeleton lord who builds upon himself with the remains of his fallen troops. The demon-clown with the impossibly-long, razor-sharp tongue. Horrors from every nightmare are maestros of grabbing things (or people) that should be out of their grasp. You can never escape the monster's hideous touch.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast's reach is increased by ten yards. He can pick up and manipulate nearby objects, as well as make Brawl rolls against foes who think themselves out of harm's way.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast's limbs grow even longer when he is hungry, and deadlier too. In addition to the Normal Effect, the Beast's reach increases by an extra (2 x Lair) yards. Furthermore, when the Beast makes a Brawl roll against someone from across some kind of threshold (such as if the Beast is underwater and grabs someone on land, or lunges out of the shadows into the light), he may immediately perform a grapple move against his victim as if he had already established a grapple. The aboleth drags its prey into the deeps, while the demon-clown just wants to latch on from afar.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes the true horror (and Horror) of the inescapable truth of his hunger. Increase his reach by another ten yards. When he makes Brawl rolls at a distance, those who cannot see the Horror can only use Wits or Dexterity for Defense. Finally, add the Beast's Lair to all grapple rolls, which are considered an Exceptional Success on three successes instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is OP and invalidates Monster from the Deep. 10 yard reach for nothing, that can increase to upwards of 20 for a Satiety, free grapples, lower Exceptionals, and hosing Defense together will break the game, both in terms of balance and overall tone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T10:30:24-08:00","id":822492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=822468#post822468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is OP and invalidates Monster from the Deep. 10 yard reach for nothing, that can increase to upwards of 20 for a Satiety, free grapples, lower Exceptionals, and hosing Defense together will break the game, both in terms of balance and overall tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps if the reach was lowered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:37:21-08:00","id":822872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=822468#post822468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is OP and invalidates Monster from the Deep. 10 yard reach for nothing, that can increase to upwards of 20 for a Satiety, free grapples, lower Exceptionals, and hosing Defense together will break the game, both in terms of balance and overall tone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see what you mean. I was hoping there wasn't too much overlap, since Monster From the Deep's big thing is hitting multiple opponents at once, but there might be issues. Here are my first thoughts on changes:<ul><li><b>Normal Effect:</b> Extension of 5 yards, gain effects of Double Jointed.</li> <li><b>Low Satiety:</b> Increase of 5 yards, add Lair to grapple rolls.</li> <li><b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Increase of 5 yards, gain effects of Advanced Double Jointed (except for the fitting-through-tight-spaces part).</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T19:27:12-08:00","id":822972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=822872#post822872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see what you mean. I was hoping there wasn't too much overlap, since Monster From the Deep's big thing is hitting multiple opponents at once, but there might be issues. Here are my first thoughts on changes:<ul><li><b>Normal Effect:</b> Extension of 5 yards, gain effects of Double Jointed.</li> <li><b>Low Satiety:</b> Increase of 5 yards, add Lair to grapple rolls.</li> <li><b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Increase of 5 yards, gain effects of Advanced Double Jointed (except for the fitting-through-tight-spaces part).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Looks better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:45:40-08:00","id":825898,"title":"","content":"Just an idea for an Atavism: Untouchable.<br /> This would be used to represent a semi-intangible creature or one that can just weave around bullets or blows. Perhaps adding Lair to Defence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T04:48:47-08:00","id":825918,"title":"","content":"That sounds like an Anakim or Makara Atavism.<br /> <br /> I can see the Lair being added to Defense as a Normal Effect.<br /> <br /> For Low Satiety, I was thinking that the Atavism should downgrade (by one level) damage take in a turn equal to the Beast's Lair.<br /> <br /> The Satiety Expenditure could treat all failed attack rolls made by the opponent as dramatic failures. And/or allow the Begotten to make a counterattack when the opponent misses in his attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T04:55:31-08:00","id":825921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=825918#post825918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like an Anakim or Makara Atavism.<br /> <br /> I can see the Lair being added to Defense as a Normal Effect.<br /> <br /> For Low Satiety, I was thinking that the Atavism should downgrade (by one level) damage take in a turn equal to the Beast's Lair.<br /> <br /> The Satiety Expenditure could treat all failed attack rolls made by the opponent as dramatic failures. And/or allow the Begotten to make a counterattack when the opponent misses in his attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. I think that would work. If we both do our own versions of it and compare them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T20:23:44-08:00","id":827285,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Untouchable</u> [Eshmaki]</b><br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> Some of the most terrifying monsters in human legends are those that one cannot lay hands on. Leviathans who develop this Atavism are not entirely tangible beings, or perhaps just simply too fast for anyone to strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast adds his Lair dots to his Defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> As Hunger gains ascendancy within his thoughts, the Beast becomes almost impossible to hit, causing his foes to stumble and harm themselves in their attempts to harm it. All failed attack rolls made against the Beast are now treated as dramatic failures.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a point of Satiety after his opponent fails an attack roll, the Beast can react quickly to inflict a devastating counterattack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":".  Edited it to be an Eshmaki Atavism. 02-12-2016, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T01:43:42-08:00","id":827359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=827285#post827285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Untouchable</u> [Makara]</b><br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> Some of the most terrifying monsters in human legends are those that one cannot lay hands on. Leviathans who develop this Atavism are not entirely tangible beings, or perhaps just simply too fast for anyone to strike.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast adds his Lair dots to his Defense. <br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> As Hunger gains ascendancy within his thoughts, the Beast becomes almost impossible to hit, causing his foes to stumble and harm themselves in their attempts to harm it. All failed attack rolls made against the Beast are now treated as dramatic failures.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a point of Satiety after his opponent fails an attack roll, the Beast can react quickly to inflict a devastating counterattack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good, I'm just wondering why it's a Makara atavism. I would have put it as an Eshmaki one. If you could just explain your reasoning that would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T15:12:42-08:00","id":827819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=827359#post827359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's good, I'm just wondering why it's a Makara atavism. I would have put it as an Eshmaki one. If you could just explain your reasoning that would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, you're right. It would make more sense as an Eshmaki Atavism given how it's about evasion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> There. tweaked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 02-12-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T16:07:33-08:00","id":829896,"title":"","content":"So, I noticed that there was relatively little space directed to interacting with the Ephemeral, in the 1st draft, at least. So, I figured I'd put together my first Atavism. Tell me what you think and how much of it is trash, if you have the time?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>WHAT WALKS BETWEEN (Makara)</b><br /> It comforts many humans to believe that the world their paltry senses can see is the only one. When the things that lurk beyond the veil reach out to menace them, they cannot comprehend what is happening in the seconds it takes to be destroyed. You, on the other hand, extend beyond this state of being, a serpent whose coils trail away under the surface into the realm of ephemeral. <br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b>Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b>The Beast may attune themselves to the strange state of existence occultists call Twilight, allowing them to see and hear(and be seen and heard by) the ephemeral beings that exist within, not limited by any particular &quot;frequency&quot;. Splitting their senses like this, however, makes it harder to focus on the world around them, however, and imposes a -2 penalty to Perception rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b>A hungering Leviathan finds the fetters limiting them to but one state of being fading, allowing for a more perfect quantum duality. The Begotten no longer suffers a penalty to Perception rolls, and may interact with objects and beings in both solid reality and in Twilight as if he were in the appropriate state of existence. The Child may not turn this effect off, of course, leaving him just as vulnerable to the attacks of others as they are to him.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The immense potency of the Beast's Horror exerts itself on the unfleshed entities around him, a world-spanning gravity that bends ephemeral beings to their will. The Begotten gains an Honorary Rank equal to (10 - [Satiety], to a maximum of 5) for the rest of the scene. As normal for Honorary Rank, the Beast counts as a Bane for any ephemeral with a Rank two less than theirs, and they also gain a number of dice against such beings with a lower Rank as if comparing Status. Neither of these effects work against Angels or beings otherwise of the God-Machine. If a character is in a Chamber (whether in their Lair or the area they copied), they add two to their Rank for the purpose of acting as a Bane.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T02:05:12-08:00","id":830102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=829896#post829896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I noticed that there was relatively little space directed to interacting with the Ephemeral, in the 1st draft, at least. So, I figured I'd put together my first Atavism. Tell me what you think and how much of it is trash, if you have the time?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>WHAT WALKS BETWEEN (Makara)</b><br /> It comforts many humans to believe that the world their paltry senses can see is the only one. When the things that lurk beyond the veil reach out to menace them, they cannot comprehend what is happening in the seconds it takes to be destroyed. You, on the other hand, extend beyond this state of being, a serpent whose coils trail away under the surface into the realm of ephemeral.*<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b>Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b>The Beast may attune themselves to the strange state of existence occultists call Twilight, allowing them to see and hear(and be seen and heard by) the ephemeral beings that exist within, not limited by any particular &amp;quot;frequency&amp;quot;. Splitting their senses like this, however, makes it harder to focus on the world around them, however, and imposes a -2 penalty to Perception rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b>A hungering Leviathan finds the fetters limiting them to but one state of being fading, allowing for a more perfect quantum duality. The Begotten no longer suffers a penalty to Perception rolls, and may interact with objects and beings in both solid reality and in Twilight as if he were in the appropriate state of existence. The Child may not turn this effect off, of course, leaving him just as vulnerable to the attacks of others as they are to him.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The immense potency of the Beast's Horror exerts itself on the unfleshed entities around him, a world-spanning gravity that bends*ephemeral beings to their will. The Begotten gains an Honorary Rank equal to (10 - [Satiety], to a maximum of 5) for the rest of the scene. As normal for*Honorary Rank, the Beast counts as a Bane for any*ephemeral with a Rank two less than theirs, and they also gain a number of dice against such beings with a lower Rank as if comparing Status. Neither of these effects work against Angels or beings otherwise of the God-Machine. If a character is in a Chamber (whether in their Lair or the area they copied), they add two to their Rank for the purpose of acting as a Bane.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>This is really good. The one thing I'd add would be the ability to sense verges and loci at Normal Effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T21:08:49-08:00","id":832309,"title":"","content":"A couple based on two very beast-like inspirations: Tesuo the Iron Man and Slenderman. <br /> <br /> <b>Mechanical Monster</b> (Anikim)<br /> The crushing gears, the roaring engines, the pitiless motions of steel and oil. Though not all beasts are drawn to machines many feel a sympathy to the power and utility that such creations represent. Humanity has often anthropomorphised the machines it interacts with taking comfort that the gears didn\u2019t intend to maliciously crush their limbs. <br /> <br /> Normal: The beast knows machines as it knows the flesh and bone that makes its body. The beast may replace the Equipment bonuses using equipment and tools for their lair rating whichever is higher. The beast\u2019s rolls gain the 8-again quality when interacting with non-electronic machines. <br /> <br /> Low Satiety: When the hunger grows the tools of humanity are no defense against the beast, what was once a helpful tool is now submissive to the beast\u2019s desires. Beasts may lower equipment advantages that characters receive equal to lair dots up to the point where characters receive a penalty for using their tools. The beast may only commit this effect to a number of objects equal to wits dots. Any object\u2019s bonus that is reduced to a negative loses its durability.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The line between flesh and machine blurs as the beast\u2019s horror makes manifest through inanimate components. The horror reshapes metal and machine to make manifest outside of the Primordial dream. The beast\u2019s body absorbs nearby machinery in order to shape the horror with hinges, pistons, and engines. The beast gains 2/2 armor and their lair dots in expendable health dots. This allows the beast to gain the advantage of merging with the beast (P.99) without existing in the mortal realm by adding points to relevant traits. If the beast loses all expendable health dots they lose the points of armor. At the end of the scene the shell breaks down into useless parts.<br /> Note: Expendable health dots are first filled when taking damage, when they are all filled with aggravated wounds they are discarded.<br /> <br /> <b>Electric Enigma</b> (Eshmaki)<br /> Bottled Lightning. The beast feels at home with the hum of electricity channeled into utilitarian ends. The beast feels at home with circuits and programs, not a ghost in a shell, but a being with awareness of the potentials contained within.<br /> <br /> Normal: Glitches seldom seem to happen around the beast, or if they do they happen in the beast\u2019s favor. The beast sings the song of circuitry, the begotten gains 9 again to Computer rolls and rolls that deal with electronics. Furthermore the beast is immune to electric damage.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: When the beast hunger spreads it seems even circuits are aware of the threat the beast represents. The beast may cause a localized brown-out wherever they go, electronics shut down and malfunction within 3 meters x Lair of the beast. This does not damage the electronic circuitry, the electricity itself seems to shy away refusing to appear. The beast may turn this ability on and off.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The beast\u2019s form becomes a sentient electric charge. Using this form the beast may travel through wiring or other conductive material at Speed x Lair+1 per turn. While in this form the beast may control electronic devices at a touch and deal bashing damage with Dex + Brawl using their lair as a weapon modifier. Characters who strike the beast while this is active with Brawl or weaponry receive Lair dots in bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T03:10:12-08:00","id":832417,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure if it <i>should</i> be a Raptor Atavism, but I made it as such, considering which monster this was inspired by.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b><u>From the Ashes</u> [Ugallu]</b><br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Resolve + Composure (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> The phoenix is a symbol of life, death, and rebirth, long thought to have been kin of the Raptors. Those Nightmares of Exposure who develop this Atavism emulate the mythical firebird's vitality, and perhaps also its ability to defy the chill of death.<br /> <br /> <u>Normal Effect</u>: The Beast is tied more strongly to the energies of the Primordial Dream, and draws upon it for greater reserves of strength. She now gains additional Health dots equal to her own Lair rating.<br /> <br /> <u>Low Satiety</u>: As the Beast's Hunger grows, the fires of her life burn more fiercely in its refusal to be extinguished. Every time she is attacked in a turn, she downgrades the first [Lair] points of damage by one level. In the case of bashing damage, this means she ignores the first [Lair] points of bashing damage inflicted in a turn.<br /> <br /> <u>Satiety Expenditure</u>: By spending a point of Satiety at the moment of death, the Beast's body dissipates as her consciousness flees into her Lair. There, it reforms as an egg, with a Durability and Structure rating equal to her Lair dots.It must then incubate for a period of [10 - Satiety] weeks, during which it is protected only by her Horror. If the egg is still intact by the end of this period, it hatches, allowing the revived Beast to merge with her Horror. The destruction of the egg before its incubation is complete, however, kills the Beast for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 01-05-2017, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:26:50-08:00","id":833241,"title":"","content":"Does anyone want to play a Voodoo beast?<br /> <br /> <u><b>In My Image (Ugallu)</b></u><br /> <br /> Many different peoples in different parts of the world once held that taking an image of someone stole and trapped a little of their soul. Of course, in the modern day people scoff at this and treat it as superstitious rubbish, ignoring the fact that people who appear in images constantly \u2013 like supermodels, movie stars and important politicians \u2013 constantly hide behind makeup and glamour, as if they are filling in or hiding something else.<br /> <br /> For some, though, images do not steal. Rather, they strengthen, pouring them back on themselves. For some, images are more than just representations of a person. For some, they are power.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast is instantly aware when any image of him is captured, by any medium. He does not know its exact location but can roll Wits + Lair to ascertain a rough direction and distance. This image need not be a picture. It could also be a statue or any other representation of the Beast. Once the image has been captured, the Beast may roll again as many times as he likes in order to locate it again. This ability only works if the image is within Lair * 100 metres of the Beast\u2019s current location.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Beast may look out from any image of himself that he knows the location of within a radius of Lair * 100 metres and may edit any image within that same radius. Both of these actions require a Wits + Manipulation roll. If the image concerned is stored in a computerised form it can only be accessed while it is being displayed.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As the Horror\u2019s hunger grows so too does its perspicacity. The Beast can now roll Wits + Lair in order to pinpoint the location exactly.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Beast can now not only see through his images but also exert his other senses and use Nightmares on those who meet the eyes of his image. More than one Beast has used an image of himself, carefully placed in another\u2019s home, to haunt his sleep. This is subject to the same distance limitations as seeing through them, although the distance at which the Beast may manipulate his image is increased to Lair * 200 metres.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With the expenditure of a point of Satiety, the Beast can not only manipulate his own image but also that of another. With an extended Wits + Crafts roll with a target number of the target's (Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance) rolling once per hour the Beast can craft an image of a person, very much reminiscent of a stereotypical Voodoo doll. In order to do so, the Beast must possess a part of the target\u2019s body. Blood or hair work well. Once the image is crafted, the Beast treats the target as though he were an image of the Beast himself so long as the Beast is holding the image. He can use other uses of this Atavism on him (besides altering the image). If his Satiety is low, he can cast Nightmares on the target. The power of the image lasts for a number of days equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair before fading.<br /> The target rolls (Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance) contested by the Beast's (Presence + Lair) once per day that the Atavism is active. If the target wins, the Beast cannot target them through the doll for that day, although the connection still remains and he may try again the next day. If the beast wins or if the result is a draw the beast may continue to use the image. For every successful roll to resist, the Beast suffers cumulative -1 die penalty to any attempts to use the doll for purposes beyond scrying. If the target gets an Exceptional Success, the Satiety Expenditure effect is cut off, and the Beast cannot re-use that effect until the days that were remaining pass.<br /> Targets with the means to strike back at remotely activated powers, such as Mages, may do so at the ST's discretion. Someone who resists this power for long enough may develop an intuition that the Beast is to blame and a vague awareness of where to find the doll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-21-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:41:56-08:00","id":833255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833241#post833241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone want to play a Voodoo beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal and Low Satiety sounds much more like Cthulhu's dread idol visions from <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> - but I like it even more that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T07:50:30-08:00","id":833260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833255#post833255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Normal and Low Satiety sounds much more like Cthulhu's dread idol visions from <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> - but I like it even more that way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hahahaha! Do you think it works though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:03:12-08:00","id":833567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833260#post833260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hahahaha! Do you think it works though?</div> </div> </div> </div> I liked it a lot. It reminded me of the Weeping Angels from Doctor Who. However, the ability to remotely cast Nightmares for weeks, even with the necessity of acquiring a body part before, is too long. I'd also limit how many uses each voodoo doll has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:20:01-08:00","id":833571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833567#post833567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I liked it a lot. It reminded me of the Weeping Angels from Doctor Who. However, the ability to remotely cast Nightmares for weeks, even with the necessity of acquiring a body part before, is too long. I'd also limit how many uses each voodoo doll has.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was actually inspired by the Angels. And I admit to paraphrasing most of the opening fluff from Witches Abroad by the ever-wonderful Terry Pratchett.<br /> <br /> The power of the Satiety expenditure power was deliberate. The idea being that the beast could use it as a kind of sword of Damocles. <br /> I think I'll keep the unlimited uses but If I was to shorten the duration, what would you recommend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:21:57-08:00","id":833572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833567#post833567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I liked it a lot. It reminded me of the Weeping Angels from Doctor Who. However, the ability to remotely cast Nightmares for weeks, even with the necessity of acquiring a body part before, is too long. I'd also limit how many uses each voodoo doll has.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could imagine a powerful Tyrant repeatedly using the You Must Obey Nightmare through an image of his enemies in order to discredit him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:38:46-08:00","id":833582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833571#post833571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was actually inspired by the Angels. And I admit to paraphrasing most of the opening fluff from Witches Abroad by the ever-wonderful Terry Pratchett.<br /> <br /> The power of the Satiety expenditure power was deliberate. The idea being that the beast could use it as a kind of sword of Damocles.<br /> I think I'll keep the unlimited uses but If I was to shorten the duration, what would you recommend?</div> </div> </div> </div> I would lower it to [Lair] days. I'd allow the target to roll their Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance each day. If they exceed the Beast's Successes, the power does not work, and repeated attempts impose a cumulative -1 penalty to the Beast's roll, as usual. If the target gets an Exceptional Success, the Satiety Expenditure effect is cut off, and the Beast cannot re-use that effect until the days that were remaining pass. Targets with the means to strike back at remotely activated powers, such as Mages, may do so at the ST's discretion. Someone who resists this power for long enough may develop an intuition that the Beast is to blame and a vague awareness of where to find the doll. By the way, you forgot to add the time per roll and a target number of Successes for the Wits + Crafts roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 02-19-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:42:41-08:00","id":833584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833572#post833572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could imagine a powerful Tyrant repeatedly using the You Must Obey Nightmare through an image of his enemies in order to discredit him.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Tyrant could also use the target as a walking poster of the Big Brother.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T16:49:40-08:00","id":833588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833584#post833584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Tyrant could also use the target as a walking poster of the Big Brother.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought was an Earthbound Demon's Reliquiary (from Demon: The Fallen). Very easy to get a cult running with that Atavism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T23:29:28-08:00","id":833729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833582#post833582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would lower it to [Lair] days. I'd allow the target to roll their Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance each day. If they exceed the Beast's Successes, the power does not work, and repeated attempts impose a cumulative -1 penalty to the Beast's roll, as usual. If the target gets an Exceptional Success, the Satiety Expenditure effect is cut off, and the Beast cannot re-use that effect until the days that were remaining pass. Targets with the means to strike back at remotely activated powers, such as Mages, may do so at the ST's discretion. Someone who resists this power for long enough may develop an intuition that the Beast is to blame and a vague awareness of where to find the doll. By the way, you forgot to add the time per roll and a target number of Successes for the Wits + Crafts roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T08:34:09-08:00","id":834442,"title":"","content":"The thought just occurred to me, there's no atavism to represent multiple heads. And that's something that appears in dozens of mythologies all over the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T08:37:54-08:00","id":834445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=834442#post834442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought just occurred to me, there's no atavism to represent multiple heads. And that's something that appears in dozens of mythologies all over the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monster From the Deep can get you that effect readily enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T08:44:26-08:00","id":834448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=834445#post834445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Monster From the Deep can get you that effect readily enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant stuff like multiple perspectives, several pairs of eyes etc. I can see what you mean though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:04:24-08:00","id":834474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=834448#post834448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant stuff like multiple perspectives, several pairs of eyes etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needs Must.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:12:09-08:00","id":834477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=834474#post834474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Needs Must.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-23T13:23:02-08:00","id":835986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=833588#post833588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought was an Earthbound Demon's Reliquiary (from Demon: The Fallen). Very easy to get a cult running with that Atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Beasts-as-Fallen Angels could be an interesting hack. They feed their Hunger for Sin, and seek to either return to God's grace (Retreat), descend into sinful madness (Merger), or free themselves from the shadow of their Fall (Incarnate). Their Lairs are shards of the Inferno, and Heroes become divine servitors hunting them at the behest of the Earthbound (effectively, other Incarnate Beasts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:20:02-07:00","id":853008,"title":"","content":"Here's another Atavism. I know it's a little close to Cavernous Maw but I thought I'd focus more on the Jonah-and-the-Whale type thing.<br /> <br /> <u><b>All-Consuming (Makara)</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The Beast gains the ability to devour anything of a Size equal to or less than his (Lair * 2) with no ill effects. In addition, the Beast may gain sustenance from any substance he eats. A Beast could subsist off of only stone if necessary. The Beast may attempt to swallow a living creature so long as it is unable to fight back (i.e., is incapacitated, unconscious, sleeping or held down). Following the consumption, the creature is dealt 1 Lethal damage each turn until it dies. However, once inside, the creature may attempt to break out of the Beast\u2019s maw. This is an extended contested roll of the creature Strength + Resolve + Supernatural Resistance vs the Beast\u2019s Stamina + Composure + Lair. Each roll takes a turn and the contest continues until the victim is either knocked unconscious or accumulates a number of successes equal to the Beast\u2019s Lair + Stamina. If the victim succeeds, he claws his way out of the Beast\u2019s mouth and both Beast and Victim suffer the Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Beast\u2019s growing hunger allows him to attempt to devour a Grappled opponent with a Contested Strength + Lair vs Strength + Stamina roll. If the Beast succeeds, treat it as if they had swallowed a living creature as above.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With the expenditure of a point of Satiety, the Beast tears open a connection to the Primordial Dream within himself, making his gaping maw into a portal to his Lair through which any that he devours are transported. Alternatively, those who are devoured can be imprisoned in a \u2018pocket dimension\u2019 of sorts which appears as some kind of confinement, as appropriate to the Horror. A Horror that takes the form of a gargantuan robotic monstrosity might trap its victims in a steel cell while a vast whale\u2019s meals go straight to its stomach. Note that the pocket dimension cannot have any kind of harmful contents. A stomach might be knee-deep in gooey green slime but it could not contain acid, for example. The Beast may spend a turn \u2018vomiting up\u2019 any swallowed using this ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T23:26:49-07:00","id":869131,"title":"","content":"I can't help but wonder if some of the effects we've discussed aren't better represented via the ability to impose Lair Traits on an environment. Such as the deep cold power, or webbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T23:40:10-07:00","id":869139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=869131#post869131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but wonder if some of the effects we've discussed aren't better represented via the ability to impose Lair Traits on an environment. Such as the deep cold power, or webbing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps, but Atavisms are more directable and usable. You'd use Atavisms when the effect is a part of the Horror as opposed to a part of the Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:01:21-07:00","id":871396,"title":"","content":"I know what effects I'd like to see Atavisms emulating, but I suck at designing mechanics.<br /> Still, we could have an Atavism to mimic the crafting prowess of the Cyclopes and Telchines, an Atavism for the healing properties of Medusa's blood or unicorn's horn, an Atavism for mimicking long prehensile arms, tentacles, or tails to manipulate objects remotely, an Atavism to burrow through earth and rock and survive underground, an Atavism to allow hibernation or cryptobiosis over long periods, an Atavism to see and even reach into Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:06:24-07:00","id":871401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=871396#post871396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what effects I'd like to see Atavisms emulating, but I suck at designing mechanics.<br /> Still, we could have an Atavism to mimic the crafting prowess of the Cyclopes and Telchines, an Atavism for the healing properties of Medusa's blood or unicorn's horn, an Atavism for mimicking long prehensile arms, tentacles, or tails to manipulate objects remotely, an Atavism to burrow through earth and rock and survive underground, an Atavism to allow hibernation or cryptobiosis over long periods, an Atavism to see and even reach into Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got the crafting, long arms, burrowing and Twilight Atavisms. They're called Sons of Wayland, Long of Limb, The Maggot God and What Walks Between respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:09:48-07:00","id":871405,"title":"","content":"Cool!<br /> Why Sons of Wayland though? I thought Wayland was a hero?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T10:30:50-07:00","id":871432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=871405#post871405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool!<br /> Why Sons of Wayland though? I thought Wayland was a hero?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure of the exact reasoning of that. You'd have to read the stuff in that post. It's about halfway through, if memory serves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T17:06:02-07:00","id":876121,"title":"","content":"I tried to make an Atavism to simulate the slow, silent, horror movie slasher walk during a chase scene. How does this look to everyone?<br /> <br /> <b>Inescapable [Eshmaki]</b><br /> An Eshmaki on the prowl is always there, breathing down even the fastest victim\u2019s neck. It is the nature of the Beast to not only be stronger or tougher than any mere mortal, but faster too.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> No matter how hard a human tries to run, the monster stalking him will always be just one step behind. Add the Beast's Lair to her speed. If she can't be seen by anyone, multiply the higher of the Beast's Strength or Dexterity by her Lair +1 when calculating her speed. The Beast may make Stealth rolls even when moving at full speed.<br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> By abandoning subtlety in exchange for pure speed, the Beast may become truly inescapable. No matter how fast her victim runs or how well he hides, he cannot escape fear. Multiply the higher of the Beast's Strength or Dexterity by her Lair +1 when calculating her speed, even when she is being observed. The Beast also inflicts a penalty equal to half her Lair, rounded up to the Speed, chase rolls, and Stealth rolls of anyone fleeing or hiding from her.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> When the Beast pushes herself, she can use her incredible speed for not only offense, but defense as well. By spending a dot of Satiety, the Beast may interrupt an attack aimed at her by moving up to her full speed out of reach, making an attack roll, or by taking any other instant action. This does not allow her to attack twice in one turn. Furthermore, the Beast adds half her Lair rounded up to her Defense for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> The increase in speed is calculated the way it is so it doesn't get absolutely ridiculous when stacked with Looming Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:39:31-07:00","id":883214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=876121#post876121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to make an Atavism to simulate the slow, silent, horror movie slasher walk during a chase scene. How does this look to everyone?<br /> <br /> <b>Inescapable [Eshmaki]</b><br /> An Eshmaki on the prowl is always there, breathing down even the fastest victim\u2019s neck. It is the nature of the Beast to not only be stronger or tougher than any mere mortal, but faster too.<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> No matter how hard a human tries to run, the monster stalking him will always be just one step behind. Add the Beast's Lair to her speed. If she can't be seen by anyone, multiply the higher of the Beast's Strength or Dexterity by her Lair +1 when calculating her speed. The Beast may make Stealth rolls even when moving at full speed.<br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> By abandoning subtlety in exchange for pure speed, the Beast may become truly inescapable. No matter how fast her victim runs or how well he hides, he cannot escape fear. Multiply the higher of the Beast's Strength or Dexterity by her Lair +1 when calculating her speed, even when she is being observed. The Beast also inflicts a penalty equal to half her Lair, rounded up to the Speed, chase rolls, and Stealth rolls of anyone fleeing or hiding from her.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> When the Beast pushes herself, she can use her incredible speed for not only offense, but defense as well. By spending a dot of Satiety, the Beast may interrupt an attack aimed at her by moving up to her full speed out of reach, making an attack roll, or by taking any other instant action. This does not allow her to attack twice in one turn. Furthermore, the Beast adds half her Lair rounded up to her Defense for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> The increase in speed is calculated the way it is so it doesn't get absolutely ridiculous when stacked with Looming Presence.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do have a few concerns.<br /> <br /> The first is that the themes behind it - I feel - can be essentially covered by using already existing Nightmares. You can slap on some Lair traits to exacerbate things to the point of what you described. I also feel the slow and methodical approach is better represented by having the Relentless Hunter and Needs Must Atavisms. You also mention Looming Presence, which is more than enough to get you any amount of speed you need unless you're chasing down a Runnerswift Changeling with Fleet of Foot. <br /> <br /> Another problem is that it's a bit clunky when calculating the speed. I know this is to make the Atavism 'less good', but at the very least I would have Low Satiety multiply the entire speed trait by Lair, maybe with a potential drawback, as many Low Satiety Atavisms imply. The horror is hungry and it's not always going to do exactly what you want, as you want it.<br /> <br /> The last problem is the Satiety Expenditure, it's very contrary to the themes of the Atavism. Horror Movie monsters don't vanish mid-swing and end up on the other side of the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T14:59:08-07:00","id":883234,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b>Whispers in the Dark [Namtaru]</b><br /> <u>Action:</u> Reflexive<br /> <u>Dice:</u> N/A<br /> <u>Satiety Effect:</u> By spending a point of satiety, the Beast can read any text regardless of language for the remainder of the scene. The voices the words aloud in her head as she follows the script. As well, the Beast enjoys the Encyclopedic Knowledge merit for the remainder of the scene. The voices aren\u2019t shy about sharing their knowledge, even if it\u2019s something the Beast might rather not know.<br /> <br /> <u>Normal:</u> The Beast is never alone. She has her horror for company, and sometimes it speaks to her. It could be the hundreds of spiders using her skull as a nest. It could be countless voices on a wind that echoes through her and around her. These voices repeat whatever the Beast hears in languages beyond count. She can always understand what an individual is saying, regardless of the speaker\u2019s language. The voices will translate, and one of the languages spoken is bound to be one that she personally understands. This Atavism also adds the Beast\u2019s Lair dots to any rolls used to translate from one language to another, as even if the Beast doesn\u2019t fully understand the other languages, she can capture enough of what is said to carry it over.<br /> <br /> <u>Low Satiety:</u> At low satiety, the Beast isn\u2019t alone in hearing the voices. When she speaks it is with the voices of countless insects, the sharp biting call of the wind echoing words from those dead from exposure. Regardless, listeners can always understand her as long as they speak a language and are not deaf. The Beast gains a bonus to all Intimidation rolls equal to their Lair. The Horror is hungry, and the voices do not perfectly translate what the Beast is saying. Any message communicated is twisted, its meaning altered with a layer of pernicious intent. This will often fill the listener with no small amount of alarm - good, the Horror has to eat, after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:06:23-07:00","id":891256,"title":"","content":"Is it just me that thinks there ought to be some kind of possession Atavism? I mean, how many nightmares are there where you can't control your body?<br /> <br /> Here's a quick outline of my idea:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bodysnatcher (Anakim)</b><br /> Action:</u> Instant<br /> <u>Dice Pool:</u> Resolve + Lair vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance (Low Satiety)<br /> <b>Normal: </b>The Beast can cast his mind into the body of another, leaving his comatose. While inside the other person's body, he can use their senses. He can remain in their body for a number of hours equal to Lair. While occupying the body, he can talk with the body's owner, perhaps posing as a 'conscience' or simply driving him mad with the constant whispers.<br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b> While inside the other person's body, he can roll Resolve + Lair vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance in order to take control of their body for a number of minutes equal to Lair. While the Beast is doing this, the victim cannot act at all, although he can still see through his eyes and use his senses.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>The Beast can choose to apply this to either the Normal effect or the Low Satiety effect (if he has access to it). In the case of the former, the Beast can piggyback in the victim's body indefinitely. If applied to the Low Satiety effect, he can control the victim's actions for a number of hours equal to Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:30:57-07:00","id":891278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=891256#post891256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me that thinks there ought to be some kind of possession Atavism? I mean, how many nightmares are there where you can't control your body?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a function of Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:34:25-07:00","id":891281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=891278#post891278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a function of Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>HM. Ah well, I'll leave Bodysnatcher up here and if someone wants it they can use it. What do you think of it mechanically?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-up