ons":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T08:37:55-07:00","id":1106579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1106562#post1106562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I believe so, though I think you can fine-tune it enough to make someone think it's ambient lighting, if you'd like.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe as a merit, let you do that or channel it through an object?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T09:02:40-07:00","id":1106589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1106579#post1106579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Maybe as a merit, let you do that or channel it through an object?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T11:09:20-07:00","id":1107061,"title":"","content":"As a rule, I'm a fan of Deionscribe's work, but I felt that Untouchable was both too powerful (esp. when combined with the excellent Ancient Horror Merit) and too weak. Too potent, because Lair + Ancient Horror could boost Defense to a degree that brought Heroes down to chance dice, and a successful attack is how Heroes place Anathema. Too weak, because it didn't touch a variety of thematically-appropriate buffs (e.g. dice tricks on Dodge rolls).<br /> <br /> With that said, here's my suggested revision. Feedback is welcome. <br /> <br /> Atavism: Untouchable<br /> The spider that jumps away from your flailing efforts to crush it - you lift your hand and think it's gone, only to find out that <i>now it's on you</i>, ready to bite. The serpent that writhes with lightning speed, twisting away from your boot and sinking fangs into your ankle before you even realize you've missed. The explosive, bunched-muscle leap of the cat or mongoose, twisting away from harm and landing in the perfect new position to counter-pounce. Where some Horrors withstand harm with armored hides and others regenerate from the most grievous wounds, Beasts with this Atavism consider not getting hit at all to be the best defense. Their vampiric and arcane cousins might break the laws of physics with eye-dazzling speed, but the Begotten listen to their Horrors for whispers of threats yet to come; they might not be <i>faster</i> than mortal, per se, but they make up the difference in economy of motion.<br /> <br /> Action: Persistent or Reflexive (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <br /> Normal Effect: The Beast adds half her Lair dots (round up) to her Defense, gains 9-Again on Dodge rolls, and uses the higher of her Wits and Dexterity to calculate his Defense score; the Horror's predatory instincts whisper warnings in the shadows of her mind.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: Hunger sharpens the Horror's predatory instincts, and the Beast finds himself anticipating danger from the smallest of warning signs. He now gains 8-Again on Dodge rolls, suffers no decrease in Defense from multiple attackers, and applies Defense against firearms attacks; he's already moving while fingers are still tightening on triggers and barrels are being brought into line.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: Every brawler and fencer has known what it feels like - that horrible, frozen-moment realization that you've committed to the attack and missed, that you're overextended, that your opponent is going to exploit your vulnerability and that there's nothing you can do. The Beast dodges with pinpoint precision and minimal wasted space, the better to stay close for the vicious counterattack. Alternatively, the preternatural echo of threat through the Primordial Dream can alert the Beast to a danger she might not otherwise have seen (you're <i>certain</i> the spider hasn't seen your hand, patiently inching closer to deliver the crushing blow, but somehow it still manages to leap away at the last second...)<br /> <br /> This effect can be employed in one of two ways each turn:<br /> <br /> If the Beast would otherwise be unaware of an opponent, she may become automatically aware of the attack and Dodge. This Dodge benefits from the rote action quality. If the attacker was concealed only by mortal means (a hidden sniper, a Stealth check, etc.) the Beast is automatically aware of his location; supernatural means of concealment provoke a Clash of Wills. <br /> <br /> If the Beast already knew she was in a fight and had decided to Dodge anyway, Satiety expenditure puts her in position to deliver a brutal riposte. After her opponent resolves his attack, the Beast may lash out with a single counterattack, which is not penalized by the opponent's Defense; he's too committed to the attack at this point to pull away. If the opponent had already sacrificed his Defense - say, for an All-Out Attack - the Beast's counterattack becomes a rote action. (Alternatively, the Beast may immediately establish a grapple and apply a single move from the Grapple list as the opponent's momentum carries him into her arms; in this case, the opponent's over-commitment is represented by the absence of an opposing Strength + Brawl roll.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T17:53:57-07:00","id":1116610,"title":"","content":"Would an Atavism that lets you transform into tools or mold objects into tools be unthematic for Beasts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T04:41:47-07:00","id":1116797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1116610#post1116610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would an Atavism that lets you transform into tools or mold objects into tools be unthematic for Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thematically it suits some depictions of Giants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T09:08:03-07:00","id":1116856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1116797#post1116797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thematically it suits some depictions of Giants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though making anything into a tool to make work go quicker sounds very Fae to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:17:15-07:00","id":1116958,"title":"","content":"Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Lord Of The Corals [Makara]</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast may alter the shape, Durability, Size and function of both inert matter and base organisms. This requires a Dexterity + Crafts extended roll, with each roll requiring one turn. The target must be within touching range. When shaping inert matter, each Success can add or subtract one Durability, Equipment Bonus, Size unit or a Skill which benefits from the Equipment Bonus. The total amount of Successes that can be distributed in one scene is equal to Lair x 3. When shaping base organisms, roll Dexterity + Medicine instead, and treat the base organisms as having all the properties of their mundane counterparts. Complex tools and mechanisms are not possible with this level of Satiety.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Beast can not only transform inert matter and base organisms with greater efficiency and potency, but also transform one into the other. The targets may be from a distance of Lair x 5 yards away, and each Success transforms [Lair + 1] units of Size. Complex tools and mechanisms may now be created and dismantled. Median organisms may be created as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast may now cause inert matter and organisms to shift into each other and lash out violently all around him, creating a deadly zone where the ground erupts in poisonous tentacles and the the enemies\u2019 weapons become swarms of locusts. As an instant action, everything within a Lair x 20 yard radius inflicst a Lair/2 round up penalty to all Physical and Perception rolls for the scene if the Satiety is Normal (full Lair penalty if it\u2019s Low). Everytime a failure is suffered for these rolls within this zone, it is downgraded into a dramatic failure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-18-2017, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:15:56-07:00","id":1118533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1116958#post1116958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Lord Of The Corals [Makara]</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast may alter the shape, Durability, Size and function of both inert matter and base organisms. This requires a Dexterity + Crafts extended roll, with each roll requiring one turn. The target must be within touching range. When shaping inert matter, each Success can add or subtract one Durability, Equipment Bonus, Size unit or a Skill which benefits from the Equipment Bonus. The total amount of Successes that can be distributed in one scene is equal to Lair x 3. When shaping base organisms, roll Dexterity + Medicine instead, and treat the base organisms as having all the properties of their mundane counterparts. Complex tools and mechanisms are not possible with this level of Satiety.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Beast can not only transform inert matter and base organisms with greater efficiency and potency, but also transform one into the other. The targets may be from a distance of Lair x 5 yards away, and each Success transforms [Lair + 1] units of Size. Complex tools and mechanisms may now be created and dismantled. Median organisms may be created as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast may now cause inert matter and organisms to shift into each other and lash out violently all around him, creating a deadly zone where the ground erupts in poisonous tentacles and the the enemies\u2019 weapons become swarms of locusts. As an instant action, everything within a Lair x 20 yard radius inflicst a Lair/2 round up penalty to all Physical and Perception rolls for the scene if the Satiety is Normal (full Lair penalty if it\u2019s Low). Everytime a failure is suffered for these rolls within this zone, it is downgraded into a dramatic failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fluff-wise, I like this alot! However, does the SatExp really destroy the enemies' weapons? cause that seems a tad overpowered, unless you exclude any non-mundane equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:27:50-07:00","id":1118573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1116958#post1116958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feedback is appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Lord Of The Corals [Makara]</b><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast may alter the shape, Durability, Size and function of both inert matter and base organisms. This requires a Dexterity + Crafts extended roll, with each roll requiring one turn. The target must be within touching range. When shaping inert matter, each Success can add or subtract one Durability, Equipment Bonus, Size unit or a Skill which benefits from the Equipment Bonus. The total amount of Successes that can be distributed in one scene is equal to Lair x 3. When shaping base organisms, roll Dexterity + Medicine instead, and treat the base organisms as having all the properties of their mundane counterparts. Complex tools and mechanisms are not possible with this level of Satiety.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Beast can not only transform inert matter and base organisms with greater efficiency and potency, but also transform one into the other. The targets may be from a distance of Lair x 5 yards away, and each Success transforms [Lair + 1] units of Size. Complex tools and mechanisms may now be created and dismantled. Median organisms may be created as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast may now cause inert matter and organisms to shift into each other and lash out violently all around him, creating a deadly zone where the ground erupts in poisonous tentacles and the the enemies\u2019 weapons become swarms of locusts. As an instant action, everything within a Lair x 20 yard radius inflicst a Lair/2 round up penalty to all Physical and Perception rolls for the scene if the Satiety is Normal (full Lair penalty if it\u2019s Low). Everytime a failure is suffered for these rolls within this zone, it is downgraded into a dramatic failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems pretty powerful and not very Beast-themed. Besides the name, what makes this power thematically appropriate for a Makara Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T17:31:53-07:00","id":1119695,"title":"","content":"I wanted to tackle one of the themes that are present in the book, but were not done as an Atavism as far as I know yet, namely the supporting nature Beasts can take. I feel like that could take some additional fleshing out. I thought about making these Merits, but something made me think Nah, Atavisms would be interesting because they would be vastly different from the rest. So, here is an attempt to expand on Mother's Kiss. Please give me feedback on what needs to be changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All Beast's have access to the Mother's Kiss. Some can do more than that, though: they can nurture their Cousins like Grendel's motherdid with her children, emulating the Dark Mother herself. They push them further, egg them on, and those working with them say they are always just at the right spot, doing just the right thing to help them on, making them real teamplayers.<br /> <br /> <b>Setting the Table [Common]</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: Normal Satiety Stamina + Satiety - Supernatural Tolerance; Low Satiety Stamina + Satiety; Satiety Expenditure: Stamina + Lair<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>Rather than needing Family Ties, the Beast can apply Mother's Kiss to any willing Supernatural. Furthermore, when supporting a Supernatural in a team effort, the Begotten knows just where to be, how to move, to make them work perfectly in sync: reduce the threshold for exceptional success to 3. If Family Ties are established with the Beast and both within 15 yards of each other, the Target adds 1/2 Lair rounded up to their Defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Horror is eager, impatient, and instead of helping gently, if forces its power on the target, pushing them to succeed so it may feed faster. Ignore Supernatural Tolerance when applying Mother's Kiss, and trigger its exceptional success at 3 dice. Also, the Beast does not have to pay Willpower to use Mother's Kiss, as the Horror steps in to hurry this up. However, since the Horror is not careful in providing its help, the Target pays a price for the help in suffering 1/2 the rolled results in Bashing Damage as strength surges into them violently. The target needs to be willing to recieve this help.<br /> In addition, when making use of Family Dinner, the Beast heals Lethal damage by the number of Satiety she gains. If she actively participated in the hunt e.g. via the use of Mother's Kiss, she regains 2 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast does not shed blood to support her chosen family, but something much more precious: her Satiety. Every success scored may be allocated by the Target as an Attribute Point for the rest of the Scene. This may take them over their usual limit.<br /> For the Rest of the Scene, team efforts with the Beast in it enjoy a +2 Bonus in addition to the Normal Effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This next one is meant to expand on Family Dinner... but taking it in a different direction<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Riling up the Pack [Common]</b><br /> Some Beasts see their Cousins and Siblings as too meek, feeling they need to stand up and take what is theirs, even if they need to push them for it.<br /> Historically, these Beasts were feared not for their own strength, but for the ferociousness they caused in others. They are walking sparks of chaos, destroying the balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: none for Normal/Low; Presence + Occult + Lair vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>As long as the Beast follows a Supernatural they have no Family Ties with, they gain a +3 Bonus on all actions meant to hide their presence. In addition, if a victim is being hunted in a way that would qualify for Family Dinner within Lair*10 Yards, the Beast is instinctively aware of it, even if she cannot know who hunts whom.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Horror's hunger is palpable. Other supernaturals within 20*Lair Yards feel it, mistaking it for their own. This can lead to confusion if they just ate, and with the right skills they may be able to realize their sensations are being tampered with, but they cannot trace it's source without a supernatural skill, which causes a Clash of Wills. Only a hunt will satisfy this sensation of hunger, posing a problem for those used to more... refined ways of feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Upon spending Satiety, the Beast can deny nourishment: the blood is dead, the plasm dissipates, the Mana corrupted.<br /> The Beast needs to be able to see the Target directly for this to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaand, finally, Primordial Pathways<br /> <br /> <b>No Barriers hold Me [Common]</b><br /> Some Beasts are intrinsically familiar with the bounderies of these worlds, able to enter and leave seemingly as they please. They could disappear there today, and reappear under your bed tomorrow...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: Wits+Composure+Lair; Occult + Lair vs. Supernatural Tolerance; Occult + Lair vs. Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>The Beast may attempt to locate wether there is a supernatural gateway within Lair*5 Yards. Using a Gateway to open to the Primordial Dream does not cost Willpower. Under the Bed can now be used to leave the Primordial Dream at the target's location.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>With the Horror growing hungry, the pathways become easier to access. The Beast can force the Door to simply stay open for [Lair] days. Additionally, it can pull the target of Under the Bed into the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> When the Horror attempts to open a Gateway, it is fuelled by Willpower. When it is fuelled by Satiety, it doesn't just open the Gateway, it tears down the fabric of it or slams it shut so hard it stays stuck. Unless tended to, the Gateway stays that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eh, the latter will be heavily reworked within the week, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 07-23-2017, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T23:28:09-07:00","id":1119785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1119695#post1119695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to tackle one of the themes that are present in the book, but were not done as an Atavism as far as I know yet, namely the supporting nature Beasts can take. I feel like that could take some additional fleshing out. I thought about making these Merits, but something made me think Nah, Atavisms would be interesting because they would be vastly different from the rest. So, here is an attempt to expand on Mother's Kiss. Please give me feedback on what needs to be changed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All Beast's have access to the Mother's Kiss. Some can do more than that, though: they can nurture their Cousins like Grendel's motherdid with her children, emulating the Dark Mother herself. They push them further, egg them on, and those working with them say they are always just at the right spot, doing just the right thing to help them on, making them real teamplayers.<br /> <br /> <b>Setting the Table [Common]</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: Normal Satiety Stamina + Satiety - Supernatural Tolerance; Low Satiety Stamina + Satiety; Satiety Expenditure: Stamina + Lair<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>Rather than needing Family Ties, the Beast can apply Mother's Kiss to any willing Supernatural. Furthermore, when supporting a Supernatural in a team effort, the Begotten knows just where to be, how to move, to make them work perfectly in sync: reduce the threshold for exceptional success to 3. If Family Ties are established with the Beast and both within 15 yards of each other, the Target adds 1/2 Lair rounded up to their Defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Horror is eager, impatient, and instead of helping gently, if forces its power on the target, pushing them to succeed so it may feed faster. Ignore Supernatural Tolerance when applying Mother's Kiss, and trigger its exceptional success at 3 dice. Also, the Beast does not have to pay Willpower to use Mother's Kiss, as the Horror steps in to hurry this up. However, since the Horror is not careful in providing its help, the Target pays a price for the help in suffering 1/2 the rolled results in Bashing Damage as strength surges into them violently. The target needs to be willing to recieve this help.<br /> In addition, when making use of Family Dinner, the Beast heals Lethal damage by the number of Satiety she gains. If she actively participated in the hunt e.g. via the use of Mother's Kiss, she regains 2 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast does not shed blood to support her chosen family, but something much more precious: her Satiety. Every success scored may be allocated by the Target as an Attribute Point for the rest of the Scene. This may take them over their usual limit.<br /> For the Rest of the Scene, team efforts with the Beast in it enjoy a +2 Bonus in addition to the Normal Effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This next one is meant to expand on Family Dinner... but taking it in a different direction<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Riling up the Pack [Common]</b><br /> Some Beasts see their Cousins and Siblings as too meek, feeling they need to stand up and take what is theirs, even if they need to push them for it.<br /> Historically, these Beasts were feared not for their own strength, but for the ferociousness they caused in others. They are walking sparks of chaos, destroying the balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: none for Normal/Low; Presence + Occult + Lair vs. Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>As long as the Beast follows a Supernatural they have no Family Ties with, they gain a +3 Bonus on all actions meant to hide their presence. In addition, if a victim is being hunted in a way that would qualify for Family Dinner within Lair*10 Yards, the Beast is instinctively aware of it, even if she cannot know who hunts whom.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The Horror's hunger is palpable. Other supernaturals within 20*Lair Yards feel it, mistaking it for their own. This can lead to confusion if they just ate, and with the right skills they may be able to realize their sensations are being tampered with, but they cannot trace it's source without a supernatural skill, which causes a Clash of Wills. Only a hunt will satisfy this sensation of hunger, posing a problem for those used to more... refined ways of feeding.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Upon spending Satiety, the Beast can deny nourishment: the blood is dead, the plasm dissipates, the Mana corrupted.<br /> The Beast needs to be able to see the Target directly for this to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaand, finally, Primordial Pathways<br /> <br /> <b>No Barriers hold Me [Common]</b><br /> Some Beasts are intrinsically familiar with the bounderies of these worlds, able to enter and leave seemingly as they please. They could disappear there today, and reappear under your bed tomorrow...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Roll</b>: Wits+Composure+Lair; Occult + Lair vs. Supernatural Tolerance; Occult + Lair vs. Supernatural Tolerance<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>The Beast may attempt to locate wether there is a supernatural gateway within Lair*5 Yards. Using a Gateway to open to the Primordial Dream does not cost Willpower. Under the Bed can now be used to leave the Primordial Dream at the target's location.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>With the Horror growing hungry, the pathways become easier to access. The Beast can force the Door to simply stay open for [Lair] days. Additionally, it can pull the target of Under the Bed into the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> When the Horror attempts to open a Gateway, it is fuelled by Willpower. When it is fuelled by Satiety, it doesn't just open the Gateway, it tears down the fabric of it or slams it shut so hard it stays stuck. Unless tended to, the Gateway stays that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> Eh, the latter will be heavily reworked within the week, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to say it, but that's not what Atavisms are. Atavisms are the manifestations of mythic attributes of a Horror, not something that develops the abilities which arise from a Beast's nature as a being of both Dream and physicality.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that some of those couldn't be re-worked into something more fitting, but as they are now, they're jarring at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T23:29:25-07:00","id":1119786,"title":"","content":"I'm on my phone at the moment, but I'll post some more specific thoughts when I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T01:43:02-07:00","id":1119804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1119695#post1119695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... [An Amazing Assortment of Things]</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, I'm kind of with ajf115 on the statement that they aren't really something I'd see as an Atavism. On the other, I really like the idea of expanded natural Beast traits. I'd love to see little expansions of this on all beast's innate powers, particularly Family Resemblance and Passing Resemblance. However, because an Atavism is an expression of what a Beast's Horror is, these may be better as Merits than as Atavisms or Nightmares.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T02:32:00-07:00","id":1119810,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the Feedback <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a>!<br /> I suppose you're right. Fell into the trap of wanting to do something different for the sake of being different, I guess. Totally ignored the Horror-Atavism relationship.<br /> Might as well try to turn this into an array of Merits. Maybe I'll just add in another Effect for High Satiety, then, too. 4-Dot-Merit each sounds about right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1513\" data-vbnamecard=\"1513\">Jakondite</a> Same here! That's why I tried this. I also want to see Family Ties gain influence. Suppose I should stick with Merits with this kinda stuff, for now, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T09:30:38-07:00","id":1135812,"title":"","content":"I read through this thread again and think we are missing something here. The point is we are using real world logic to design atavisms, however many Beast atavisms are working on dream logic (like cyclopean strength depending on the size of target - not weight). I think we should try to use dream logic here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T16:42:17-07:00","id":1136750,"title":"","content":"Collaboration with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a><br /> <br /> <b>Thousand Eyes</b><br /> Most monsters have eyes. A certain few, however, have a lot of eyes, placed all over their body, like Argus Panoptes, the greek giant. Others have fewer, but special eyes. They all have one thing in common: they See.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> You can see in all directions at once, and are immune to being blinded.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> Your vision cannot be impeded by physical objects. Effectively, you can spend an instant action to see selectively through materials in the way.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>Pluck an eyeball from your body, and place it somewhere. You may spend satiety, and see remotely through that eye for a scene. The eyeball will last 1 week or until used before drying up. You can place up to [1+Lair] eyeballs like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Manyskin</b><br /> Some Monsters do not come directly at you. They send mundane animals first. You get the feeling that the birds are watching you, that they follow you - and you are right. For they do the Monster's bidding. And they will soon descend on you.This is done by Horrors that prefer indirect action, e.g. the living tree gathering the whispers, the crones in the forest collecting secrets to assert their dominance over the people by striking unexpectedly where it hurts the most, or the leshy that coldly watches on as wolves tear you apart for defiling his territory.<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: Pres+Lair vs Resolve + ST<br /> Dram Fail: The animal becomes immediately hostile to you and attacks or flees if it can.<br /> Fail: The action fails.<br /> Success: Activates as below.<br /> Exceptional Success: The animal gains the Bonded Condition<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>Take control of target animal you can see. You can move the animal, and see from it's senses. Your body however, is motionless while you focus on the creature, and you are unaware of what happens around you. The animal will not perform tasks it percieves as dangerous. You may end this effect at any time. You can control animals of up to Lair+1 Size with this atavism, or a number of animals who's total size equals Lair+1.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>The hungry horror doesn't ask animals, it tells. Your horror may force an animal to perform any action, dangerous or not. You are also more aware of your own body during this, though still unable to move without ending the connection.<br /> <br /> <b>Sat Expenditure</b>: Your size limit doubles for one scene. The animal(s) may be used as the origin point for your Lair traits. If controlling a single animal, it gains access to 1 nightmare of your choosing. The Beast is able to move without ending the connection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 02-10-2018, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-02T18:01:27-07:00","id":1136774,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Who the hell covers themselves in eyeballs, you've only made yourself more vulnerable!&quot;</i> - Yu Yu Hakusho Abridged.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Might need help thinking up a dice pool for this one...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hibernation</b><br /> <br /> Some monsters are known for their hibernation cycles, emerging periodically to feast upon humanity before vanishing again for years at a time. These restful periods allow them to conserve their energy and drop off the radar of many Heroes who would see them destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast can enter a deep slumber in order to conserve resources and mask its trail. As long as they remain asleep in this fashion, their length of time between satiety depletion is doubled its usual rate. In addition, the Beast's does not impose a subconscious effect on the Primordial Dream, effectively masking them from the instinctive awareness of Heroes.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> Desperate to conserve as much energy as possible, the Beast shuts down all non essential bodily functions. The length of time between satiety depletion is now multiplied by their dots in Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a point of satiety, the Beast can project their sense of sight and sound outside of their body in order to observe the physical world while they sleep. Such an ability has been instrumental for many such Beasts, who wish to keep themselves updated on what is happening in the world while their bodies rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T08:33:58-07:00","id":1144428,"title":"","content":"<b>Heart of the Land (Makara):</b><br /> <br /> Like the ancient precursors of the ancient dinosaurs, some leviathans crawled out of their watery homes and adapted to survive on dry land. There, they discovered a new kind of depth in which to call home, the depths of the wild!<br /> <br /> Mechanically speaking, Heart of the Land is a remodeled version of Heart of the Ocean. Instead of water, the Beast is able to travel through soil at double their usual speed, rapidly burrowing through the earth as though it were water. Like many subterranean creatures, the Beast always seems to have a fresh pocket of air while underground, ensuring that they do not suffocate from being buried alive. Their burrowing also deposits loose soil, which quickly fills in the tunnels behind them and hides the evidence of their activities from prying investigators.<br /> <br /> When experiencing the effects of low Satiety, the Beast enters a state of communion with the land itself. This communion is born of instinct, rather than spiritualism, but the effects are the same as those for Heart of the Ocean. The Beast gains a preternatural awareness of nearby prey, being able to sense their location and movements through subtle messages in the environment. This awareness does not rely purely on the sense of sight and, as such, it is not fooled by tricks that might evade the naked eye. However, this awareness is not omniscient; the Beast doesn't know the location of everybody in the area. Rather, their awareness is laser focused on those who would make obvious targets for feeding their Satiety.<br /> <br /> Instead of watery brine corroding the environment, spending a point of satiety causes the environment to succumb to the ravages of nature. Patches of dirt seem to manifest out of nowhere and quickly give way to creeping plant life as vines and mosses spread across the area. Like a blade of grass breaking through concrete, the plants and soil gradually break down the surrounding area, the effects of which continue to persist even after the Beast leaves the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-27-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T13:27:38-07:00","id":1144526,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> Interesting take, and certainly an easy way to modify to accommodate tunneling movement. I know <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> had a version of this on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818688#post818688\">Page 7</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas/page12#post913203\"> Page 12</a>.<br /> <br /> It intrigues me to see that tunneling through the ground Graboid style has made three different appearances. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T14:43:36-07:00","id":1144539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1144526#post1144526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Interesting take, and certainly an easy way to modify to accommodate tunneling movement. I know <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> had a version of this on <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=818688#post818688&amp;quot;]Page</a> 7[/url] and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> on <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas/page12#post913203&amp;quot;]</a> Page 12[/url].<br /> <br /> It intrigues me to see that tunneling through the ground Graboid style has made three different appearances. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a popular concept. Besides, Tremors was awesome. And then there's Dune to factor in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T08:30:23-07:00","id":1144786,"title":"","content":"My group and I came up with this for my Anakim, because I wanted my Horror to drag around his large weapon like Pyramid Head in the Silent Hill.<br /> So my character has a large axe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Horrific Weapon</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Normal</b><br /> Action: Reflexive. <br /> The Beast summons his Horror's weapon to his hand in an instant. Once summoned, the weapon is visible to all and becomes a real object- it can be dropped or stolen, for instance. The weapon cannot be &quot;resummoned&quot; for a scene even if destroyed or lost. <br /> The weapon's damage modifier is equal to the Beast's Lair dots and its Initiative penalty equals the Beast's (Satiety -2), minimum 1 (but see below). <br /> When this Atavism is selected, choose a weapon type (for instance, Large Axe; dagger). When wielding a non-supernatural version of that weapon type, subtract your Lair dots from your opponent's Defense. <br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety</b><br /> The true nature of the Horror's weapon now shines through even more. When this Atavism is chosen, choose either 9-Again or Armor Piercing. The summoned weapon gains this quality. <br /> When wielding a non-supernatural version of his weapon, the Beast cannot be disarmed and may use his weapon even in a grapple. <br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b><br /> Action: Reflexive. <br /> On Satiety expenditure, the Beast's summoned weapon deals Aggravated damage when used to attack this turn. He also ignores the initiative penalty. <br /> When using a Fighting Style with a non-supernatural weapon of your type, your weapon damage type does not change but if the style would cause you to lose your Defense, you do not. If the style would instead cause a dice penalty, ignore that penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Did you miss me?</b><br /> I'm back! Long hiatus from the forums. Hope I didn't miss much.<br /> Here's where I've been keeping my stuff.<br /> <a href=\"http://evosworkshop.wikidot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://evosworkshop.wikidot.com/</a><br /> I made &quot;Demon the Return&quot; and &quot;Psychic the Gifted&quot; is in progress.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17413-evo_shandor","name":"Evo_Shandor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T13:59:45-07:00","id":1144929,"title":"","content":"I like it. But why would you ever want to carry another weapon if you could just call one to hand for no cost? Maybe make calling it to hand a Satiety Expenditure effect and rejigger the rest of the effects around that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And if I understand damage rating right, that means you get [Lair] automatic damage on a successful hit, right? I dunno, sounds kinda OP.<br /> <br /> Also, do you think we should ask for this thread to be pinned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:23:07-07:00","id":1144950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1144929#post1144929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. But why would you ever want to carry another weapon if you could just call one to hand for no cost? Maybe make calling it to hand a Satiety Expenditure effect and rejigger the rest of the effects around that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And if I understand damage rating right, that means you get [Lair] automatic damage on a successful hit, right? I dunno, sounds kinda OP.<br /> <br /> Also, do you think we should ask for this thread to be pinned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Modifiers are usually just things weapons do. This is not even too much of an outlier in strenght: Limb from Limb turns your unarmed +0B into +Lair Lethal at low Satiety, or +Lair Agg on spending satiety. That means a hit deals damage equal to the weapon modifier + successes. No successes, no hit, no damage. Automatic successes are something else.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17413-evo_shandor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar17413_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17413\" data-vbnamecard=\"17413\">Evo_Shandor</a> Gotta admit, this feels more like it should be a combination of a fighting style and a Merit like Nightmare Armory rather than an Atavism.<br /> As I did wrong at least once here, too, Atavisms are supposed to reflect your Horror's nature. So unless it is somehow integral to your Horror that he can summon weapons to his side, you could achieve similar effects with using the aforementioned combination.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T14:56:59-07:00","id":1144974,"title":"","content":"I'm not familiar with Nightmare Armory. No books near me now. Where would I find it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Did you miss me?</b><br /> I'm back! Long hiatus from the forums. Hope I didn't miss much.<br /> Here's where I've been keeping my stuff.<br /> <a href=\"http://evosworkshop.wikidot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://evosworkshop.wikidot.com/</a><br /> I made &quot;Demon the Return&quot; and &quot;Psychic the Gifted&quot; is in progress.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17413-evo_shandor","name":"Evo_Shandor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:01:02-07:00","id":1144976,"title":"","content":"I agree that an atavism probably wasn't the best choice, but it was what we settled on in order to give my horror an axe. We created it our first time playing Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Did you miss me?</b><br /> I'm back! Long hiatus from the forums. Hope I didn't miss much.<br /> Here's where I've been keeping my stuff.<br /> <a href=\"http://evosworkshop.wikidot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://evosworkshop.wikidot.com/</a><br /> I made &quot;Demon the Return&quot; and &quot;Psychic the Gifted&quot; is in progress.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17413-evo_shandor","name":"Evo_Shandor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T15:15:58-07:00","id":1144985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evo_Shandor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1144976#post1144976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that an atavism probably wasn't the best choice, but it was what we settled on in order to give my horror an axe. We created it our first time playing Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>totally fine, and hey, as long as it worked for your table and you guys had a great time, don't sweat the details, right?!<br /> <br /> just a general observation. Which DID help in me working on a style, though. A style based on swinging around immense, huge weaponry akin to Cloud's Bustersword or pyramid head's ... whatever that was he pulled at times.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: regarding nightmare armory, my bad, that is from our game's homebrew, so obviously you wouldn't have access to that. But generally, making &quot;pulling weapons out of my hat&quot; a merit is pretty simple. Just do a basic template regarding str requirements and weapon modifier, and make additional ranking in the merit increase the modifier/durability.<br /> Pretty mean trick with throwing knives and corresponding styles, come to think of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 09-28-2017, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T17:14:45-07:00","id":1145018,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> I wasn't saying automatic successes. I understand that the damage only happens if the hit connects. I just thought that doing at least [Lair]+1 Bashing, Lethal or even Aggravated damage in one hit with no point expenditure seemed OP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T00:34:18-07:00","id":1145120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1145018#post1145018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I wasn't saying automatic successes. I understand that the damage only happens if the hit connects. I just thought that doing at least [Lair]+1 Bashing, Lethal or even Aggravated damage in one hit with no point expenditure seemed OP</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, misunderstood that. Well, it is slightly stronger than limb from limb as written (thanks to stuff like 9 - again/armorpiercing AND dealing lethal at normal satiety) but other than that seems fair. + remember, weapon modifiers are easily at 2 or 3. So before hitting Lair 4, this wont be stronger than common weapons one could buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T10:09:58-07:00","id":1154755,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Feather-Light Tread (Eshmaki)</b></u><br /> Not all monsters are lumbering behemoths or dragons that leave devastation in their wake. Some are so subtle, so light-footed, that none - barring perhaps the greatest of Heroes - can tell that they were ever there. These are the monsters that tip-toe into your life, change it forever and then leave once more with you never having known they were there.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> Your effect upon the world is light: wherever you would leave a physical trace, whether a footprint, DNA or any other such marker. Any attempt to notice, identify or otherwise draw information from these traces suffers a penalty equal to your Lair, although supernatural methods such as a Mage's Mage Sight or a Hero's Heroic Tracking are not affected and equipment such as security cameras can still record you as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety Effect:</b> As the Horror becomes ever more famished, its touch upon the world grows ever-lighter. You no longer leave any mundane traces to be found and any attempt to track you magically (including Heroic Tracking) results in a Clash of Wills. Furthermore, you may stand on any solid thing without causing an effect, from a power line to the topmost twigs of a tree and gain half your Lair, rounded up, as a bonus to climbing rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> With the expenditure of a point of Satiety you can not only leave few traces but actually erase them from the minds of your pursuers. Any individuals actively tracking you or seeking information on you must roll Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance versus your Manipulation + Lair or immediately lose track of you somehow - they mistake another set of tracks for yours and only realize their blunder an hour later, they press the delete button by accident and lose crucial evidence or some other mishap occurs. This cannot be used while your pursuers are within line of sight of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 11-01-2017, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T07:01:59-08:00","id":1164519,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Skinwalker (Eshmaki) </b></u><br /> Sometimes the monster is not lurking beneath your bed or in a fancy castle filled with stolen gold. Sometimes it is right beside you, wearing a normal facade and you would never know any better until it is too late.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None for Normal Satiety and Low Satiety, Manipulation + Subterfuge - Composure for Satiety Expenditure<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> You can alter your form into that of anyone you have seen directly within the past [Lair] days as an instant action. You gain a bonus to Social and Perception rolls equal to your Lair for impersonating others this way. Lastly, you gain the Untouchable and Closed Book Merits, the latter with a rating equal to Lair/2 round up. These Merits are for free and ignore prerequisites.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> You may shapeshift into anyone you have seen within the last [Lair] weeks reflexively. You gain the Rote Quality on all Social and Perception rolls for impersonating others, and any supernatural attempt at piercing your disguise or detecting your lies provokes a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Roll the aforementioned dice pool. On a Success, you gain a Perfect Impression for Social Maneuvering using your stolen identity and all of its memories, going back [10 - Current Satiety] in days. On an Exceptional Success, memories go back [10 - Current Satiety] in weeks, any Failure suffered when trying to investigate you is downgraded to a Dramatic Failure and Exceptional Successes cannot be achieved (this includes supernatural attempts if Low Satiety). These effects last for one scene, but may be extended for subsequent scenes with further Satiety Expenditure. You lose the memories even if you have Eidetic Memory/Mimir's Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-02-2017, 10:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T09:01:44-08:00","id":1164546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1164519#post1164519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Roll the aforementioned dice pool. On a Success, you gain a Perfect Impression for Social Maneuvering using your stolen identity and all of its memories, going back [10 - Current Satiety] in days. On an Exceptional Success, memories go back [10 - Current Satiety] in weeks, any Failure suffered when trying to investigate you is downgraded to a Dramatic Failure and Exceptional Successes cannot be achieved (this includes supernatural attempts if Low Satiety). These effects last for one scene, but may be extended for subsequent scenes with further Satiety Expenditure. You lose the memories even if you have Eidetic Memory/Mimir's Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>I presume if you're after information you can write it down while you still have the memories, though. Do you remember remembering them, or only the act of remembering them, if you see what i mean.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T11:43:03-08:00","id":1180824,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Unstoppable (Anakim)</b></u><br /> The Beast is a freight train, a charging boar and a landslide all in one. To attempt to turn him from his path, stall or slow him is futile. Better just to run, and hope that it's not faster than you.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal</b>: The Beast is a force of immense momentum, adding +1 to its Speed each turn it continues to move, up to a maximum of +(Lair). This bonus lasts until the Beast stops moving, or changes direction drastically. Furthermore, if the Beast is subjected to any Tilt or Condition which would impede its movement (Undergrowth, Flooded, Leg Wrack etc), it ignores those effects that directly impact its movement or Speed. Other effects are not ignored (e.g. if a Beast with this Atavism is subjected to the Flooded Tilt by chest-high water, he can still move at his normal speed and suffers no penalties on Physical rolls to move, but finds it as difficult as any other to swing a sword). If such a Condition is directly imposed by magic, roll a Clash of Wills. A Beast with this Atavism can walk perfectly fine with one leg and if legless can crawl faster than most can walk.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety</b>: The Beast's Hunger drives him onwards, sublimating lesser needs into its singular purpose. While at Low Satiety, a Beast with this Atavism treats journeying as food, drink and rest for the purposes of exhaustion, thirst and starvation. An Unstoppable Beast can walk tirelessly across the Sahara so long as he keeps going. This effect only applies if the Beast himself is doing the locomotion, so riding in a car, on a train or an aeroplane does not count. Furthermore, the Beast's hunger spurs them on, increasing the bonus to speed to +2 per turn up to a limit of (2*Lair)<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: No barrier can halt the Beast's advance, no illusion shake his relentless pursuit. Whenever the Beast is directly pursuing another - meaning chasing or tracking them, not investigating to try and identify a culprit or similar - he may expend a point of Satiety. This grants him a pool of dice equal to (Lair/2) rounded up which are added to any dice pool used in his pursuit, including Clashes of Wills against supernatural efforts by his quarry to stall his pursuit. These dice can only be added to dice pools which directly impact the pursuit. For example, they could be added to a roll to open a Primordial Pathway to follow a werewolf into the Shadow or to resist debilitating magic, but not to open that same Pathway if the quarry has not entered the Shadow or to resist a mage's lightning bolt - although injury may result in the abandonment of the pursuit, the magic does not directly impact this. The Storyteller is the final arbiter of which dice pools are and are not valid for use of these dice. If the quarry escapes the Scene or the Beast gives up, is rendered unconscious or Feeds or the Scene ends, the effect ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T02:56:33-08:00","id":1193028,"title":"","content":"My first Atavism for one of the new Families, this one was inspired by the Balrog and by R.R.Martin's Others' weapons and armour of ice. I'm not sure about the mechanics of the thing, so any comments on those would be welcome. I'm also not sure whether this should be Inguma, but *shrugs*. What else should it be?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Inhuman Panoply (Inguma)</b></u><br /> Humans like to think that they know all there is to know about making things. After all, they took tin and copper and invented bronze, took wood and shaped it into bows and ships. But there are older things, things which know the ways of making strange substances and eldritch implements.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended, Reflexive<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Intelligence + Crafts (Interval 1 hour, Terminus (Lair)), Lair + Resolve vs Durability (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> The Beast can shape objects out of phenomena related to one of his Lair Traits \u2013 ice for Extreme Cold, for example, fire for Burning or plant life for Undergrowth. The Trait in question is chosen when this Atavism is selected, and may not be changed save at the Storyteller's discretion. The Beast is immune to all damage and negative effects from that phenomenon and can use Intelligence + Crafts to shape it without tools into an equivalent of any mundane object of a Resources value equal to or lesser than (1/2*Lair), rounded up. These objects have Durability equal to (1/2*Lair), Structure equal to (Lair) and function as a normal example of their kind except as noted below. This can lead to truly strange items such as a 'laptop' which appears to be a strange bud or bulb and which opens when activated, displaying its 'screen' on a colour-changing petal.<br /> <br /> Such objects are obviously supernatural and provoke a Breaking Point the first time they are perceived by a mortal in a scene. Furthermore, the alien nature of their structure degrades outside of the Lair, suffering one point of Structure damage ignoring Durability per day outside the Lair or per hour in the phenomenal world. If used by a person who is not the crafter, a member of their Brood or of their Cult (if they have one), the object takes 3 points of Structure Damage each round, ignoring Durability.<br /> <br /> A Beast can maintain a number of such objects equal to their (Resolve) outside the Lair. Within the Lair, an unlimited number of such objects may be Maintained. Taking an object out of the Lair permanently adds it to a Beasts 'maintained' objects and it remains as such even if returned to the Lair. If a Beast who currently has maintained objects equal to their Resolve attempts to make another outside of the Lair or draws another out of the Lair the oldest maintained object breaks and degrades into an example of its natural stuff \u2013 swords of light vanish in a flash, ice cracks and shatters and fire flares briefly then winks out. The same happens if an object's Structure is depleted.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> With the Beast's growing hunger, its malice and power leaks into its creations. The equipment bonus from the objects' nature increases by (\u00bd*Lair), rounded up. Furthermore, the Beast can use an Instant action to summon one of their creations to their hand from somewhere within their direct line of sight or may spend a point of Willpower to summon an object to their hand from their Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Whenever one of the Beast wields one of its creations in a direct contest against a mundane object \u2013 blocking a weapon with your a shield of hardened ice \u2013 the Beast may spend a point of Satiety to roll Lair + Resolve. If the Beast rolls more successes than the object's Durability, the mundane object takes Structure damage equal to the Beast's Lair in a manner appropriate to the object being used \u2013 the shield might freeze-shatter a metal sword used against it \u2013 and reduces its Durability by (\u00bd*Lair), rounded down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-11-2018, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:40:06-08:00","id":1193112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evo_Shandor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1144974#post1144974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not familiar with Nightmare Armory. No books near me now. Where would I find it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast corebook page 236. It is a Numina associated with the Unfettered but I'd say Legendary Horrors may also take it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:45:01-08:00","id":1193116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193112#post1193112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast corebook page 236. It is a Numina associated with the Unfettered but I'd say Legendary Horrors may also take it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:11:42-08:00","id":1193434,"title":"","content":"Are we going to talk about how many things in the new book are extremely similar to what was floated around on these threads? Ravenous Maw being the example that springs to my mind straight away because with the new book out I just switched my ongoing characters All Consuming Atavism for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T22:53:46-08:00","id":1193448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193434#post1193434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we going to talk about how many things in the new book are extremely similar to what was floated around on these threads? Ravenous Maw being the example that springs to my mind straight away because with the new book out I just switched my ongoing characters All Consuming Atavism for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was adressed in the BPG threads. Personally, I think it is awesome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T23:34:14-08:00","id":1193451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strictura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193434#post1193434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we going to talk about how many things in the new book are extremely similar to what was floated around on these threads? Ravenous Maw being the example that springs to my mind straight away because with the new book out I just switched my ongoing characters All Consuming Atavism for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was either a case of 'great minds think alike' (because although fools rarely differ I cannot accept that that <i>glorious</i> book was written by fools) or ideas from here percolating through to the staff. Either is awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-10-2018, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T06:35:00-08:00","id":1193520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193448#post1193448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was adressed in the BPG threads. Personally, I think it is awesome</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. This has helped clear up a lot of the confusion we were experiencing at the table with Beast. And through the flow of our current story I am in a position where I have set my character up for several of the cool new Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T05:32:14-08:00","id":1193887,"title":"","content":"So, in light of the new Families, are there any homebrew Atavisms around here that should be re-categorised?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T08:58:57-08:00","id":1193936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193887#post1193887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in light of the new Families, are there any homebrew Atavisms around here that should be re-categorised?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some time ago, I posted an Atavism called Long of Limb; at the time I keyed it to the Eshmaki, envisioning an appendage reaching out of the shadows and pulling someone into the darkness, but I think it might be more thematic for the Talasii.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's another Atavism that's been brewing in my mind for quite some time:<br /> <br /> <b>Swamp Hag Cunning (Namtaru)</b><br /> <br /> Some Beasts are connected to the fears of witches, sorcerers, diabolists, and others who truck with forces beyond mortal ken, their Horrors providing them with a nightmarish version of such magics. Theirs, however, are not the enchantments of a kindly fairy or the revelation of higher truths, no. A Beast's magic is an ugly thing, petty, spiteful, cruel. If you come to her thatched hut lost in the foul swamp and debase yourself properly, the Hag may even share some of her power with you. For a cost, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Persistent (Normal) or Instant (Low, Expend.)<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult (Low); Presence + Occult + Lair vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance (Expend.)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Horror provides the Beast with secret knowledge to hurt others in tricky ways beyond mere brute force. Add one-half the Beast's Lair dots, rounded up, to rolls to create poisons, traps, or occult charms (such as an amulet to ward off a ghost or a cursed ring that penalizes one type of Skill). Traps created with the use of this Atavism tend to be &quot;witchy&quot; in nature: A tripwire might take the form of a line of rune-gashed stones that emits a ghostly scream if broken, etc. Furthermore, the Beast's knowledge of poisonous herbs and venomous creatures gives her an immunity to the Poison Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast can find wisdom in hunger, but it may not be what anyone would ever want to find. When Starving, the Beast can perform a type of extispicy; she slices open a serpent to read its entrails, cuts the head off a chicken and observes its haphazard death-march, or performs other gruesome acts of blood and viscera. This requires killing a small animal, or at least disemboweling a larger one (around, say size 5); in this latter case, the victim might survive if immediate medical attention or supernatural healing is administered. Some Beasts have special ritual spaces prepared for their dark divinations, complete with cruel-looking athame and blood-stained grimoires, while others prefer to strike with their Atavisms and let the instincts of the Dark Mother wash over them. Either way, roll Wits + Occult.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Beast receives a chilling vision of her own doom. She gains the Shaken Condition; until it is resolved, she cannot access any of this Atavism's effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Beast receives no answers, having only a dead animal for her troubles.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Beast finds the answer to a question she seeks. Either the Storyteller can give the player a glimpse of the most likely outcome of a certain event, or show her the best way to accomplish a certain goal. Add the Beast's Lair to rolls related to the vision. If the Beast reads the entrails of a human, she may also ask a question about anyone related to her victim (such as a family member, loved one, stalker, or the last Beast to feed from him).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Beast gains the Steadfast Condition. It can only be resolved in the context of her vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes a foul curse on the unfortunate target of her vengeance. This requires having some piece of the victim, such as a lock of hair, vial of blood, or photograph. While heaping invections upon the target, the Beast destroys the sympathetic object (ripping up the photo, burning the hair, drinking the blood, etc.), and rolls Presence + Occult + Lair, contested by the victim's Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. Each net success on the Beast's part allows her to place any Personal Tilt of her choosing on her victim. Tilts that come in multiple levels of severity always inflict the least potent of their type, but additional successes can be allocated to increase their level (eg, one success can cause the Moderate Sick Tilt, while two successes create the Grave version).<br /> <br /> The Beast can target someone with this effect from any distance so long as they are both on the same plane of existence, <i>or</i>, if the Beast is within her Lair, while the target is in the physical location corresponding to one of her Chambers.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> And here's a related Nightmare while I'm at it:<br /> <br /> <b>Witch's Brew</b><br /> <br /> <i>Everyone knows this: Don't take candy from strangers. Don't leave your drink unattended. Don't accept that apple pie from your kindly neighbor. They could have put anything in it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>To use this Nightmare, the Beast must create or tamper with a beverage of some sort. This could take the form of brewing a foul-smelling liquid in a cauldron, mixing up a mojito, or merely stirring a packet of sugar into someone's coffee. The Beast takes a -2 penalty to the next roll she makes to activate a Nightmare; in return, the next person who imbibes the tampered beverage suffers its effects.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast can imbue a Nightmare into a number of drinks equal to her Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast makes the drink especially tempting. This is the best cup of coffee her victim's ever smelled, or the Hero is convinced that this is a magical potion that will increase his might tenfold. The Beast can choose whether this effect applies to anyone, a single person of her designation, or other specified group in-between. A person who fits the criteria and who comes across the Nightmare-infused beverage must make a Resolve + Composure roll or immediately drink the beverage, downing it in one gulp if possible. Offering the drink to someone who fits the criteria always counts as Soft Leverage.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> As per the invoked Nightmare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 03-14-2018, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T09:42:04-08:00","id":1193947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193936#post1193936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some time ago, I posted an Atavism called Long of Limb; at the time I keyed it to the Eshmaki, envisioning an appendage reaching out of the shadows and pulling someone into the darkness, but I think it might be more thematic for the Talasii.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here's another Atavism that's been brewing in my mind for quite some time:<br /> <br /> <b>Swamp Hag Cunning (Namtaru)</b><br /> <br /> Some Beasts are connected to the fears of witches, sorcerers, diabolists, and others who truck with forces beyond mortal ken, their Horrors providing them with a nightmarish version of such magics. Theirs, however, are not the enchantments of a kindly fairy or the revelation of higher truths, no. A Beast's magic is an ugly thing, petty, spiteful, cruel. If you come to her thatched hut lost in the foul swamp and debase yourself properly, the Hag may even share some of her power with you. For a cost, of course.<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Persistent (Normal) or Instant (Low, Expend.)<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Occult (Low); Presence + Occult vs Composure + Supernatural Tolerance (Expend.)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Horror provides the Beast with secret knowledge to hurt others in tricky ways beyond mere brute force. Add the Beast's Lair dots to rolls to create poisons, traps, or occult charms (such as an amulet to ward off a ghost or a cursed ring that penalizes one type of Skill). Furthermore, the Beast's knowledge of poisonous herbs and venomous creatures gives her an immunity to the Poison Tilt.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast can find wisdom in hunger, but it may not be what anyone would ever want to find. When Starving, the Beast can perform a type of extispicy; she slices open a serpent to read its entrails, cuts the head off a chicken and observes its haphazard death-march, or performs other gruesome acts of blood and viscera. This requires killing a small animal, or at least disemboweling a larger one (around, say size 5); in this latter case, the victim might survive if immediate medical attention or supernatural healing is administered. Some Beasts have special ritual spaces prepared for their dark divinations, complete with cruel-looking athame and blood-stained grimoires, while others prefer to strike with their Atavisms and let the instincts of the Dark Mother wash over them. Either way, roll Wits + Occult.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Beast receives a chilling vision of her own doom. She gains the Shaken Condition; until it is resolved, she cannot access any of this Atavism's effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The Beast receives no answers, having only a dead animal for her troubles.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The Beast finds the answer to a question she seeks. Either the Storyteller can give the player a glimpse of the most likely outcome of a certain event, or show her the best way to accomplish a certain goal. Add the Beast's Lair to rolls related to the vision. If the Beast reads the entrails of a human, she may also ask a question about anyone related to her victim (such as a family member, loved one, stalker, or the last Beast to feed from him).<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The Beast gains the Steadfast Condition. It can only be resolved in the context of her vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast unleashes a foul curse on the unfortunate target of her vengeance. This requires having some piece of the victim, such as a lock of hair, vial of blood, or photograph. While heaping invections upon the target, the Beast destroys the sympathetic object (ripping up the photo, burning the hair, drinking the blood, etc.), and rolls Presence + Occult, contested by the victim's Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. Each net success on the Beast's part allows her to place any Personal Tilt of her choosing on her victim. Tilts that come in multiple levels of severity always inflict the least potent of their type, but additional successes can be allocated to increase their level (eg, one success can cause the Moderate Sick Tilt, while two successes create the Grave version).<br /> <br /> The Beast can target someone with this effect from any distance so long as they are both on the same plane of existence, <i>or</i>, if the Beast is within her Lair, while the target is in the physical location corresponding to one of her Chambers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Atavism, but I have a couple of issues with it.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the effects feel a little too... disparate. And I know I'm guilty of this in my Atavisms as well, but I feel like an Atavism should have a tight conceptual purview. The Normal and Satiety Expenditure effects work fine, but the extispicy feels both a bit disconnected from the other two (you've kind of got generic occult/traps -&gt; divination -&gt; curse). What if the Low Satiety was some way of adding 'dark magic' to the traps and vexations that the Atavism improves, maybe by making detecting them traps or poisons, disarming the former or identifying/making an antidote to the latter a Clash of Wills? Also, shouldn't the Normal effect be (1/2 Lair) bonus? Because otherwise you can potentially get 10 dice just from that. On the other hand, it's only dealing with 'mortal' magic/charms.<br /> <br /> Huh. What about moving the base effect up to Low Satiety and having the base effect be the ability to spend X amount of time in meditation/communing with the Dream/whatever to gain (Lair) dots of mortal supernatural Merits? Like Unseen Sense or psychic Merits or Omen Sense or whatever? We've already got some nice stuff for 'dark magic' there, and it would fit damn well. Maybe have some form of limit on the number of uses or something, or some kind of price. On the other hand, most Supernatural Merits have Drawbacks already, so that might be enough. <br /> <br /> Secondly, and this is more a personal opinion than anything solid, I think that the Atavism should be Inguma, not Namtaru. I could see it working for Namtaru as well, but i can't help but think that 'dark magic that any normal-looking person could practice' fits fear of the Other better than it does fear of revulsion/disgust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193936#post1193936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's a related Nightmare while I'm at it:<br /> <br /> <b>Witch's Brew</b><br /> <br /> <i>Everyone knows this: Don't take candy from strangers. Don't leave your drink unattended. Don't accept that apple pie from your kindly neighbor. They could have put anything in it.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>To use this Nightmare, the Beast must create or tamper with a beverage of some sort. This could take the form of brewing a foul-smelling liquid in a cauldron, mixing up a mojito, or merely stirring a packet of sugar into someone's coffee. The Beast takes a -2 penalty to the next roll she makes to activate a Nightmare; in return, the next person who imbibes the tampered beverage suffers its effects.<br /> <br /> <b>High Satiety:</b> The Beast can imbue a Nightmare into a number of drinks equal to her Lair.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast makes the drink especially tempting. This is the best cup of coffee her victim's ever smelled, or the Hero is convinced that this is a magical potion that will increase his might tenfold. The Beast can choose whether this effect applies to anyone, a single person of her designation, or other specified group in-between. A person who fits the criteria and who comes across the Nightmare-infused beverage must make a Resolve + Composure roll or immediately drink the beverage, downing it in one gulp if possible. Offering the drink to someone who fits the criteria always counts as Soft Leverage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just like this Nightmare. I can see lots of fun being had with it. Bravo. Do you want to post it on the homebrew Nightmares thread as well? You do seem to be missing an Exceptional Success result, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-10-2018, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:52:56-08:00","id":1193978,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> Be sure to add the nightmare to the homebrew nightmares thread! The Exceptional success is easily enough fixed - most of these delayed/proxi nightmares simply invoke the actual nightmares exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T17:06:21-08:00","id":1194091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1193947#post1193947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Atavism, but I have a couple of issues with it.<br /> <br /> Firstly, the effects feel a little too... disparate. And I know I'm guilty of this in my Atavisms as well, but I feel like an Atavism should have a tight conceptual purview. The Normal and Satiety Expenditure effects work fine, but the extispicy feels both a bit disconnected from the other two (you've kind of got generic occult/traps -&gt; divination -&gt; curse). What if the Low Satiety was some way of adding 'dark magic' to the traps and vexations that the Atavism improves, maybe by making detecting them traps or poisons, disarming the former or identifying/making an antidote to the latter a Clash of Wills? Also, shouldn't the Normal effect be (1/2 Lair) bonus? Because otherwise you can potentially get 10 dice just from that. On the other hand, it's only dealing with 'mortal' magic/charms.<br /> <br /> Huh. What about moving the base effect up to Low Satiety and having the base effect be the ability to spend X amount of time in meditation/communing with the Dream/whatever to gain (Lair) dots of mortal supernatural Merits? Like Unseen Sense or psychic Merits or Omen Sense or whatever? We've already got some nice stuff for 'dark magic' there, and it would fit damn well. Maybe have some form of limit on the number of uses or something, or some kind of price. On the other hand, most Supernatural Merits have Drawbacks already, so that might be enough.<br /> <br /> Secondly, and this is more a personal opinion than anything solid, I think that the Atavism should be Inguma, not Namtaru. I could see it working for Namtaru as well, but i can't help but think that 'dark magic that any normal-looking person could practice' fits fear of the Other better than it does fear of revulsion/disgust.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I just like this Nightmare. I can see lots of fun being had with it. Bravo. Do you want to post it on the homebrew Nightmares thread as well? You do seem to be missing an Exceptional Success result, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your feedback. In my defense, Heart of the Ocean is probably just as disparate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> I do think you're right though; the concept could be tighter. The divination part was a sudden inspiration while taking a shower. That kind of thought. I'm not sold on the idea of gaining Merits through the Atavism, but I will think a bit more about what I'm trying to do here. I want all the parts to feel visceral and dark; like mentioned in the flavor text, this Atavism is about &quot;filthy&quot; magic.<br /> <br /> You might be right about this being more of an Inguma thing; I first came up with the idea some time ago, and connected it with the portrayal of hideous-looking witches, like hags or Gruntilda, hence the Namtaru association.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you like the Nightmare. I'd forgotten about the thread on that subject, funnily enough. I'll add it there. I'd also forgotten about the Exceptional Success clause on meta-Nightmares, so I'll add that in as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:07:02-08:00","id":1194159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1194091#post1194091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for your feedback. In my defense, Heart of the Ocean is probably just as disparate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1194091#post1194091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think you're right though; the concept could be tighter. The divination part was a sudden inspiration while taking a shower. That kind of thought. I'm not sold on the idea of gaining Merits through the Atavism, but I will think a bit more about what I'm trying to do here. I want all the parts to feel visceral and dark; like mentioned in the flavor text, this Atavism is about &quot;filthy&quot; magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point. And giving a Beast access to mortal supernatural Merits might break the power economy a bit much, especially if they can change them up. It was really just a sudden idea; I honestly didn't think too much about it. I'm just trying to think of other options and I'm coming up a bit blank, other than using the rules in <i>Dark Eras Companion</i> for Rites somehow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1194091#post1194091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be right about this being more of an Inguma thing; I first came up with the idea some time ago, and connected it with the portrayal of hideous-looking witches, like hags or Gruntilda, hence the Namtaru association.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. As I say, it could certainly work for the Namtaru, I just think that it fits the Inguma better. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:40:37-08:00","id":1194167,"title":"","content":"I like that the Atavism doesn't have too much of an overlap with Mimir's Wisdom regarding the &quot;Getting answers for questions&quot;, thank to the divination route and try to catch glimpses of the future. The Sat expenditure should somehow include the Lair for the roll, though, otherwise the Atavisms growth wouldn't work as well with the Power Stat. Unless that's your intention.<br /> I agree with the 1/2 Lair rounded up issue.<br /> I also feel like it shouldn't be traps, but occult traps (mostly because when entering a witch's lair, you won't step into a Bear Trap, but rather probably offset some sort of curse), but maybe that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T00:42:47-08:00","id":1194169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1194167#post1194167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also feel like it shouldn't be traps, but occult traps (mostly because when entering a witch's lair, you won't step into a Bear Trap, but rather probably offset some sort of curse), but maybe that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you can set 'traps' without any tools or materials by inscribing occult signs or spilling blood or whatever, which manifest as curses with similar effects - a snare-equivalent is a curse that binds your legs together, a bear trap is a lash of entangling thorns or similar and a 'tripwire alarm' is a sign that when stepped over screams like a lost soul. I'm thinking of the Hag from <i>Dead By Daylight</i> as I suggest this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T08:16:46-07:00","id":1194249,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> These are both great suggestions. I'll reword the first ability to occult-style traps. I like that. I'll also change the Normal Effect to 1/2 Lair rounded up, and make the Satiety Expenditure dice pool Presence + Occult + Lair (or maybe just Presence + Lair if that's too much).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T05:38:38-07:00","id":1197947,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Ephemeral Flesh (Eshmaki)</u></b><br /> Made from shadow-stuff or stranger material still, some monsters are not scary because they can shrug off anything, but because they are not even bothered by anything in the first place.<br /> <br /> Persistent (Normal), Reflexive (Sat. Expenditure)<br /> Dice Pool: Wirs+Occult+Lair (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: The Beast is far lighter than they are supposed to be: running on snow, thin branches or jumping falling debris up are feasible. They add their Lair to all athletics dicepools.<br /> In addition, situation in which they exert themselves physically due to harsh conditions like Thin Air or high Gravity, they ignore a number of penalty modifiers up to half their Lair rounded up.<br /> <b>Low Satiety Effect</b>: <i>Stumped. Any ideas?</i><br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: The Beast's body turns intangible. By essentially skipping between planes world for brief amounts of time, the Beast may overcome adversity and obstacles.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The Beast is stuck in between planes, and cannot interact with anyone or anything for 3 turns, after which they incurr their Lair in Lethal damage.<br /> Failure: The Beast cannot skip between planes.<br /> Success: The Beast can skip between planes for up to rolled successes consecutive turns. During this time, they can be seen, but pass through everything. This allows them to walk through walls, ignore open fire, they cannot be grabbed etc. Passing through living beings like this causes a Resolve+Composure roll. If it fails, the victim gains the Spooked condition. At ST discretion, this may be cause for a Breaking Point.<br /> The Beast cannot 'fly' upwards, but they may sink through floors at their speed.<br /> Exeptional Success: Instead of consecutive turns, the Beast can decide when to use up their turns, allowing them to be intangible one turn, and entirely solid the next.<br /> <br /> Should the Beast run out of turns while inside a solid object, the are sent out to the nearest exit at their speed per turn. Each turn they spent inside the object, they take its Durability in Bashing Damage, which cannot be mitigated or soaked by armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:14:29-07:00","id":1209184,"title":"","content":"<b><u>Symbiotic Passenger (Namtaru)</u></b><br /> Basically, The horror piggibacks a smaller Astral being on it's back. Satiety drain doubles. or in case of Legendary Horror the essence drain is doubled. Maximum Rank - Lair/2 rounded up.<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: The Beast May use any Influence of the Being it piggibacks. .<br /> <b>Low Satiety Effect</b>: The Beast lets the being use any numina it possesses through him freely. Any costs are paid by the symbiotic.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: The Beast's body thums with borrowed power. add creatures power/finesse/resistance points to attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-20-2018, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T06:51:33-07:00","id":1209222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1209184#post1209184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Symbiotic Passenger (Namtaru)</u></b><br /> Basically, The horror piggibacks a smaller Astral being on it's back. Satiety drain is doubles. or in case of Legendary Horror the essence drain is doubled. .<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect</b>: The Beast May use any Influence of the Being it piggibacks. .<br /> <b>Low Satiety Effect</b>: The Beast lets the being use any numina it possesses through him freely. Any costs are paid by the symbiotic.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure</b>: The Beast's body thums with borrowed power. add creatures power/finesse/resistance points to attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, but I feel there should be a limit / power-scale. As is, a Beast with this could be a starting character, but could channel Rank 5+ beings.<br /> How about making it a sort of 'captivating Astral beings' kind of thing, with them being able to channel up to [Lair] Rank beings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:14:24-07:00","id":1209230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1209222#post1209222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting idea, but I feel there should be a limit / power-scale. As is, a Beast with this could be a starting character, but could channel Rank 5+ beings.<br /> How about making it a sort of 'captivating Astral beings' kind of thing, with them being able to channel up to [Lair] Rank beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Lair/2 would be more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T07:24:15-07:00","id":1209234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1209230#post1209230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Lair/2 would be more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lair /2 rounded up? Seems reasonable to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T05:05:50-07:00","id":1216953,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone. I found <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> 's Irkalla really neat, and wanted to add it as an option to my players, but I don't like having Families with only three Atavisms. So I had to create a new one. Cinder, feel free to steal if you like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Life beyond Death (Irkalla)</b><br /> The fear of the dead coming back to haunt the living is tangible in a lot of culture, and some Horrors embodies just that: pile of bones held together with rotten sinew, dead skin sewn as a grotesque body, or just the proverbial zombie leaving decaying flesh in his wake. A Beast with such Horror is able to draw entropy and stasis in its body, gaining the mixed blessing of undeath.<br /> <b>Normal:</b> As an instant action, the Beast can enter a Dead State, or revert to an Alive State. While dead, he gain the following advantages and weakness:<br /> - He appears completely dead. No mundane medical exams may detect the deception. Supernatural powers still register him as alive.<br /> - He add his Lair to Stamina roll to resist poison, drug, illness and pain.<br /> - He doesn't have to breathe, and so become immune to suffocation, gas poisoning, and drowning.<br /> - He can't eat, drink or sleep, but doesn't suffer from the consequences of hunger, thirst and fatigue. These consequences still build up with time, but only apply when reverting to the Alive State.<br /> - Wound penalties aside, he doesn't suffer any consequences from having his health track full of bashing or lethal damages.<br /> - He can't heal, even with other supernatural powers (which include other Atavisms like Relentless Hunter), unless by spending Satiety in his Lair or with a power that specifically heal undeads.<br /> - The Beast is obviously dead. He cannot have social interaction (aside from Intimidation) with normal people, and even supernatural (including other Beasts) find him unclean somehow, reducing it's Impression by two levels.<br /> - The dead coming back is a nightmare on it's own. Characters with Integrity make a breaking point roll if they see the Beast in Dead State. This roll is penalized by the Beast wound penalties (even at low Satiety), such wounds highlighting how unnatural a walking dead is. This breaking point is however not enough to create a Chamber.<br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As his hunger grow, the Best's flesh become truly dead meat:<br /> - You can snap his neck, slit his throat, pierce his heart, it's only a minor inconvenience. He cannot be targeted by a Killing Blow.<br /> - He doesn't suffer wound penalties.<br /> - As a vampire, non mystical weapons inflicts only bashing damages. Anathema inflict their damages as usual.<br /> - If a supernatural power try to determine if the Beast is alive or dead, it must succeed in a Clash of Will to not register him as dead.<br /> - While it doesn't bother him in Dead State, the Beast's bones are more brittle, and its flesh tend to fall off. Mark with a point bashing damages suffered while at low Satiety. When reverting to Alive State (at any Satiety), these damages are upgraded to lethal damages.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>When spending Satiety, the Beast is impossible to kill, or even to slow down. This effect last for a scene or an hour (whichever is shorter), and can be renewed each scene with one Satiety without running out.<br /> - Even if the his health is full of aggravated damages, the Beast can still act normally. At storyteller discretion, enough damage (such as inflicted by industrial machinery) can destroy fully the Beast body, but even if a crawling arm remains, the Beast can still act.<br /> - Any tilts or conditions inflicted by damages, such as Arm Wreck or Blinded, see their effects negated. They are not healed or resolved, and will take effect again when this effect wears off. Tilt and Condition imposed while this effect is active are normally inflicted, but won't take effect before the end of this power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","user":"Nepher","date":". 05-15-2018, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T13:40:11-07:00","id":1217100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1216953#post1216953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone. I found <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> 's Irkalla really neat, and wanted to add it as an option to my players, but I don't like having Families with only three Atavisms. So I had to create a new one. Cinder, feel free to steal if you like it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Life beyond Death (Irkalla)</b><br /> The fear of the dead coming back to haunt the living is tangible in a lot of culture, and some Horrors embodies just that: pile of bones held together with rotten sinew, dead skin sewn as a grotesque body, or just the proverbial zombie leaving decaying flesh in his wake. A Beast with such Horror is able to draw entropy and stasis in its body, gaining the mixed blessing of undeath.<br /> <b>Normal:</b> As an instant action, the Beast can enter a Dead State, or revert to an Alive State. While dead, he gain the following advantages and weakness:<br /> - He appears completely dead. No mundane medical exams may detect the deception. Supernatural powers still register him as alive.<br /> - He add his Lair to Stamina roll to resist poison, drug, illness and pain.<br /> - He doesn't have to breathe, and so become immune to suffocation, gas poisoning, and drowning.<br /> - He can't eat, drink or sleep, but doesn't suffer from the consequences of hunger, thirst and fatigue. These consequences still build up with time, but only apply when reverting to the Alive State.<br /> - Wound penalties aside, he doesn't suffer any consequences from having his health track full of bashing or lethal damages.<br /> - He can't heal, even with other supernatural powers, unless by spending Satiety in his Lair or with a power that specifically heal undeads.<br /> - The more hungry he is, the more he appears decayed. His social rolls (excluding Intimidation) are capped by his Satiety.<br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As his hunger grow, the Best's flesh become truly dead meat:<br /> - You can snap his neck, slit his throat, pierce his heart, it's only a minor inconvenience. He cannot be targeted by a Killing Blow.<br /> - He doesn't suffer wound penalties.<br /> - As a vampire, non mystical weapons inflicts only bashing damages. Anathema inflict their damages as usual.<br /> - If a supernatural power try to determine if the Beast is alive or dead, it must succeed in a Clash of Will to not register him as dead.<br /> - While it doesn't bother him in Dead State, the Beast's bones are more brittle, and its flesh tend to fall off. Mark with a point bashing damages suffered while at low Satiety. When reverting to Alive State (at any Satiety), these damages are upgraded to lethal damages.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>When spending Satiety, the Beast is impossible to kill, or even to slow down. This effect last for a scene or an hour (whichever is shorter), and can be renewed each scene with one Satiety without running out.<br /> - Even if the his health is full of aggravated damages, the Beast can still act normally. At storyteller discretion, enough damage (such as inflicted by industrial machinery) can destroy fully the Beast body, but even if a crawling arm remains, the Beast can still act.<br /> - Any tilts or conditions inflicted by damages, such as Arm Wreck or Blinded, see their effects negated. They are not healed or resolved, and will take effect again when this effect wears off. Tilt and Condition imposed while this effect is active are normally inflicted, but won't take effect before the end of this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this concept, despite some overlap with existing Kinship Merits and Atavisms. However, the Normal Effect, I feel, should have a limit on how long he can keep the state up, otherwise there are very few reasons not to spend tremendous amounts of time in this state when necessary. E.g. [Lair] hours feels fair, I think?<br /> I very much like the Low Satiety drawback, otherwise it'd be too op.<br /> I'd also think that normal regeneration and healing does not work on a dead body, so x-nay on reducing damage AND healing them with Relentless Hunter. An Irkalla with this and Unbreakable would already be plenty tanky, and close to indestructible upon spending Satiety on Unbreakable and going Dead State.<br /> <br /> The Satiety Expenditure I can see where you're coming from, but feels a tad much. Then again, Promethean Titans do have a similar ability...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T01:43:50-07:00","id":1218832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1217100#post1217100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also think that normal regeneration and healing does not work on a dead body, so x-nay on reducing damage AND healing them with Relentless Hunter. An Irkalla with this and Unbreakable would already be plenty tanky, and close to indestructible upon spending Satiety on Unbreakable and going Dead State.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already there. I'll add a reference to Relentless Hunter, since it's the main healing Beast's power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1217100#post1217100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Satiety Expenditure I can see where you're coming from, but feels a tad much. Then again, Promethean Titans do have a similar ability...</div> </div> </div> </div>Promethean was the main inspiration of the whole Atavism <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1217100#post1217100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this concept, despite some overlap with existing Kinship Merits and Atavisms. However, the Normal Effect, I feel, should have a limit on how long he can keep the state up, otherwise there are very few reasons not to spend tremendous amounts of time in this state when necessary. E.g. [Lair] hours feels fair, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm stump here. The whole goal was to spend tremendous amount of time in Dead State, but doing so damage your social interactions. The Satiety expenditure is a sink hole that force you to hunt again and again to remain &quot;alive&quot;, but too much time spent in this time increase your hunger and fatigue to levels you can't go back to. You're a zombie, not a sexy vampire. The limit on social interaction seems too weak, and I should go to Integrity breaking point, but I'm not sure how to balance it. Let me try something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T07:18:08-07:00","id":1218902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1216953#post1216953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Life beyond Death (Irkalla)</b><br /> The fear of the dead coming back to haunt the living is tangible in a lot of culture, and some Horrors embodies just that: pile of bones held together with rotten sinew, dead skin sewn as a grotesque body, or just the proverbial zombie leaving decaying flesh in his wake. A Beast with such Horror is able to draw entropy and stasis in its body, gaining the mixed blessing of undeath.<br /> <b>Normal:</b> As an instant action, the Beast can enter a Dead State, or revert to an Alive State. While dead, he gain the following advantages and weakness:<br /> - He appears completely dead. No mundane medical exams may detect the deception. Supernatural powers still register him as alive.<br /> - He add his Lair to Stamina roll to resist poison, drug, illness and pain.<br /> - He doesn't have to breathe, and so become immune to suffocation, gas poisoning, and drowning.<br /> - He can't eat, drink or sleep, but doesn't suffer from the consequences of hunger, thirst and fatigue. These consequences still build up with time, but only apply when reverting to the Alive State.<br /> - Wound penalties aside, he doesn't suffer any consequences from having his health track full of bashing or lethal damages.<br /> - He can't heal, even with other supernatural powers (which include other Atavisms like Relentless Hunter), unless by spending Satiety in his Lair or with a power that specifically heal undead.<br /> - The Beast is obviously dead. He cannot have social interaction (aside from Intimidation) with normal people, and even supernatural (including other Beasts) find him unclean somehow, reducing it's Impression by two levels.<br /> - The dead coming back is a nightmare on it's own. Characters with Integrity make a breaking point roll if they see the Beast in Dead State. This roll is penalized by the Beast wound penalties (even at low Satiety), such wounds highlighting how unnatural a walking dead is. This breaking point is however not enough to create a Chamber.<br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b>As his hunger grow, the Best's flesh become truly dead meat:<br /> - You can snap his neck, slit his throat, pierce his heart, it's only a minor inconvenience. He cannot be targeted by a Killing Blow.<br /> - He doesn't suffer wound penalties.<br /> - As a vampire, non mystical weapons inflicts only bashing damages. Anathema inflict their damages as usual.<br /> - If a supernatural power try to determine if the Beast is alive or dead, it must succeed in a Clash of Will to not register him as dead.<br /> - While it doesn't bother him in Dead State, the Beast's bones are more brittle, and its flesh tend to fall off. Mark with a point bashing damages suffered while at low Satiety. When reverting to Alive State (at any Satiety), these damages are upgraded to lethal damages.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>When spending Satiety, the Beast is impossible to kill, or even to slow down. This effect last for a scene or an hour (whichever is shorter), and can be renewed each scene with one Satiety without running out.<br /> - Even if the his health is full of aggravated damages, the Beast can still act normally. At storyteller discretion, enough damage (such as inflicted by industrial machinery) can destroy fully the Beast body, but even if a crawling arm remains, the Beast can still act.<br /> - Any tilts or conditions inflicted by damages, such as Arm Wreck or Blinded, see their effects negated. They are not healed or resolved, and will take effect again when this effect wears off. Tilt and Condition imposed while this effect is active are normally inflicted, but won't take effect before the end of this power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea here, but I feel like if this were an atavism I could take, I shouldn't be able to take Unbreakable, which, while less good on fluffiness, is far superior in crunch. I'd probably move the integrity breaking point to the low satiety section, and grant wound penalty ignoring into the normal effect. I'd also remove the only bashing damage portion in low satiety, and grant full immunity to poison/drug/illness/pain here. I also wouldn't worry about putting hunger/thirst/fatigue coming back to haunt you (pun intended) when you return to living state. While this does make using it 'safer', the fact is you're turning into a repulsive zombie. That's going to draw hunters like no tomorrow, not to mention Heroes finding you super easily.<br /> <br /> Satiety expenditure leaves me feeling a conundrum. I love it, but I would have done it slightly differently. Most of it's just some mild editing, but I did add one major effect:<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>When spending Satiety, the Beast automatically enters dead state and is near impossible to kill, or even to slow down. This effect last for a scene or an hour (whichever is shorter), and can be renewed each scene with one Satiety without running out.<br /> Even if the his health is full of aggravated damage, the Beast may still act normally. Full body destruction can kill the Beast. Otherwise, when the satiety effect ends a Beast with a full track of damage automatically downgrades one box of aggravated to Lethal damage. Any physical tilts inflicted through damage, such as Arm Wreck, are negated until this effect ends.<br /> <br /> Note: The beast only downgrades the 1 ag to lethal *if* they re already at full ag damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T12:11:24-07:00","id":1218996,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3648_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3648\" data-vbnamecard=\"3648\">Nepher</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a> <br /> Ah, I have to admit I didn't see the Integrity breaking point trigger. That is a fair argument and would render my &quot;being undead all the time has little to no drawbacks&quot; point moot. You could pull a Skin Deep and allow Heroes a bonus on Heroic Tracking when interacting with &quot;shaken&quot; people to give it more teeth.<br /> <br /> This and Unbreakable would make the Character immune to anything but supernatural weapons and environmental tilts and the like for measly 2 Satiety. Good thing grenades deal Agg when close enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T13:56:35-07:00","id":1219045,"title":"","content":"Has anybody suggested an Atavism for modular body parts?<br /> <br /> That means the ability to detach (and reattach) pieces of your body at will, and still control them while you're separated from you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T05:58:03-07:00","id":1219598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219045#post1219045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anybody suggested an Atavism for modular body parts?<br /> <br /> That means the ability to detach (and reattach) pieces of your body at will, and still control them while you're separated from you?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to do something like that as a part of my attempt to replicate John Carpenter's Thing through Beast, but I got nothing solid for now.<br /> <br /> It's a fun concept for a Namtaru Atavism, no doubt about that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T06:53:51-07:00","id":1219613,"title":"","content":"Maybe as a merit that requires Infestation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T13:06:45-07:00","id":1219755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219045#post1219045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anybody suggested an Atavism for modular body parts?<br /> <br /> That means the ability to detach (and reattach) pieces of your body at will, and still control them while you're separated from you?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Detachable Limbs Modification Demonic Form Ability would be a good place to look, mechanically. Maybe normal effect is you can ignore Limb/Arm Wrack Tilts (since you can just detach and stick them back on), with Low Satiety or Satiety Expenditure letting you control them, or regrow them completely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T13:44:25-07:00","id":1219773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219755#post1219755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Detachable Limbs Modification Demonic Form Ability would be a good place to look, mechanically. Maybe normal effect is you can ignore Limb/Arm Wrack Tilts (since you can just detach and stick them back on), with Low Satiety or Satiety Expenditure letting you control them, or regrow them completely?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think regrowing them would be part of the Relentless Hunter atavism. otherwise, you'd be practically indestructible.<br /> <br /> Although maybe low satiety would give your detached body parts the ability to levitate, instead of crawling along the floor? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-17-2018, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T14:16:46-07:00","id":1219784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219773#post1219773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I think regrowing them would be part of the Relentless Hunter atavism. otherwise, you'd be practically indestructible.<br /> <br /> Although maybe low satiety would give your detached body parts the ability to levitate, instead of crawling along the floor? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, animation is a pre-requisite for levitation. Since LS and SE are both options, one can't outright rely upon the other.<br /> <br /> Relentless Hunter is pure damage restoration. This would cover limbs specifically. A Makara Hydra or Namtaru Pennangalan could find great use in the regrowth option.<br /> <br /> After consideration, make that the Satiety Expenditure one? Low Satiety allows for control of limbs - combo them to rip off your own arm and fling it at someone, then just regrow it while it strangles them. Got the Satiety to burn? <i>Do it again</i>.<br /> <br /> Wings of the Raptor should allow your limbs (since they are you, after all) to fly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-17-2018, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T15:17:16-07:00","id":1219805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219784#post1219784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, animation is a pre-requisite for levitation. Since LS and SE are both options, one can't outright rely upon the other.<br /> <br /> Relentless Hunter is pure damage restoration. This would cover limbs specifically. A Makara Hydra or Namtaru Pennangalan could find great use in the regrowth option.<br /> <br /> After consideration, make that the Satiety Expenditure one? Low Satiety allows for control of limbs - combo them to rip off your own arm and fling it at someone, then just regrow it while it strangles them. Got the Satiety to burn? <i>Do it again</i>.<br /> <br /> Wings of the Raptor should allow your limbs (since they are you, after all) to fly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Right, I meant satiety expenditure, not low satiety.<br /> <br /> Got them confused!<br /> <br /> Hmm, a pennangalan with the ability to regenerate its body parts...<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of the monster reproducing through osmosis!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T16:20:17-07:00","id":1219816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219805#post1219805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Right, I meant satiety expenditure, not low satiety.<br /> <br /> Got them confused!<br /> <br /> Hmm, a pennangalan with the ability to regenerate its body parts...<br /> <br /> Now I'm thinking of the monster reproducing through osmosis!</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean mitosis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-17T16:38:42-07:00","id":1219820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219816#post1219816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean mitosis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes! <br /> <br /> Been a while since science class. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T02:31:25-07:00","id":1219902,"title":"","content":"A purely mechanical take on this atavisms:<br /> <br /> Normal satiety: your limbs detach. You may remove your arms or legs, and have them crawl along on their own for stamina+lair rounds. At the end of this time your limbs must be reattached. Detached limbs may be used to manipulate objects as though they were still attached.<br /> <br /> Low satiety: double duration the like may be attached, and it may levitate during their detached timeframe.<br /> <br /> Satiety expenditure: your detachments may include eyes and even your head. At the end of the duration, your detached limbs will wither to dust, and your body will grow a new one.<br /> <br /> All damage taken by individual limbs is recieved by the host. Detached Limbs have a health pool equal to 1+lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T06:47:46-07:00","id":1219948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219902#post1219902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A purely mechanical take on this atavisms:<br /> <br /> Normal satiety: your limbs detach. You may remove your arms or legs, and have them crawl along on their own for stamina+lair rounds. At the end of this time your limbs must be reattached. Detached limbs may be used to manipulate objects as though they were still attached.<br /> <br /> Low satiety: double duration the like may be attached, and it may levitate during their detached timeframe.<br /> <br /> Satiety expenditure: your detachments may include eyes and even your head. At the end of the duration, your detached limbs will wither to dust, and your body will grow a new one.<br /> <br /> All damage taken by individual limbs is recieved by the host. Detached Limbs have a health pool equal to 1+lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good. I think you should be able to detach your head as a base effect, though, in case someone wanted a Dullahan Horror.<br /> <br /> The limbs transferring damage is potentially dangerous - if subjected to multiple attacks or area attacks, they are transferring more damage than the Beast's Health, all at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T07:01:01-07:00","id":1219954,"title":"","content":"I still think this should be a merit with Infestation or Life Beyond Death as a prerequisite","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T08:14:47-07:00","id":1219968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219816#post1219816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean mitosis?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although reproducing via Osmosis could also be terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T09:33:23-07:00","id":1219995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219948#post1219948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good. I think you should be able to detach your head as a base effect, though, in case someone wanted a Dullahan Horror.<br /> <br /> The limbs transferring damage is potentially dangerous - if subjected to multiple attacks or area attacks, they are transferring more damage than the Beast's Health, all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did the health transferance like that intentionally. If you have relentless or unstoppable, you'll probably be fine.<br /> <br /> As far as the head- given that it's an extremely vital organ, I figured it should be at least low satiety. I also wasn't sure what else to give it that would fit.<br /> <br /> Aquatosic- that's a fine variant, but this thread is for atavisms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","user":"ArchonAres","date":". 05-18-2018, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T10:47:00-07:00","id":1220020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1219902#post1219902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A purely mechanical take on this atavisms:<br /> <br /> Normal satiety: your limbs detach. You may remove your arms or legs, and have them crawl along on their own for stamina+lair rounds. At the end of this time your limbs must be reattached. Detached limbs may be used to manipulate objects as though they were still attached.<br /> <br /> Low satiety: double duration the like may be attached, and it may levitate during their detached timeframe.<br /> <br /> Satiety expenditure: your detachments may include eyes and even your head. At the end of the duration, your detached limbs will wither to dust, and your body will grow a new one.<br /> <br /> All damage taken by individual limbs is recieved by the host. Detached Limbs have a health pool equal to 1+lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>as always, gret mechanics!<br /> now we just need to fluff it up.<br /> regarding damage transfer: would destroyed detached limbs not be drawback enough? (-dext, possibly - str for some time)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:34:27-07:00","id":1220033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220020#post1220020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> as always, gret mechanics!<br /> now we just need to fluff it up.<br /> regarding damage transfer: would destroyed detached limbs not be drawback enough? (-dext, possibly - str for some time)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe have it so that the damaged limbs regenerate over long periods (I'm imagining a bit like Deadpool's hand, only slower), or even make the Satiety Expenditure the ability to instantly regrow a limb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T11:48:59-07:00","id":1220037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220033#post1220033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe have it so that the damaged limbs regenerate over long periods (I'm imagining a bit like Deadpool's hand, only slower), or even make the Satiety Expenditure the ability to instantly regrow a limb.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say Satiety Expenditure regrows it the current/next turn. Again, you can replicate the Hydra, or throw your animate limbs at people like weird guided weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-18T12:07:26-07:00","id":1220048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220037#post1220037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">throw your animate limbs at people like weird guided weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>... Now I can't get <i>Jojo's Bizarre Adventure</i> out of my head.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T00:19:17-07:00","id":1220454,"title":"","content":"We need a new Inguma atavism. I thought Hivemind would be a fitting concept:<br /> Normal gives +Lair to group efforts involving the beast. Effect applies up to Lair\u00d75 yards away. Up to Lair people can be integrated into the hivemind. Dicepool is Int+Occult+Lair ( vs. Resolve+ST even if the target is 'willing'). Victim can try and shake it off with resolve + composure. Upon experiencing a breaking point, they are seperated.<br /> When part of hivemind, weak Telepathic Communication is possible (Think telegraphstyle), and everyone loses their vice and virtue equivalents, Adopting the beast's Legend and life instead. Lasts until severed.<br /> Low Satiety gives a shared dicepool for skills, effectively allowing the brawler To use the scientist's knowledge, and the scientist to throw a proper punch. Diuble-edged blade, though: They also share impressions, so many conditions and tilts experienced by one apply to all of them, e.g. wound penalties. The hivemind does not let go: penalties attempts to leave by Lair. May include pain as a distractor.<br /> Expenditure finally takes over, and the hivemind literally moves each body independently as if they were limbs of a larger whole. That is taxing on the beast's mind: when moving more than wits/2 rounded down people at once, all actions suffer a cummulative -1 penalty for each additional body. In addition to the Low Satiety effect, the hivemind now also shares a willpower dicepool.<br /> This effect holds for a scene. Afterwards, everyone suffers Insensate, Disoriented and cannot replenish Willpower for a scene due to exhaustion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Very rough, first draft, but I just had the idea and thought you might like it. Plus i think it fits the Inguma well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T05:43:37-07:00","id":1220521,"title":"","content":"Hive mind sounds more like a Nightmare. But a great nightmare","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T05:49:50-07:00","id":1220524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220521#post1220521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hive mind sounds more like a Nightmare. But a great nightmare</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe call it Your Mind Is Not Your Own, or possibly You Are Not An Island? Maybe the normal effect is 'hallucinating' voices (i.e. telepathy) but gaining a bonus to teamwork and the higher levels go further. The mind-control is already covered by You Must Obey, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T08:08:53-07:00","id":1220542,"title":"","content":"How about You Are A Drone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T08:20:44-07:00","id":1220544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220542#post1220542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about You Are A Drone?</div> </div> </div> </div>That works too, although the sound of it makes me think more 'conformity' than 'dominated'. Office-drone rather than borg-drone, if you see what I mean, although I'll admit that's likely just my interpretative side speaking.<br /> <br /> I study English Lit. What can you do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:00:09-07:00","id":1220549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220544#post1220544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I study English Lit. What can you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's a valid interpretation. I still prefer mine, but if you think it will give some people the wrong idea, I'll concede. I study journalism and communication in general, so I'm big on making sure people interpret my work the way I intended.<br /> <br /> though, this nightmare doesn't have to be about literal hiveminds. Conforming to the point that you might as well be a drone worker to those around you and being considered boring could be another source of this fear.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What about You Are A Tool? Add victim's skill ratings as straight equipment bonuses to other's work till the end of the scene as well as standard teamwork effects. But Resolve+Composure roll to do anything by yourself.<br /> <br /> Will repost this in Homebrew Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 05-20-2018, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:09:06-07:00","id":1220551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220549#post1220549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that's a valid interpretation. I still prefer mine, but if you think it will give some people the wrong idea, I'll concede. I study journalism and communication in general, so I'm big on making sure people interpret my work the way I intended.<br /> <br /> though, this nightmare doesn't have to be about literal hiveminds. Conforming to the point that you might as well be a drone worker to those around you and being considered boring could be another source of this fear.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What about You Are A Tool? Add victim's skill ratings as straight equipment bonuses to other's work till the end of the scene as well as standard teamwork effects. But Resolve+Composure roll to do anything by yourself.<br /> <br /> Will repost this in Homebrew Nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>You Are A Tool sounds great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:16:12-07:00","id":1220554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220454#post1220454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a new Inguma atavism. I thought Hivemind would be a fitting concept:<br /> Normal gives +Lair to group efforts involving the beast. Effect applies up to Lair\u00d75 yards away. Up to Lair people can be integrated into the hivemind. Dicepool is Int+Occult+Lair ( vs. Resolve+ST even if the target is 'willing'). Victim can try and shake it off with resolve + composure. Upon experiencing a breaking point, they are seperated.<br /> When part of hivemind, weak Telepathic Communication is possible (Think telegraphstyle), and everyone loses their vice and virtue equivalents, Adopting the beast's Legend and life instead. Lasts until severed.<br /> Low Satiety gives a shared dicepool for skills, effectively allowing the brawler To use the scientist's knowledge, and the scientist to throw a proper punch. Diuble-edged blade, though: They also share impressions, so many conditions and tilts experienced by one apply to all of them, e.g. wound penalties. The hivemind does not let go: penalties attempts to leave by Lair. May include pain as a distractor.<br /> Expenditure finally takes over, and the hivemind literally moves each body independently as if they were limbs of a larger whole. That is taxing on the beast's mind: when moving more than wits/2 rounded down people at once, all actions suffer a cummulative -1 penalty for each additional body. In addition to the Low Satiety effect, the hivemind now also shares a willpower dicepool.<br /> This effect holds for a scene. Afterwards, everyone suffers Insensate, Disoriented and cannot replenish Willpower for a scene due to exhaustion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Very rough, first draft, but I just had the idea and thought you might like it. Plus i think it fits the Inguma well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hivemind<br /> normal satiety: the beast may add up to Lair x2 willing subjects to it's hive mind, at a range of Lair x5 yds. While connected to the Hive mind, you gain a bonus to teamwork rolls equal to half the Beasts Lair. You also gain limited empathic connection to the members of the Hive, and can send and receive emotions from one another.<br /> <br /> Low satiety: The Hive mind pumps more information between the drones, allowing them to see, hear, smell, and feel what the others and the Hivemind can. The Hivemind may now also send and receive pictures and words through its link, increasing the communication between drones. Range and teamwork benefits doubly.<br /> <br /> Satiety expenditure: the beast can forcibly induct a member into the Hive, and give orders to its members for the duration of the scene. Anyone forcibly indicted counts as two willing members. The Hivemind can also order members to action. Resisting is a clash of wills. This effect lasts for an hour or a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T09:23:03-07:00","id":1220558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1220551#post1220551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You Are A Tool sounds great.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's good, because I just finished writing it up in Homebrew Nightmares and I want to get some feedback. Biggest issue is I'm not sure what Attribute to use for the Beast's dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T10:55:28-07:00","id":1234048,"title":"","content":"Parasite (Namtaru)<br /> Few things are considered as disgusting as parasitism - the survival on someone else's lifeforce.<br /> Roll: Dext+Occult+Lair vs.Occult +ST (low Satiety); Stamina+Strength+Lair vs. Stamina+ST<br /> Action: Instant and Reflexive<br /> <br /> Normal Effect:<br /> By succeeding in a touch-attack, the Beast inflicts the Syphoned condition. This could be a metaphysical connection, a 'energy-link' or some sort of parasitic organism that is implanted. The Beast can inflict Minor tilts like Sick on demand. (Need help with ideas here.)<br /> Once per scene, the Begotten can syphon lifeforce off of those with the condition by inflicting Lair Bashing damage, and heal themselves for the same amount. The damage may be distributed per the player's choice. By dealing an appropriate amount of Bashing, they may heal Lethal damage, but they cannot inflict Lethal damage this way.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety Effect: When the Horror hungers, it takes what it needs. When harming another, the Horror takes strength from the pain, and heals Lair/2 rounded down Bashing damage per turn.<br /> However, the hungry Horror is demanding, and not likely to show restraint: when Syphoning, it deals Lethal Damage those with the condition.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: Not sure yet, some sort of curveball like entering someone.<br /> <br /> I want some more help with that one - I am sure you can tell where I'm going with this. I considered doing this in a Merit rather than an<br /> <br /> Also working on some sort of mobility atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T11:17:22-07:00","id":1234053,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Satiety Expenditure could simply allow you to lifesteal more than once per scene? Or maybe it could be a bit mind-controlly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-11T17:42:50-07:00","id":1234122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1234048#post1234048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parasite (Namtaru)<br /> Few things are considered as disgusting as parasitism - the survival on someone else's lifeforce.<br /> Roll: Dext+Occult+Lair vs.Occult +ST (low Satiety); Stamina+Strength+Lair vs. Stamina+ST<br /> Action: Instant and Reflexive<br /> <br /> Normal Effect:<br /> By succeeding in a touch-attack, the Beast inflicts the Syphoned condition. This could be a metaphysical connection, a 'energy-link' or some sort of parasitic organism that is implanted. The Beast can inflict Minor tilts like Sick on demand. (Need help with ideas here.)<br /> Once per scene, the Begotten can syphon lifeforce off of those with the condition by inflicting Lair Bashing damage, and heal themselves for the same amount. The damage may be distributed per the player's choice. By dealing an appropriate amount of Bashing, they may heal Lethal damage, but they cannot inflict Lethal damage this way.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety Effect: When the Horror hungers, it takes what it needs. When harming another, the Horror takes strength from the pain, and heals Lair/2 rounded down Bashing damage per turn.<br /> However, the hungry Horror is demanding, and not likely to show restraint: when Syphoning, it deals Lethal Damage those with the condition.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: Not sure yet, some sort of curveball like entering someone.<br /> <br /> I want some more help with that one - I am sure you can tell where I'm going with this. I considered doing this in a Merit rather than an<br /> <br /> Also working on some sort of mobility atavism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like maybe leveraging the concept of Extreme Environments might be useful here, even if the effect is limited to a person as opposed to an environment. Basically, the target gets Stamina in time (hours or turns) before they start taking damage. Or just give the target a Disease Condition, except you gain what they lose. Normal is Bashing, LS is Lethal, SE forces a roll immediately?<br /> <br /> Another thing is you might treat Normal/Low Satiety/Satiety Expenditure as syphoning different things - Willpower, Natural Healing Rate (victim doubled, Beast halved), direct Health, etc. Or maybe forced sensory sharing (like the Parasite ability in Starcraft).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T12:16:15-07:00","id":1234358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1234122#post1234122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like maybe leveraging the concept of Extreme Environments might be useful here, even if the effect is limited to a person as opposed to an environment. Basically, the target gets Stamina in time (hours or turns) before they start taking damage. Or just give the target a Disease Condition, except you gain what they lose. Normal is Bashing, LS is Lethal, SE forces a roll immediately?<br /> <br /> Another thing is you might treat Normal/Low Satiety/Satiety Expenditure as syphoning different things - Willpower, Natural Healing Rate (victim doubled, Beast halved), direct Health, etc. Or maybe forced sensory sharing (like the Parasite ability in Starcraft).</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like that idea!<br /> will be changing normal to stealing regeneration, with an option of forcefully stealing Health over a period of time via Disease-like Tilt once per chapter. (this way, not displacing Relentless Hunter). Max Lair/2 rounded down targets at once.<br /> low satiety will be lethal, and immediate once per scene.<br /> Expenditure will be an attack like a tick-horror taking a sip or blood flowing from victim to Beast that deals Lair Lethal, and heals for Lair/2 rounded down. Usuable in combination with other Atavisms.<br /> <br /> (proper writeup when hand free)<br /> <br /> Alternatively, would be fun to have the exp turn it around and have the beat donate Health/Strength/Stamina. making this into a symbiotic relationship. But ill keep that idea for anothrer time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T08:16:47-07:00","id":1240879,"title":"","content":"Beastial (Inguma)<br /> Some monsters are defined by their similarity to or relationship with animals, like skinchangers. By tapping into their Horror's nature, Begotten prove to have incredibly keen instincts.<br /> <br /> Normal: The Beast adds their Lair to rolls involving Animal Ken and Survival. In addition, they are not bothered by difficult terrain, and have an increased sense of smell: they can track a scent as if they were dogs. Their animalistic instincts also give them an edge in battle: they calculate Defense with the Higher of dexterity or wits.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: The hungry Horror does not ask, it demands. By groaning, howling, and otherwise imitating animal noises, the Begotten can order even wild animals around as if they were tamed and trained by him. In addition, the Begotten can grow nails and fangs to deal +1 Lethal in unarmed combat. However, a beast is hard to control and easily distracted: penalize Composure rolls by -2.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The Begotten can turn into an animal of their choice, losing the ability to talk and all their social skills and merits (other than Intimidate and Animal Ken), but gaining abilities common for those animals, as well as retain access to their Nightmares and Atavisms. The Animal must not be smaller than their size - (Lair/2 rounded down) or larger than their size + (Lair/2 rounded down). If they chose an animal that is e.g. usually size 2, they can still opt to retain their Size.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":".  Vent0's advice 08-01-2018, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-31T17:13:33-07:00","id":1241081,"title":"","content":"What about the higher of Dexterity and Wits? It is such a simple thing, but common to animals and useful in some cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T02:38:35-07:00","id":1241218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1241081#post1241081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the higher of Dexterity and Wits? It is such a simple thing, but common to animals and useful in some cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent point, added!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:12:55-07:00","id":1241224,"title":"","content":"One question I have, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>, is whether, with the Low Satiety effect, you can also understand animals. For instance, could I ask an animal what it's seen, or is the power limited to ordering them around?<br /> <br /> Also, I kind of feel that you should still be able to speak in animal form - these are nightmare-beasts, after all, and talking animals are a staple of myth and fable. Imagine a great monster-wolf hunting you, and taunting you all the while as you try to hide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 08-01-2018, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T03:31:42-07:00","id":1241229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1241224#post1241224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I have, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, is whether, with the Low Satiety effect, you can also understand animals. For instance, could I ask an animal what it's seen, or is the power limited to ordering them around?<br /> <br /> Also, I kind of feel that you should still be able to speak in animal form - these are nightmare-beasts, after all, and talking animals are a staple of myth and fable. Imagine a great monster-wolf hunting you, and taunting you all the whole as you try to hide.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Little pigs, little pigs, let me in ... &quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T04:35:29-07:00","id":1241244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1241224#post1241224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I have, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, is whether, with the Low Satiety effect, you can also understand animals. For instance, could I ask an animal what it's seen, or is the power limited to ordering them around?<br /> <br /> Also, I kind of feel that you should still be able to speak in animal form - these are nightmare-beasts, after all, and talking animals are a staple of myth and fable. Imagine a great monster-wolf hunting you, and taunting you all the whole as you try to hide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point. Had Not considered that due to slightly railroading. Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> 's line is too cool to not use <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Yeah, I should have specified that yes, you can understand animals. Their usefulness, of course, is similar to animals used with Animalism, as some concepts are just beyond them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:51:19-07:00","id":1244301,"title":"","content":"<b>Blood of Medusa:</b> Legend says that the mythical Gorgon's blood was so acidic that man made weapons would dissolve instantly upon piercing her flesh. Some Begotten, especially Namtaru, have exhibited a similar blood quality, although in a much more diluted state.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> Your blood contains acidic properties that rapidly break down foreign substances they come into contact with. Whenever a melee weapon inflicts Lethal damage to you, your blood causes it to suffer 2 points of Durability damage. If the damage is inflicted with bare hands, the attacker suffers 1 point of Aggravated damage from acidic burns. The acidic properties of your blood do not affect Chosen Blade weapons!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> When your hunger flares, your blood does too, inflicting an additional 2 points of Durability damage to weapons that cause you Lethal damage. Damaged inflicted by unarmed attacks suffer an additional point of Aggravated damage from acidic burns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> A dormant bloodline flows through the veins of Beasts who possess this Atavism, and for a brief moment, they can awaken its full potential. By spending a point of Satiety, the Beast can reduce the next attack caused by a Lethal weapon to a single point of damage. The weapon is also destroyed in the process, as its material components are dissolved instantly upon breaking the skin. Lethal damage inflicted by unarmed attacks cause the enemy to suffer 4 points of Aggravated damage and receive an appropriate Tilt in the process. Once again, this does not affect Chosen Blade weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-09-2018, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T18:36:53-07:00","id":1244339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1244301#post1244301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Blood of Medusa:</b> Legend says that the mythical Gorgon's blood was so acidic that man made weapons would dissolve instantly upon piercing her flesh. Some Begotten, especially Namtaru, have exhibited a similar blood quality, although in a much more diluted state.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> Your blood contains acidic properties that rapidly break down foreign substances they come into contact with. Whenever a melee weapon inflicts Lethal damage to you, your blood causes it to suffer 2 points of Durability damage. If the damage is inflicted with bare hands, the attacker suffers 1 point of Aggravated damage from acidic burns. The acidic properties of your blood do not affect Chosen Blade weapons!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> When your hunger flares, your blood does too, inflicting an additional 2 points of Durability damage to weapons that cause you Lethal damage. Damaged inflicted by unarmed attacks suffer an additional point of Aggravated damage from acidic burns.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> A dormant bloodline flows through the veins of Beasts who possess this Atavism, and for a brief moment, they can awaken its full potential. By spending a point of Satiety, the Beast can reduce the next attack caused by a Lethal weapon to a single point of damage. The weapon is also destroyed in the process, as its material components are dissolved instantly upon breaking the skin. Lethal damage inflicted by unarmed attacks cause the enemy to suffer 4 points of Aggravated damage and receive an appropriate Tilt in the process. Once again, this does not affect Chosen Blade weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing scales oddly. Low Satiety can be an upgrade of Normal, but the Satiety Expenditure invalidates both, rather than being an additive.<br /> <br /> For point of suggestion, what about applying the Fragile tag to any weapon that strikes the Beast (either for Normal or Low)? For the Expenditure, what about instead the blood <i>sprays</i>, affecting not only the weapon that struck them, but creatures and other equipment nearby?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T20:41:24-08:00","id":1272111,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a> I like your Inhuman Panoply, but I feel it is a bit clunky and too detailed. I also think it should be Anakim, since some giants are known for exceptional crafting talent. It was the Cyclopes who created Zeus' famous thunderbolts, for example.<br /> <br /> Here is my attempt at a simplified version. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Inhuman Panoply (Anakim)</b></u><br /> <i>Humans like to think that they know all there is to know about making things. After all, they took tin and copper and invented bronze, took wood and shaped it into bows and ships. But there are older things, things which know the ways of making strange substances and eldritch implements.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant (Normal Satiety), Reflexive (Low Satiety)<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Intelligence + Crafts<br /> <br /> <b>Normal:</b> The Beast can Craft Equipment using his Lair Traits when within their immediate presence, such as fire for Burning or plants for Undergrowth. The resulting object has the same Size of a mundane equivalent [caps at Lair x 5], Durability equal to [Lair + 1] and Equipment Bonus equal to the penalty chosen for the activation roll [caps at Lair/2 round up]. The resulting object cannot be overly complex and you must select two Lair Traits (Minor and/or Major) that can be affected (this can be changed at the start of each chapter). Your creations vanish when you stop paying attention to them or the scene ends, whichever comes first. This Atavism stacks with traits that increase the Beast's mental faculties, such as Mimir's Wisdom. He may have a number of such items outside of his Lair equal to [Lair x 2]. Inside the Lair, this number is increased to [Lair x 5].<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> With the Horror's growing Hunger, its malice and power leaks into its creations. The resulting objects may have complex mechanisms and do not vanish so quickly. They last for a number of (10 - Satiety at the time of the roll) in hours with a Success, or in days with an Exceptional Success. Supernatural attempts to affect these items trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast's creations become truly awe-inspiring or terrifying for the scene. When openly wielding them, he may select either the Inspired or Shaken Condition to inflict on all onlookers who fail a Resolve + Composure - Lair roll. Furthermore, he may imbue one item with an Atavism he has, except Inhuman Panoply itself. The duration and effects of the item are determined by the Beast's Satiety at the time of the activation. The user of the item has an effective Lair equal to half of the Beast's (rounded up) and cannot mimic the Satiety Expenditure of the imbued Atavism. The maximum number of such items is listed under the Normal Satiety effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-05-2019, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T21:11:59-08:00","id":1272116,"title":"","content":"It's a bit ironic that 'dwarven smiths' will now be Anakim! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I love the idea for 'forgemasters Giants'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T08:08:37-08:00","id":1272181,"title":"","content":"it ain't too surprising, the smiths in Greek mythology were cyclopses afterall","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T15:57:40-08:00","id":1272248,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> , I like your mechanics better than my own, though I'll stand by my decision to put Inhuman Panoply with the Inguma. I can see your logic, but I personally feel that the 'thrust' of the Atavism, so to speak, is more about 'they match us in our uniqueness and make tools of things we cannot', rather than 'their crafts surpass us so completely that we cannot hope to match them'. Perhaps the Anakim crafting-Atavism is specifically focused around making <i>better</i> things than humans can? I'm not sure. Perhaps there's space for the Inguma to forge curses into things, ala Andvari and the ring he cursed.<br /> <br /> Either way, Inhuman Panoply is definitely something which the Anakim should take semi-regularly - how else would they forge thunderbolts into weapons, as you said?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-01-2018, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T03:53:12-08:00","id":1272350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1272248#post1272248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> Perhaps there's space for the Inguma to forge curses into things, ala Andvari and the ring he cursed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be vey fitting IMO. The main pattern of the Inguma's nightmares is the fear that something or someone totally unobtrusive could always turn out to be something evil under camouflage, and what would say it better than cursed items ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T06:17:36-08:00","id":1272371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1272350#post1272350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be vey fitting IMO. The main pattern of the Inguma's nightmares is the fear that something or someone totally unobtrusive could always turn out to be something evil under camouflage, and what would say it better than cursed items ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, there's a Mummy Kinship nightmare that does this, but it feels like something that should have an Atavism as well, now that the Inguma are a thing. With the BPG, it's moved from something they need to borrow other supernaturals' themes to do to something that feels native. That said, I'm not sure what the Atavism would be called, or how it would work without being too Nightmare-ish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 12-02-2018, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T14:03:00-08:00","id":1281571,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Vengeance (Eshmaki)</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>Everyone knows it: a cornered beast is much more dangerous, for it will fight with even more ferocity. How much more frightening would a mortally wounded dragon be, then?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> Whenever the Beast would suffer from Wound Penalties, they are turned into Bonuses instead.<br /> <b>Low Satiety Effect:</b> The Beast may chose to ignore a physical Tilt like Armwreck for [Lair*2] turns. No matter if their arm snapped in half or their ankle broken; they move just as well. When the immunity runs out, the wounds come back - with a vengeance: the tilt is aggravated (e.g accompanied by a situationally appropriate second tilt, as per ST like gaining another leg wreck) or alternatively, giving the Beast a generic Exhaustion Condition: Beast now moves at 1/2 their speed, loses their defense and suffers a temporary -2 to all physical and mental rolls until resting up properly.<br /> <b>Spending Satiety:</b> For the rest of the scene, losing a Healthbox gives a single bonus die to be used on the next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> I admit, this is inspired by the good ol' 'Turning Red' of enemies in games, where hitting an enemy made them faster and/or change their movements and thus more dangerous.<br /> This is to help all those batman-like nemesis emulate their hero even more, with a Heroic Second Wind-like ability. Also encourages quickly putting a Beast down in a fight, since a death-of-a-thousand-cuts approach here is even more dangerous. (Cue Heroes going totally overboard, to be on the safe side.) Needs an addendum to the Normal effect, as-is it is kinda underpowered imo. Maybe something to encourage reckless behaviour like an 8-again on something like untrained physical skills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 01-18-2019, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-19T11:26:13-07:00","id":1313150,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Digital Gargoyle [Ugallu]</b></u><br /> <i>In their arrogance, humans surround themselves with ever more advanced technology, not paying attention to how vulnerable it makes them. All it takes is one surgical strike at the right infrastructures to make their empires of steel and silicon fall apart.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast can roll Wits + Computers to perceive the surroundings and active usage of any digital technology within [Lair x 10] meters. If he has another Atavism that enhances his senses (such as Needs Must) or mental faculties (such as Mimir's Wisdom), he may combine the relevant effects. Merits such as Investigative Aide and Connected Lair may also apply at ST discretion. He retains awareness of his own surroundings while doing this and may thus benefit from Defense and so on.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The range becomes [Lair x 50] meters and the Beast gains Rote Quality on all mundane Computers rolls. He can roll Intelligence + Computers as an Instant Action to take full control of a device within range for a number of hours equal to Successes during this scene. He can turn it on/off, use programs, edit files, delete information, implant false clues and so on.<br /> <br /> Should the devices have extensions that can physically interact with their surroundings, the Beast may hi-jack these extensions as if they were part of the Horror. He uses his own Skills, but replaces Physical Attributes with the equivalent Mental Attributes. Switching between viable devices requires an Instant Action. He may only switch devices a number of times equal to [Lair] each scene. Mundane attempts to detect or counter his hi-jacking suffer his Lair as a penalty, while supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills. If the Beast is detected or countered, he gains the Shaken Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Once each scene, the Beast can use digital technology within range as a gateway into his Lair. You achieve an automatic Success on the roll to open the Primordial Pathway, and add your Computers to your Resolve to determine how many turns it lasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T00:15:14-07:00","id":1313799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1313150#post1313150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Digital Gargoyle [Ugallu]</b></u><br /> <i>In their arrogance, humans surround themselves with ever more advanced technology, not paying attention to how vulnerable it makes them. All it takes is one surgical strike at the right infrastructures to make their empires of steel and silicon fall apart.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast can roll Wits + Computers to perceive the surroundings and active usage of any digital technology within [Lair x 10] meters. If he has another Atavism that enhances his senses (such as Needs Must) or mental faculties (such as Mimir's Wisdom), he may combine the relevant effects. Merits such as Investigative Aide may also apply. He retains awareness of his own surroundings while doing this and may thus benefit from Defense and so on.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The range of the Normal Satiety effect is now measured in kilometers. The Beast rolls one automatic Success on all Computers rolls, plus the actual results on the dice. Furthermore, he can roll Intelligence + Computers to take full control of any such device for a number of hours equal to Successes during this scene. He can turn it on and off, use programs, edit files, delete information, implant false clues and so on. If the device is connected to others through a network or a similar setup, he may affect any and all connected devices simultaneously. Attempts to detect or counter this suffer his Lair as a penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast can use digital technology as a means of manifesting Lair Traits during this scene. Should his Satiety be Normal, choose one device within range as a manifestation point and use two Minor Traits or one Major Trait. Should his Satiety be Low, you manifest the aforementioned Lair Trait(s) around any or all connected devices. Do not make separate rolls or spend Willpower points: you achieve an automatic Success and add your Computers to your Resolve to determine how many turns it lasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope you don't mind. I love this Atavism and this idea is perfect for a Beast character of mine. I changed it quite a bit to use it for him:<br /> <br /> <b>Digital Gargoyle [Ugallu]</b><br /> In the time before man tamed electricity and built his great cities, he lived on the edge of the wild. In that era the monsters were found between the dark trees of the forest. How many stories did they tell to scare each other, to impart lessons, that featured the words \u201cinto the woods.\u201d Now, in their arrogance, humans surround themselves with ever more advanced technology. Technology which outstrips the ability of most of them to understand. In lack of understanding there is fear. The new woods are digital. Modern man fears what\u2019s at the end of the wire; be it the government, AI, Aliens or something less definable. In chat rooms and private networks, the modern cautionary fable often features \u201cclicked on the link.\u201d<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Wits + Computer (Normal Effect); Intelligence + Computer (Low Satiety)<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> The Beast\u2019s Horror is not constrained to the Beast\u2019s own physical body, he can roll Wits + Computer to suffuse his Horror into any technological network that has at least one active device in a location he is occupying. The Beast can inhabit any connected devices in this location, plus those in an additional location per dot of Lair he possesses. This can represent rooms connected by a security system, computer labs currently connected via the internet or streets on the city\u2019s traffic grid. They only need to be connected via technology, physical distances between parts of this network do not matter.<br /> While connected to this network the Beast can extend his senses through it. This is a strange form of perception. To the Beast the screens of monitors are like dozens of hazy eyes, the cables vibrate like bones in an ear. If a device connected to the network has a camera or audio receiver the Beast can access it and gains any benefit it possesses on top of the Beasts usual perception. For example, he could access a stream of night vision camera footage, and even copy it. He may download and retain information from connected devices within his own mind as if he was a computer with storage capacity equal to his Lair x 10 in Gigabytes. He may later download this stored information to a compatible device with another use of this Atavism.<br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The hungry Beast is restless, his Horror trying to stretch to its prey even if its limbs are made of data and electrical wiring. If he is networked into a device the Beast can roll Intelligence + Computers to take full control of it. He can turn it on and off, use programs, edit files, delete information and so on. If the device is connected to anything that can have a physical impact on the environment the Beast can use this as well. A clever Beast could use a factories robot assembly line to dismember a hero in seconds or delete an entire schools academic record (including the \u2018fool proof\u2019 backup.) This is beyond simply using the technology, to the Horror it is the Beasts body. Attempts to detect or counter the Beast\u2019s actions suffer the Beasts Lair as a penalty. This includes defense against attacks made with the technology the Beast inhabits. If another Beast using this Atavism, or a creature with a similar power, tries to override or counter the Beasts actions it triggers a Clash of Wills.<br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> By spending a point of Satiety the Beast can use the network he inhabits as a means of manifesting his Lair Traits. When using this ability, the affected locations count as having one of the Beasts Minor Lair traits in effect for the purpose of manifesting additional Lair Traits. When the Lair Trait(s) manifest the effect seems to spread outward from the device(s) the Beast is inhabiting. The Normal Effect allows the Beast to manifest his Lair Traits, up to his usual maximum, within one of the network locations for a scene. At Low Satiety the Lair Traits simultaneously manifest within every location affected by the Atavism for a scene.<br /> <br /> <b>SIDEBOARD:</b> If the Beast has another Atavism or power that enhances his senses (such as Needs Must) or mental faculties (such as Mimir's Wisdom), he may combine the relevant effects with this one. Merits such as Investigative Aide or Connected Lair may also apply at the Storytellers discretion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The ego is not king of its own castle.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13329-strictura","name":"Strictura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13329_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T07:28:33-07:00","id":1313846,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Flesh Artisan [Namtaru]</b></u><br /> <i>The human body, for all of its flaws, is a sacred temple. The Gorgon contemptuously violates such sanctity and uses others' forms as his canvas for wicked and revolting experiments.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast adds his Lair to all mundane Medicine rolls and needs no tools. He numbs pain, stops bleeding and unfurls the flesh like a lotus. Furthermore, he never needs to perform extended actions no matter the seriousness of the wounds or illnesses: his rolls always take a turn each. This requires him to touch the target first, so Defense will apply if they are unwilling. <br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast gains Rote Quality on all Medicine rolls. He may thoroughly alter the victim's appearance as an Instant Action. This can only make changes that could naturally occur in a human, such as changing their age, sex, ethnicity and such. This lasts for (10 - Satiety at the time of the roll) days on a Success, or weeks on an Exceptional Success. This may cause a bonus or penalty to all relevant Social rolls equal to [Lair]. Doing this inflicts the Leveraged Condition, which can represent the victim wanting to stay as their ideal self or return to their previous form.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast rolls [highest between Dexterity + Medicine - Stamina as an Instant Action to warp and twist the flesh of his victims into impossible shapes, which lasts for the scene. For every dot of Lair, select one of the following. Other modifications may be chosen at ST discretion.<ul><li><b>Natural Weaponry:</b> Brawl attacks deal +2L with Armor Piercing 2.</li> <li><b>Tough Hide:</b> Armor 2/2.</li> <li><b>Redundant Organs:</b> Ignore one type of Physical Tilt altogether.</li> <li><b>Bestial Perception:</b> A new type of sense, such as thermal vision, tracking by scent and echolocation.</li> <li><b>Bestial Swiftness:</b> A new type of locomotion, such as wings, breathing underwater, camouflage or digging through the ground.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T09:29:05-07:00","id":1313862,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> I decided to rewrite one of your Atavisms, what do you think?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood Of Medusa [Namtaru]</b></u><br /> <i>Legend says that the mythical Gorgon's blood was so acidic that man made weapons would dissolve instantly upon piercing her flesh. The Beast inherits this defense mechanism, making her a walking chemical hazard.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> Your blood contains acidic properties that rapidly break down foreign substances they come into contact with. Whenever a melee weapon inflicts Lethal damage to you, your blood causes it to suffer [Lair/2 round up] points of Structure damage, ignoring Durability. If the damage is inflicted with bare hands, the attacker suffers [Lair/2 round up] points of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> The Beast can cover a weapon with her blood without damaging it by suffering 1 Resistant Lethal damage. The corrosion effect lasts for her (10 - Satiety) in days. The Beast is immune to mundane poisons and diseases, and decreases the Toxicity rating of supernatural equivalents by her Lair, down to a minimum of 1. This Atavism does not affect Chosen Blades of Heroes.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> When your Hunger flares, your blood does too. You deal your full Lair in Structure damage and the blood sprays outward into the immediate vicinity, affecting all objects caught within and characters who fail a Dexterity + Athletics - Lair roll. Your blood can also melt through supernatural barriers and protections with a successful Clash Of Wills. She can suppress this effect at will without a roll if she wishes to avoid hurting bystanders.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> A dormant curse flows through the veins of the Beast, and for a brief moment, they can awaken its full potential. Reduce all attacks caused this turn by a Lethal weapon to a single point of damage. The weapons are also destroyed in the process, as their material components are dissolved instantly upon breaking the skin. Lethal damage inflicted by unarmed attacks cause the enemy to suffer [Lair] points of Lethal damage and receive an appropriate Tilt in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T13:05:23-07:00","id":1313889,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> Seems to be a marked improvement. I don't think I'm very skilled at creating a mechanically balanced Atavism, anyways. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T08:11:17-07:00","id":1314948,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Phantom Thief [Eshmaki]</b></u><br /> <i>The avaricious always seek to closely guard their material belongings with a love they seldom show to other people. The Beast demonstrates the folly of their vices by casually taking away all their most prized treasures.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast adds his Lair to all Larceny rolls and needs no tools when they would normally be required. Locks, safes and so on quickly twist open with his touch alone. Furthermore, he never needs to perform extended actions no matter the level of security: his rolls always take a turn each. This requires him to touch the target, so he may still be detected. The Beast may stack this Atavism with traits like From The Shadows and Sleight Of Hand. This Atavism does not work on the Chosen Blades of Heroes.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast gains Rote Quality on all Larceny rolls. He may also perform Larceny rolls at a distance of [Lair x 3] meters, but must still be able to directly perceive the item or its container. This represents the Horror ignoring intervening distances and directly manifesting stolen items in the Beast's hands. Mundane attempts to notice or counter this suffer his Lair as a penalty, while supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> For the rest of the scene, the Beast can enter and exit the Astral frequency of Twilight. This is done as an Instant Action if Satiety is Normal, or reflexively if Satiety is Low. During this, he can directly take a number of items equal to [Lair x 2] into his Lair, or from the Lair into his hands. The objects must be valid targets for Larceny and have a maximum size of [Lair + 5].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-05-2019, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T10:51:33-07:00","id":1314970,"title":"","content":"This Atavism was originally written in this thread by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17413-evo_shandor\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar17413_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"17413\" data-vbnamecard=\"17413\">Evo_Shandor</a>. I just changed it to fit my preferences.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Abominable Armament (Anakim) [Originally Written By Evo Shandor]</b></u><br /> <i>In many legends, Giants wield massive weapons that can easily destroy whole armies. Those who saw such massacres and survived live in fear of ever facing such cruel might ever again. The Beast inherits this legacy and uses it to brutal effect against those who are foolish enough to fight him.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast reduces the Defense of the enemy by his [Lair] when making Weaponry attacks. Should he be unarmed, he can forego the normal +2 of an All Out Attack in order to summon an armament with a Damage Bonus equal to [Lair] during this turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast gains Rote Quality on Weaponry rolls and can strike from a distance of up to [Horror's Power x 2] meters away. Furthermore, if summoning an armament by making an All Out Attack, he keeps half of his Defense round up.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast swiftly cleaves through hordes of enemies in one massive swing as the Horror becomes fully visible for a terrifying moment. The Beast makes one attack roll and hits everyone within his immediate vicinity, applying Down And Dirty Combat. This stacks with the Rote Quality if Satiety is Low. Heroes are immune to Down And Dirty Combat inflicted by this effect and therefore require normal combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-07-2019, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T12:41:11-07:00","id":1314995,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Lord Of Animals (Eshmaki)</b></u><br /> <i>While living in their walled cities, humans like to think they are safe from the predators of the wilderness. The Beast knows better and can watch his prey with the eyes of animals, ready to strike when it is least expected.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast adds his Lair to all mundane Animal Ken rolls. When this Atavism is acquired, choose a number of Animal Ken Specialties equal to [Lair], which may be changed at the start of each chapter. The Beast can possess an animal represented by such Specialties through a roll of Wits + Animal Ken. Possessing and leaving the animal requires an Instant Action each. This lasts for [Lair] in minutes on a Success, and [Lair] in hours on an Exceptional Success.<br /> <br /> Acceptable categories include specific ones like canines, birds, ungulates, arthropods and rodents, but not broad ones like carnivores or vertebrates. When training a favored animal in order to establish the Bonded Condition, the Beast never makes Extended Actions, ignores the animal's Resolve and needs no Equipment. His rolls always take one turn each, as the animals find him inherently trustworthy and worthy of respect.<br /> <br /> The Beast remains aware of his surroundings while possessing a favored animal, and thus keeps his Defense and such. The targeted instance can be a swarm of critters with Size 0-2 and a radius of [Lair x 3] meters, or a single critter with Size of up to the Horror's Resistance. However, it must be within [Lair x 10] meters, or [Lair x 50] meters if it is a very uncommon animal. The Beast can do any action the animal could, but uses his own Attributes, Skills and Merits. The Beast can still communicate verbally while possessing the animal, but cannot use Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast gains Rote Quality on all mundane Animal Ken rolls. Furthermore, he can extend any of his Atavisms through a possessed target. Possessing and leaving the animal is now a Reflexive Action. Mundane attempts to control or influence animals for which he has the Bonded Condition suffer a penalty equal to his Lair, while supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Once per scene, the Beast can use one of his favored animals as a gateway into his Lair. He receives an automatic Success on the roll to open the Primordial Pathway, and adds his Animal Ken to his Resolve to determine how many turns it lasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T16:52:24-07:00","id":1315046,"title":"","content":"I wrote my own version of one of your Atavisms, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>. What do you think?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Draining Kiss [Namtaru]</b></u><br /> <i>Humanity shudders in revulsion at those animals who consume their prey in a different way than simply eating the flesh. Spiders, lampreys, mosquitoes, and more all feed by drinking the nutrients from their victim's body. This revulsion is reflected in the monsters humans have made up in their nightmares: seductive vampires, breath-stealing hags and others, here to steal our blood, ichor, emotions, prana, or other such vital liquids. Naturally, such a primal fear finds representation among the Begotten.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> Every turn the Beast is in intimate physical contact with her victim, he receives 1 lethal damage, and the Beast heals 1 lethal or 2 bashing damage. Those who are killed by this Atavism tend to appear shriveled or desiccated. This Atavism is used as a Grapple. Many Beasts find it prudent to immobilize their target before beginning their ministrations.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> Appetites grow, and a Beast's belly is a greedy thing. The Beast may drain 1 Willpower point each turn instead of causing damage (up to his normal maximum). The experience can be ecstatic or agonizing, chosen by the Beast. When the victim runs out of Willpower or suffers more lethal damage than his Stamina as a result of this Atavism, roll Resolve + Composure - Lair. Failure causes the Swooned or Shaken Condition. A Dramatic Failure also causes the Addicted Condition. The victim suffers the Beast's Lair as a penalty to break free from the Grapple, and supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills. These drained Willpower points vanish at the end of the scene if not used.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast can drain entire crowds of people at once, leaving behind piles of desiccated (and often smiling) corpses as his Horror becomes fully visible for a repulsive moment. He may target any and all directly perceptible victims within his immediate vicinity. Roll Presence + Persuasion - Composure. On a Success, all targets suffer Aggravated damage equal to Successes + Lair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-28T22:57:40-07:00","id":1315098,"title":"","content":"Since I have nothing better to do, I went ahead and rewrote one of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a>'s Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <u><b>In My Image (Ugallu)</b></u><br /> <i>Humans have always drawn the likeness of gods and monsters and ascribed a mystical significance to such an act. The entities so captured in stone and ink are said to draw power from the devotion of those who gaze upon their icons. The Beast can likewise use images of himself to watch and influence potential victims from afar, who are seldom aware of how vulnerable such idols make them. </i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast is instantly aware when any image of him is captured, by any medium. He does not know its exact location but can roll Perception to ascertain a rough direction and distance. This image need not be a picture. It could also be a statue or any other representation of the Beast. This ability only works if the image is within [Lair x 100] meters of the Beast\u2019s current location.<br /> <br /> The Beast may see and hear through any image of himself that he knows the location of within the aforementioned range. He may also edit it, but his likeness must stay recognizable. Extending your senses through an image and returning them to you both require an Instant Action. If the image is stored in a digital form, it can only be accessed while it is being displayed. He may not communicate verbally through the image, but may edit it to include a single written sentence, usually a foreboding one.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> As the Horror\u2019s hunger grows, so does its perspicacity. The range is increased to [Lair x 500] meters and the Beast automatically knows the exact distance and direction of all images. Extending your senses through an image and returning them to you is now done reflexively. The Beast may communicate verbally through them, which allows Social rolls against observers.<br /> <br /> His editing may thoroughly alter his likeness, usually to display his Horror. He may roll Manipulation + Intimidation - Resolve to inflict the Shaken or Frightened Condition, selected each time. Either action requires the victim to look directly at the image. More than one Beast has used an image of himself to haunt a victim in places they thought were safe. This may generate Lair Resonance via Traits like Exposed and Mirages at ST discretion.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast may turn any of his images within range into a nightmarish vision of deadly terror. Roll Presence + Intimidation - Resolve, dealing Aggravated damage to all onlookers equal to Successes + Lair. Those who die appear to have suffered a horrible heart attack or seizure, with their skin turning deathly pale and their eyeballs turning completely black.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-29T12:20:14-07:00","id":1315245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1315046#post1315046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote my own version of one of your Atavisms, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a>. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly a tad more powerful than my original, though I also believe that that was the very first homebrew Atavism I ever wrote, so I was still trying to get comfortable with the design space. The Satiety Expenditure effect is quite different, and contains echoes of Monster From the Deep, which I find interesting; it also requires less bookkeeping than mine--generally a good thing. Overall, I approve. Nice work!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-30T03:00:22-07:00","id":1315414,"title":"","content":"Original versions by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1838_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1838\" data-vbnamecard=\"1838\">danparadox</a><br /> <br /> <u><b>Mechanical Monster (Anakim)</b></u><br /> <i>The crushing gears, the roaring engines, the pitiless motions of steel and oil. Though not all Beasts are drawn to machines, many feel a sympathy to the power and utility that such creations represent. Humanity has often ascribed its own traits to the machines it interacts with, taking comfort that the gears don't want to mutilate them. The Beast brutally destroys such flimsy notions of safety.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast knows machines as it knows the flesh and bone that makes its body. He adds his Lair on all Crafts rolls for mechanical repairs, modifications and sabotaging. He does not need any tools, as metal bends and morphs with his touch alone. He never makes Extended Actions in the aforementioned circumstances, no matter the complexity of the task. His rolls always take one turn each.<br /> <br /> He may use this effect to Craft Equipment, but any modifications must be possible via mundane means. This Atavism may stack with traits like Mimir's Wisdom and Automotive Genius, but does not affect technology that is mostly electronic/digital. Chosen Blades of Heroes are immune to this Atavism, but clever Beasts may use it to generate Lair Resonance via Traits like Crushing and Razored at ST discretion.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> When the Hunger grows, the tools of humanity are now submissive to the Beast. He gains the Rote Quality on all relevant Crafts rolls. Mundane attempts to detect or counter this suffer his Lair as a penalty, while supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills. If the Beast is detected or countered, he suffers the Shaken Condition. Furthermore, he may make such rolls at a distance of up to [Lair x 5] meters.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Horror becomes fully visible and roars with the sound of a million hungry gears. Roll Intelligence + Crafts - Stamina against all directly perceptible targets within his immediate vicinity, dealing Aggravated damage equal to Successes + Lair. The result is nothing short of a horrifying massacre: victims are dragged screaming into mechanical maws.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Electric Enigma (Eshmaki)</b></u><br /> <i>We may fool ourselves into thinking that we have tamed lightning, but many of us feel a certain sense of awe at natural displays of such elemental might. The Beast embodies this awe, as his veins course with electricity and he lashes out with it at his unsuspecting victims.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast can roll Manipulation + Science to control the flow of electricity within [Lair x 10] meters. He may cause localized blackouts and other types of sabotage, and generally reduces the Equipment Bonus of all relevant technology by his [Lair]. Furthermore, he is immune to all damage from electricity.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The range is increased to [Lair x 50] meters. If an Equipment has its Bonus reduced to zero and someone uses it regardless, Failures become Dramatic Failures (a Beat is still earned). The Beast may electrocute someone within the immediate vicinity of a preexisting electricity source inside the aforementioned radius by rolling Wits + Science - Defense.<br /> <br /> This electrocution lasts for a number of turns equal to Lair and causes bashing damage each turn according to the type of source (see Beast The Primordial, page 171). The victim may roll Strength + Stamina - Lair each turn to break free. Mundane attempts to counter or detect the Beast's Normal Satiety effect suffer his Lair as a penalty, while supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills. If the Beast is detected or countered, he suffers the Shaken Condition. Those who die leave behind twitching, hairless corpses.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast becomes living electricity for the scene. He may travel through wiring or other conductive material, crossing [Lair x 50] meters each turn. He gains a bonus to Defense and Initiative equal to [Lair/2 round up] and reduces all damage from ranged attacks to 1 bashing, or 2 bashing on an Exceptional Success. His Brawl attacks have a Bashing Damage Bonus equal to Lair and inflict the Stunned Tilt if damage exceeds the target's Stamina. If his Satiety is Low, he may also consider himself a source of electricity for the purposes of attacking others at range, with a Bashing Damage Bonus equal to his Lair and the option of Automatic Fire. His maximum range when using himself as the source of the blasts is equal to [Science x 10] meters.<br /> <br /> Anyone who makes a Brawl or Weaponry attack against the Beast is electrocuted, unless they spend 1 Willpower point to ignore the effect for this turn (which does not add dice to the roll), or use a weapon made from a non-conductive material such as wood or most rocks. The Chosen Blades of Heroes ignore electrocution if they are melee, and deal full damage if they are ranged. While in the form of living electricity, the Beast cannot benefit from other traits that give a Damage Bonus, such as Limb From Limb or Cyclopean Strength. However, he may generate Lair Resonance via Traits like Electrified and Disruption at ST discretion. Those who die have their internal organs boil through their skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 08-24-2019, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-06-05T14:11:22-07:00","id":1316700,"title":"","content":"This Atavism was originally written by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a><br /> <br /> <u><b>Hydra's Regeneration [Namtaru]</b></u><br /> <i>Like the namesake monster of Greek mythology, the Beast cannot be killed by dismemberment or even decapitation. Her extremities and head always grow back, and may even act independently after being severed to overwhelm his foes. Those who cannot escape will scream in agony as their flesh melts away.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> You may detach any or all of your limbs as an instant action, and control them reflexively. They crawl and slither on their own for [Stamina + Lair] turns, during which they can lunge and attack. At the end of this time, or when your limbs are cut off by another, they must be reattached or you suffer an appropriate Tilt. Detached limbs may be used to manipulate objects and attack as though they were still attached. Each such limb is considered to use your own dice pools for Physical Actions, as well as your own Derived Traits (except for Defense, which is 0). But since you cannot detach sensory organs, such limbs cannot be controlled if outside your Perception range and become inert.<br /> <br /> Each such limb has Health equal to your Stamina only. If your limbs have been lost or destroyed, the associated Tilt is permanent unless the Beast enters his Lair and spends 1 Satiety to grow back each limb. If he has Relentless Hunter, 1 Satiety grows back all limbs. A Beast can only have a number of ambulatory limbs outside of his Lair equal to [Lair x 2]. Inside the Lair, this number is increased to [Lair x 5]. If multiple limbs attack the same target, do not make separate rolls for each one. Instead, every limb after the first decreases the Defense of the victim by one. This Atavism does not apply to the Chosen Blades of Heroes.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> You may detach sensory organs and even your head reflexively. Anything that is detached grows back in the same turn, removing the associated Tilts. The detached body parts can now make Perception rolls if they are sensory organs. Limbs and your head have access to your Defense. You may also use Atavisms through the body parts, but not the Satiety Expenditure effect. For example: they could glide and climb walls through Wings Of The Raptor, or tear victims apart through Limb From Limb. You cannot use Nightmares through them, but they count as images of the Beast for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1315098#post1315098\"><b>In My Image</b></a>. Every detached body part remains animate as long as Satiety is Low, but they must still be perceived directly by the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Regardless of where they are, the detached body parts violently spasm as if caught in death throes, and detonate in a blast of corrosive blood and gore. Anyone caught within melee combat distance of a detached body part must roll Dexterity + Athletics or suffer Lethal damage equal to the Stamina of the Beast. If the victim is being Grappled by a limb, they can make one last attempt to escape using Strength + Brawl, but they must spend 1 Willpower (which does not add dice). If the Satiety is Low, either roll to escape suffers Lair as a penalty and the damage inflicts Tilts. While inside the Lair, damage is equal to the Resistance of the Horror (maximum of 10).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-05-2019, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T07:34:27-07:00","id":1323443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1314995#post1314995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Lord Of Animals (Eshmaki)</b></u><br /> <i>While living in their walled cities, humans like to think they are safe from the predators of the wilderness. The Beast knows better and can watch his prey with the eyes of animals, ready to strike when it is least expected.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety:</b> The Beast adds his Lair to all Animal Ken rolls. When this Atavism is acquired, choose a number of Animal Ken Specialties equal to [Lair/2 round up], which may be changed at the start of each chapter. Once per scene, the Beast can borrow the senses of an animal represented by such Specialties through a roll of Wits + Animal Ken. Possessing and leaving the animal requires an Instant Action each. This lasts for [Lair] in minutes on a Success, and [Lair] in hours on an Exceptional Success. Acceptable categories include specific ones like canines, birds, ungulates, arthropods and rodents, but not broad ones like carnivores or vertebrates. When training a favored animal in order to establish the Bonded Condition, the Beast never makes Extended Actions, ignores the animal's Resolve and needs no Equipment. His rolls always take one turn each, as the animals find him inherently trustworthy or worthy of respect.<br /> <br /> The Beast remains aware of his surroundings while possessing a favored animal, and thus keeps his Defense and such. The targeted instance can be a swarm of critters with Size 0-3 and a radius of [Lair x 5] meters, or a single critter with Size of up to 10 + [Lair x 2]. However, it must be within [Lair x 10] meters, or [Lair x 50] meters if it is a very uncommon animal. The Beast can do any action the animal could, but uses his own Attributes, Skills and Merits. To compensate, he gains a bonus of [Lair/2 round up] on all relevant rolls for the animal (e.g. Stealth, Athletics, Brawl, Survival, Intimidation). The Beast can still communicate verbally while possessing the animal, but cannot use Nightmares.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast gains Rote Quality on all Animal Ken rolls. Furthermore, he can extend any of his Atavisms through a possessed target. However, he cannot use the Satiety Expenditure effect while doing so. Relevant rolls for the possessed animal also receive 8 Again. Possessing and leaving the animal is now a Reflexive Action. Mundane attempts to control animals for which he has the Bonded Condition suffer a penalty equal to his Lair, while supernatural attempts trigger a Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Beast summons a phantasmagorical instance of a favored animal by rolling Manipulation + Animal Ken, which benefits from the Rote Quality if Satiety is Low. The summoned instance lasts for the scene and must be able to naturally survive in the current environment (e.g. no sharks on land). The instance cannot deal damage to living beings if Satiety is Normal, but can use Perception and perform Physical Actions. Each instance is represented as a Retainer with a rating equal to Successes when acting on its own [caps at 5]. Such animals have Health equal to [Retainer rating x 2] and a Speed equal to that of the Beast, but Defense and Initiative Modifiers of zero.<br /> <br /> If Satiety is Low, the instance may cause damage to living beings using their [Retainer rating x 2] as a dice pool and dealing +0L. The Beast can possess his phantasmagorical animals as if they were real. However, if the Beast suffers lethal damage exceeding his Stamina or any amount of aggravated damage from a single attack during possession, all summoned animals immediately vanish and he gains the Stunned Tilt for turns equal to his [Lair]. The phantasmagoria may generate Lair Resonance via Traits like Swarms and Thunderous at ST discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feels like a powered up, refined version of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8122\" data-vbnamecard=\"8122\">ArchonAres</a>' and my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=1136750#post1136750\">Manyskin</a> with a different twist. Very thematic, I like it.<br /> Some questions, if you allow:<br /> Using your own attributes saves some charting work, which is always good. However, that makes taking over e.g. a Grizzly less useful than a common house cat: the latter can hide better, reach more places, is less conspicious and would deal the same damage, have the same rate of success for just about every task. Is this intentional? (Not saying this is bad, just curious.)<br /> I feel like the size calculation is a bit too lenient - a starting Beast would be able to take over animals of size 12 - Grizzlies are size 7, Hippos size 10! This way, a Lair 2 Beast would already be capable of commanding African Elephants - not too much room for growth unless you dip into the sea. If you want to reflect some sort of power growth via Lair, I'd recommend lowering the starting size limit or changing the calculation wholesale (e.g. Size 3 + Lair). And leading back to the former: what happens when the animal takes PC's Health in damage?<br /> <br /> This type of Atavism is an absolute must have for all Leshy, Lords of the Wood, Plantblooded, Swamp Thing-knockoffs, Ents, Demontrees and the like imo, good job!<br /> (Might I ask why the 'no sharks on land' restriction? I feel like this would be an awesome chance for 'ghost sharks' a la <i>Love, Death and Robot'</i>s &quot;Fish Night&quot;.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T02:16:11-07:00","id":1378706,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1423_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1423\" data-vbnamecard=\"1423\">espritdecalmar</a> I took inspiration from how you wrote &quot;All That Glitters&quot; as an expansion for &quot;Siren's Treacherous Song&quot;.<br /> <br /> House Rule: <u><i><b>Limb From Limb</b></i></u> deals +0L and inflicts Tilts even at Normal Satiety. Because it makes no sense for an Atavism with such a name to deal Bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Abominable Armament (Anakim) [Originally Written By Evo Shandor]</b></i></u><br /> <i>In many legends, Giants wield massive weapons that can easily destroy whole armies. Those who saw such massacres and survived live in fear of ever facing such cruel might ever again. The Beast inherits this legacy and uses it to brutal effect against those who are foolish enough to fight him.</i><br /> <br /> This Atavism has the same mechanics as Limb From Limb + the above house rule, except that it has the following effect for Satiety Expenditure and uses Weaponry instead of Brawl. To most observers, the Beast appears to be using mundane armaments. But to those who are sensitive to the Primordial Dream, the Beast wields chimerical and surreal armaments themed after his Family, Hunger, Lair and Kinship.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The Beast swiftly cleaves through hordes of enemies in one massive swing as the Horror becomes fully visible for a terrifying moment. The Beast makes one attack roll and hits everyone within his immediate vicinity, applying Down And Dirty Combat. Heroes are immune to Down And Dirty Combat inflicted by this effect and therefore require normal combat.<br /> <br /> A Beast who acquires both Limb From Limb and Abominable Armament can apply either Brawl or Weaponry on each attack, and apply either option for Satiety Expenditure, regardless of which Skill they select. Acquiring the other Atavism only costs 2 Experiences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T22:35:36-07:00","id":1379179,"title":"","content":"This might work better as a Nightmare, probably with a name like &quot;You Cannot Remember Anything&quot;. But the brain-eating option makes less sense for a Nightmare, methinks. I also don't know how to make it distinct from the Tabula Rasa Nightmare.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>Devourer Of Memories [Inguma]</b></i></u><br /> <br /> Normal Effect: The Beast must use this Atavism as a custom Grapple Maneuver. Roll Intelligence + Investigation + Lair - Resolve. You absorb an hour of memories for each Success. The Beast can designate a specific topic to narrow down what memories he will absorb. This topic must be expressed as a single sentence and must be related to the Hunger. At ST's discretion, the Beast can apply the Leveraged Condition on the victim if the memories are especially incriminating or dangerous. The Beast can pierce supernatural abilities that protect the mind via a successful Clash Of Wills.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: The Beast does not need to establish a Grapple. He can absorb memories from a distance of up to [Horror's Power x 10] meters away. The Beast also measures the absorbed memories in days rather than hours.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: The Beast does not merely absorb the memories, he replaces them with whatever he wants. The Satiety is spent after a successful Grapple, or from a distance if Satiety is Low. This inflicts the Amnesia Condition. At the ST's discretion, if the Beast phrases the implanted memories as described under Normal Satiety, he can nudge the victim toward certain decisions on an instinctive level. This does not force them to perform actions that would cause a Breaking Point for them (that is the purview of abilities like the &quot;You Must Obey&quot; Nightmare), but could achieve effects like giving Perfect Impression for Social Maneuvering or compel them to use a Skill other than the one which is expected for the situation. If the victim suffers extreme dissonance from the false memories, he can roll Resolve + Composure - Lair as an Instant Action to Resolve the Amnesia Condition.<br /> <br /> Note: The Unchained are immune to this Atavism. Repeated use on the same victim within a relatively short period of time causes tell-tale psychosomatic effects and psychotic episodes. This registers to Heroes as the actions of a Beast. By killing the victim and consuming their brain entirely raw within five minutes, the Beast gains access to all of their memories, which can be represented as an Informed Condition for anything the ST deems relevant. This is in addition to the +4 to Satiety Potential for killing the victim. The Beast doesn't suffer any ill effects normally associated with consuming neural tissue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-07-2020, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-01T10:06:42-07:00","id":1458235,"title":"","content":"Hopefully some minor necro is okay for homebrew content threads. I've been in a mood to write some Beast things lately for perhaps obvious reasons, and what started as a reskin of Shadowed Soul turned into its own little thingamajig.<br /> <br /> <b>Watery Grave [Makara]</b><br /> <br /> Water\u2019s a powerful thing. It makes up three-fourths of our planet, as well as about the same amount of our own bodies. Without it, we quickly wither, but too much can so easily kill us, whether from filling our lungs or smashing against our bones. That we are so intimately reliant on something so inexorably lethal forever colors the resonance of our collective dreams. Some Leviathans are the monsters that prowl the lakes and rivers and seas, while others take the form of the water itself, first rushing in to devour us, then surging away to avoid our desperate grasp all the same.<br /> <br /> Any water affected by this Atavism must be in liquid form; it has no power over ice or vapor.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive or Instant (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>The Beast, while submerged in water, gains a keenly honed sense of positioning, not dissimilar to a dolphin\u2019s echolocation, but with no need to make any sound. She suffers no penalties to seeing underwater, whether from murky conditions, the sting of salt, or even a lack of eyes. This does not extend to the land or air. With a touch, she can also determine the type and quality of any liquid: whether it is potable, polluted, poisoned, or so on. <br /> <br /> Finally, while fully submerged in water, she may take an instant action to become one with the liquid, dissolving completely, becoming invisible, intangible, and impervious to harm. She cannot move, except to regain physical form. Exposure to electricity or magical attack will also eject her, as will extreme desiccation that reduces the body of water to less than her Size. Mundane sonar will not detect her presence, and supernatural detection forces a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast becomes as one with the water surrounding her. She can control a contiguous body of water she is touching as if it were an extension of her own, out to (five times Lair) yards. She can shape the water in unnatural ways, such as forming twisting columns on the surface, receding at the bottom to reveal sunken treasure, or creating a barrier around something she wishes to protect. By forming water into rushing tendrils, she can make Brawl attacks and even grapple moves against distant opponents. Add half her Lair rating (rounded up) to any Physical actions she takes via this hydrokinesis. Each use of this ability still requires an instant action.<br /> <br /> There is a downside to this power, though many Beasts are unaware of it: Any water the Begotten is manipulating also counts as an extension of her body for mystical purposes such as sympathetic ties. A foe couldn\u2019t harm the Beast by stabbing a connected puddle with a mundane knife, but a mage could target her with a touch-range spell merely by making contact with the swimming pool she\u2019s wading in.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>With a force of will, the Beast becomes water itself. Her body and immediate possessions all transform into liquid, which she can move and shape as she pleases while retaining a generalized awareness of her surroundings. She can easily slide out of an opponent\u2019s grasp, as well as trickle through grates or down pipes\u2014or into a victim\u2019s lungs. She moves at her normal Speed, and can still use other Atavisms but not Nightmares. As water, she is immune to most types of damage, save for electricity or extreme heat or cold, or certain types of magical attacks at Storyteller discretion. This transformation lasts until the end of the scene, but the Begotten may end it early as a reflexive action; if she does so while within a larger body of water, she may immediately reform anywhere within the water that she can perceive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-13T13:57:22-08:00","id":1472385,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">These things enter my head and must come out again, like a pearl in an oyster.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Trick of the Light [Inguma]</b><br /> <br /> Deception comes easy to monsters. The kushtaka weaves illusions of victims\u2019 loved ones to draw them out onto perilous ice floes, while cunning elves bewitch mortals into seeing heaps of dross as mounds of untold riches for which they might eagerly trade their firstborn children. A Beast with this Atavism traffics in lies, their prey left unable to trust even their own senses.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> N/A<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect:</b> As an instant action, the Beast can create an illusory figure no larger than Size 5 out to (Lair dots) yards away. By default the illusion is a stationary image, though the Beast can direct it to move or appear to take some other effect, including making sound, as an instant action. The illusion is odorless, and possesses no physical substance, passing through solid matter like a hologram. Visual incongruities allow observers to make a reflexive Intelligence + Wits roll to recognize the image as false; the Beast may contest this with their own roll of Manipulation + Subterfuge if aware of the risk.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the Beast may use this effect to mask extant objects or beings (again up to Size 5), such as altering the wording on a sign or changing the color of a person\u2019s eyes. As above, this does not affect other sensory qualities of the target, such as temperature, texture, or scent.<br /> <br /> The Begotten can maintain up to (half Lair dots, rounded up) illusions at once, all of which vanish immediately if their creator is rendered unconscious. A conjured illusion can be dismissed as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> A hungry Horror is a crafty one, pushing more of the Primordial Dream into the Beast\u2019s figments. Illusions can now be directed, including changing any or all of their details, as a reflexive action. In addition, the Beast gains the ability to include other sensory cues in their creations, giving them distinct smells or textures, and even a small degree of solidity; in mechanical terms, solid illusions have Durability 0, Structure 1, and are unable to affect the world outside the most minor of physical efforts, such as activating a touchscreen or ruffling a curtain. When actively directed, they have Defense equal to the Beast\u2019s Wits; otherwise they have a Defense of 0.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> The Begotten infuses the waking world with the dream-logic of their Lair, creating an illusion that is all-too real. The Size of the illusion created can be up to (Lair + 5), possessing any sensory traits the Beast desires. In addition, the illusion is treated as an Actor (BPG, pg 157); its three Attributes each start at one dot, to which the Beast then distributes their Lair dots. Each phantasm should be designated a theme that it follows when not directed, such as \u201cdisappointed mother\u201d or \u201capple tree.\u201d The Begotten may alter any quality of the conjured Actor, including theme, solidity, or Size (but not Attributes) as an instant action (or reflexive at Low Satiety), turning a fifty-dollar bill into a tangle of carnivorous vines, or rendering a solidified bridge suddenly insubstantial. If conjured in the Beast\u2019s own Lair, other characters do not add their Supernatural Tolerance as a weapon rating to attacks against the illusion.<br /> <br /> One drawback to this power is known: Actor-phantasms summoned with this Atavism share any Bane Anathema the Beast suffers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-11T15:58:31-07:00","id":1478614,"title":"","content":"Not quite sold on this atavism, but here it is what I got so far, any suggestions on how to improve it? Should I nerf it?<b><br /> <br /> False Trails [Inguma]</b><br /> <br /> Some monster are renowed for being tricksters and notoriously hard to track down or all well know to leave false trails that lead their would be hunters to their doom, the Ciguapa for example has backward feets to confuse anyone following after her steps, the fair folk legends are filled with tales of them leading people astray deep in the woods. The Beast with this atavism is a particularly dangerous prey to track, a well know triskter it can turn any hunt on its would be hunter often with deadly results.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Intelligence+Subterfuge+Lair (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Persistant (Normal effect), Reflexive (Low Satiety), Contested and Extended (Satiety Expenditure)<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Effect: </b>Any attempt to track down or investigate the passing of the beast character must contend with their Lair as a penalty as the beast occludes the marks of his passage or actions, little evidence is left behind or if there is any evidence, it is misleading and hard to parse. Supernatural attempts have to contend with a clash of wills as this atavism muddles even the supernatural senses of would be hunters.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety: </b> Tricksters are hard to deal with because more often than not they are onto anyone trying to pull one over them, while starving the beast gets a sense of somone trying to track down or investigate the beast followed with a short vision of their would be stalker, the beast gets a vague sense of the state of the investigation or tracking attempt.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure: </b>This ability is what makes trying to track down a triskster so dangerus, when the beast spends satiety it actually starts to leave a believable trail, the normal effect still occludes the investigation or tracking but now it works to hide the deception, the Beast for the next 24 hours works to mislead its pursuers entering a constested action against them. Against supernatural abilities it forces a clash of wills but the Beast adds half it's lair rating rounded up as automatic successes.<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The Beast pretty much hands itself in a silver plate, the pursuers gain a situational advantage against the Beast when they finally found them, the storyteller has the final say of what constitutes a situational advantage but it's a substantial boon to the pursuers or a major complication to the Beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure: </b>No success are achieved on the roll, if the pursuers win they are unaffected by the beast atavism and suffer no drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <b>Success: </b>The beast accumulates successes needed to win, if the beast wins it can lead the pursuers away or should the beast character choose to face them it does so with a number of advantages equal to half their lair rounded up, the storyteller has the final say on what is appropiate, but the beast can choose the location and timing of their encounter, the pursuer or pursuers face the beast ill equipped to deal with them, they are led to one of the Beast chambers, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional sucess:</b> A great many successes are accumulated and if the beast wins they can choose one major advantage over their pursuers, again the storyteller has the final say of what is appropiate or possible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T18:28:22-08:00","id":1497250,"title":"","content":"If I'm you, and you're me, then who's driving the plane? Made this for one of my players, as they didn't quite like how Doppelganger worked, so I revised it, but it slowly turned into its own Atavism!<br /> <br /> <b>Twin Souls [Inguma]</b><br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> 1 hour<br /> <br /> <b>Normal Satiety: </b>The Beast splits into two, sharing the Beast\u2019s mind and body (Satiety, Willpower, Skills, Attributes). The new body has its own health, but spawns without equipment. She can only act through one body each turn during combat.<br /> <br /> The duplicate has all abilities of the Beast, but both lose access to Twin Souls while split. To merge back together, they can either spend an hour to choose one body to turn into dust, or to simply touch the other one as an Instant Action and fuse. As there is only one Horror, only one body can merge with the Horror in the Lair.<br /> <br /> If a body dies, the Beast suffers the Soul Shocked condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Satiety:</b> The Beast\u2019s mind is truly a sight to behold, allowing them to use the teamwork action on themself for Mental and Social skills. They may also partially control them in combat as a teamwork action for Physical skills.<br /> <br /> <b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> Instead of splitting themself, they can split a willing ally into two bodies. They cannot get the benefits of the Low Satiety effect. This only lasts for a day, instead of indefinitely like the Beast can. Upon the duration expiring, they may choose which body remains, and which one vanishes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":